se by cutting and re-sculpting. The \"dread-locks\" were completely re-sculpted, to accommodate the twist of the head and to give a more natural look to the piece. The spear is also scratch built. I also added small feathers, shells, and bones to this hunters wardrobe. As for the \"jungle\" base, it is entirely scratch built with the exception of a few small twigs and vines. \n<p>\nMy name is Anthony Mestas. I currently write, \"Making The Scene\", for Amazing Figure Modeler magazine. I offer my build-up services to fellow collectors and manufacturers, under the name \"Life Force Studio\". \n</p>'),(30,239,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3231,239,'predator_a',0,NULL),(31,239,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3231,239,'predator_b',0,NULL),(32,239,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3231,239,'predator_c',0,NULL),(33,170,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3232,170,'an_predator2',0,NULL),(34,200,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3232,200,'predator',0,NULL),(35,305,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3232,305,'predator',0,NULL),(36,330,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3233,330,'cain',0,NULL),(37,248,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3234,248,'tank',0,NULL),(38,270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3235,270,'abduction',0,NULL),(39,330,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3236,330,'cesare',0,NULL),(40,5013,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3237,5013,'lin',0,NULL),(41,280,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3238,280,'nosferatu',0,NULL),(42,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3239,149,'lair',0,NULL),(43,252,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3240,252,'crtrbl1',0,NULL),(44,263,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3240,263,'creature',0,NULL),(45,263,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3241,263,'deadly',0,NULL),(46,206,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3242,206,'drag',0,NULL),(47,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3243,159,'kong',0,NULL),(48,252,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3244,252,'rodan1',0,NULL),(49,263,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3245,263,'munsters',0,NULL),(50,170,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3246,170,'angelissa',0,NULL),(51,18,'2004-02-28 10:13:50',3246,282,'http://jamesart.com/angelissa.html',1,NULL),(52,18,'2004-02-28 10:14:08',3247,282,'http://jamesart.com/tabitha.html',1,NULL),(53,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',