olepeople',0,NULL),(784,4864,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3879,4864,'molepeople',0,NULL),(785,4864,'2006-06-09 12:52:03',3886,4864,'shecreature',0,'For More B-Monsters visit my site:\r\nwww.monsterjones.com'),(786,4864,'1999-03-11 13:13:27',3885,4864,'teenwerewolf',0,'Base scratchbuilt with spilled box of popcorn (styrofoam)\nand movie poster on wall at the 1950\'s-style Arkoff theater. One of my favorite films and kits!'),(788,4864,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3882,4864,'elvira',0,NULL),(789,4864,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3881,4864,'attackingmartian',0,NULL),(790,4864,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3880,4864,'wolfman',0,NULL),(791,4864,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3883,4864,'metaluna',0,NULL),(792,4865,'1997-06-27 11:04:02',3894,4865,'barnabas',0,'Grass and lichen added to base.'),(793,4865,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3221,4865,'blackbarnabas',0,NULL),(794,4865,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3309,4865,'mask',0,NULL),(795,4865,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3518,4865,'terminator',0,NULL),(796,4865,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3887,4865,'teenfranky',0,NULL),(797,4865,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3496,4865,'batman',0,NULL),(798,4865,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3499,4865,'catwoman',0,NULL),(799,4865,'1997-06-27 11:20:16',3888,4865,'penquin',0,'Scratch built monocle and cigarette holder.'),(800,4865,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3274,4865,'joker',0,NULL),(801,4865,'1997-06-27 11:22:53',3238,4865,'nosferatu',0,'Base and door scratch built.  Rat courtesy of Aurora Plastics.'),(802,4867,'1997-06-27 12:15:40',3896,4867,'wolverine',0,'I started sculpting about two and a half years ago Wolverine was my first successfull piece. He is made from super sculpey and wire. Any coments will be welcome good or bad.'),(803,4867,'1997-06-27 14:39:35',3897,4867,'harleyquin',0,'Harley Quin is my favorite piece.  She is small and cute. I did not take any creative liberty on this one. I tried to make her look as close to her comic counter part as posible except for the lips which are red instead of black.'),(804,4867,'1997-06-27 14:41:55',3899,4867,'drfate',0,'Dr. fate is my largest piece to date aside from the James cagney I am curently working on from angels with dirty faces. I did not know what type of base to make so I did her logo.'),(805,4867,'1997-06-27 14:44:00',3900,4867,'potatoe',0,'The potato\'s were going to be MM\'s but I did not thaw out the sculpey before baking so when it was done the potato with the knife had a wierd texture so thats how it came to be.'),(806,4867,'1997-06-27 14:47:31',3901,4867,'pumpkin',0,'My tribute to Oz. From the looks of it we\'re not in Kansas anymore. I like it a lot.'),(807,4867,'1997-06-27 14:49:54',3902,4867,'jones',0,'Olvier Wendel Jones the orignal computer hacker. His banana junior was not complete at the time of the photo.'),(808,4867,'1997-06-27 14:51:34',3903,4867,'wonderwoman',0,'Wonder Woman is the one. She stands seven inches tall. The base was my first atempt at marble. The concept of the piece is slave no more, that is why the bust is topeled over.'),(809,4867,'1997-06-28 11:01:08',3904,4867,'swampthing',0,'I must confess the Swamp Thing is a knock off piece. I came across a photo of the Swamp Thing statue being offered for sale, and a friend of mine asked me do you think you can sculpt it. I said probably and so here it is. I think it came out pretty close to the original that was for sale.'),(810,4867,'1997-06-28 11:02:52',3905,4867,'woody',0,'Woody Wood Pecker is a piece I made for my dad. For quite a while he had no tail.'),(811,4867,'1997-06-28 11:04:31',3906,4867,'paintboy',0,'Advance is my logo from my business card I came up with him quite a few years back.'),(812,4867,'1997-06-28 11:06:29',3907,4867,'brain',0,'I sculpted the Brain for my mom as a birthday gift.'),(813,4867,'1997-06-28 11:08:02',3908,4867,'riddler',0,'The riddler is quite a small piece. He stands no more than six inches tall. At the time of the photo being taken, I had not yet changed his hand that is by his face, which I was unhappy with from the start.'),(814,4867,'1997-06-28 11:09:59',3909,4867,'red',0,'Bullseye and Electra is my first atempt at a two figure scene. There are a few things I would like to have changed in it but oh well.'),(815,4867,'1997-06-28 11:12:22',3910,4867,'smokin',0,'John Constantine is the cigarette smoking trench coat wearing British bloke from Hellblazer.'),(816,4867,'1997-06-28 11:16:36',3911,4867,'green',0,'Green Lantern is my favorite super hero so I had to pay tribute.'),(817,4868,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3912,4868,'flivver',0,NULL),(818,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3219,346,'suzy',0,NULL),(819,346,'1997-06-29 10:03:06',3913,346,'ko',0,'I have always been a major fan of Project A-Ko and it was a great joy to finally locate A-Ko and C-Ko thanks to fellow kit builders telling me about New Type out of San Fransico.'),(820,346,'1997-06-29 10:10:58',3659,346,'bko',0,'B-Ko was by far one of the easiest models I\'ve built yet after Suzy and a pure joy to look at.'),(821,346,'1997-06-29 10:12:10',3914,346,'midoka',0,'This vinyl model was a bit hard because the pieces were not made well but, a little imagination helped creat a nice model.'),(822,346,'1997-06-29 10:13:29',3915,346,'aines',0,'This vinyl model was a bit hard because the pieces were not made well but, a little imagination helped creat a nice model.'),(823,4869,'1997-06-29 10:17:20',3513,4869,'robin',0,'This was my very first vinyl model and my very first one to submit on the internet.  I\'m very happy the way it turned out and I hope you Batman and Robin fans approve.'),(824,4870,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3916,4870,'slpless',0,NULL),(825,4871,'1997-06-30 09:50:49',3917,4871,'wings',0,'Jeff added some real roughage to the base and recently won 1st place with wings kit at the Character Shop model contest.'),(826,4872,'1997-06-30 09:49:25',3752,4872,'alex',0,'The tongue was sculpted with super sculpey and EZ water was tinted and used to make the dripping blood.'),(827,4872,'1997-06-30 08:56:49',3504,4872,'franky',0,'Built by John Delamere Painted by John Delamere and Paul Antonelli Jr. This kit was modified to hold a pizza in one hand and the menu was made for the other hand.  The menu includes full menu written on inside, really. John Delamere is always changing and modifing kits.'),(828,4873,'1997-06-30 09:53:00',3918,4873,'gzilla',0,'Billiken kits keep true to form as this kit had the rinkles in the suit but I wanted to make it look as real as possible. The leg joints were puttied using Milliput then sculpted back in the detail ribbs. Same for the arms. Godzilla is probably my favorite subject to paint.'),(829,4874,'1997-06-30 09:54:38',3919,4874,'vampy',0,'Bob loves to paint the human female body and does great work with eyes and flesh tones.'),(830,4875,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3920,4875,'cylena',0,NULL),(831,4876,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3921,4876,'oip',0,NULL),(832,4876,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3923,4876,'nina',0,NULL),(833,4876,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3922,4876,'kib',0,NULL),(834,4877,'1997-07-07 23:31:52',3924,4877,'ovrapt',0,'This was my first shot at sculpting my own dinosaur models,\nI found it a challenge & a lot of fun .\n<p>\nFACT FILE<br>\nThe Egg Thief - OVIRAPTOR PHILOCERATOPS<br>\nSize - 6ft. 6in. Weight - 73lb.<br>\nLocation - Mongolia Time - Late Cretaceous 83 to 73 MYA.<br>'),(835,4877,'1997-07-07 23:33:11',3925,4877,'stego',0,'Horizon kits good workmanship.'),(836,4877,'1997-07-07 23:34:26',3926,4877,'tric',0,'Great kit, good detail.'),(837,4877,'1997-07-07 23:40:56',3927,4877,'tlwrap',0,'Do not use the paints that come with this kit!\nI added sand & some plants to the base.'),(838,4879,'1997-07-08 13:29:33',3488,4879,'pred2b',0,'Because he looked like a short little guy, I lengthened his legs approximately 1/2\" with some Expert\'s choice epoxy putty from Bare Metal Foil.  There sure was a LOT of seamwork on this model!'),(839,4879,'1997-08-15 15:19:28',3928,4879,'conan',0,'There was a lot of detailing work with this model. I spent   \naround 50 hours or so finishing it, resculpting hair, fur,   \nwristbands, and adding a small spider on the base(sculpted out of   \nwhite putty).  Now I know why people say fleshtones are the toughest   \nthing to do.  Whew!'),(840,4880,'1997-07-08 13:40:28',3878,4880,'martian',0,'There wasn\'t much to this kit when it came to putting it \ntogether (6 pieces total).  After painting on a base coat, I used colored \nink thinned with water and a few drops of the base color as a wash for \neach area.  I then did a two stage dry brush of lighter shades of the \nbase color, in order to build up the highlights.  I painted all the \ndetail areas in black as an outlinning technique for the final detailing. \nEyes, teeth, nails, jewelry, and sash edging (aternating with silver, \ncopper, and gold) were all detailed last before sealing with a matte \nsealer.  The paints were water-based acrylic and applied with nylon \nbrushes (no air brush used).'),(841,4880,'1997-07-08 13:41:33',3476,4880,'alien',0,'I pretty much followed how the instructions said to paint it.  \nAlien is primered black with a purple wash made of colored ink, water, \nand dark purple acrylic paint.  I then lightly dry brushed the alien with \nsilver and detailed the nails and teeth.  The base was painted black, \nwith a two stage dry brush of brown and green, to bring out the \nhighlights.  I then sealed the model with a matte sealer.  Paints were \nwater-based acrylic and applied with nylon brushes (no airbrush used).'),(842,4880,'1997-07-08 13:46:24',3929,4880,'mummy',0,'This is an original 1963 Aurora Mummy.  I bought it off a guy \nin his forties who said he built the model when he was thirteen.  All \nthe pieces were there and it had been painted with Testors Enamel Paints \n(Black, Red, Green, and Yellow) directly over the plastic.  I heard that \nLye would remove enamel paint, so I first soaked the model in Easy-Off \nOven Cleaner (5% Lye Type, with VERY strong fumes).  The paint did come \noff with some scrubbing using an old toothbrush; however, the glue also \ngave way and I was able to remove the stones, snake, and eventually the \nMummy from the base (he broke at the ankle on one foot).  I primered the \nmodel and began painting it with water-based acrylic paints.  The hardest \npart about painting this model was trying to keep the colors distinct \nbetween the Stones, the Sand, the Mummy\'s Wrappings, and it\'s skin, so \nthe parts of the model would not bend together and look the same (I \nre-did the stones 5 times).  The Mummy himself was dry-brushed in \nmultiple stages directly over a black primer.  The base was washed with \nwatered down color ink and dry brushed in multiple stages to bring out \nthe highlights.  I only detailed the Mummy\'s eyes and the name display on \nthe base.'),(843,4880,'1997-07-08 13:47:22',3930,4880,'wolfman',0,'This is an original 1964 Aurora Wolf Man.  I bought it off a \nguy in his forties who said he built the model when he was thirteen.  \nApparently his mother kept the models for him after he left home (nice \nmom).  The model was intact (one Rat has a broken tail missing) and was \npainted with Testors Enamel Paint directly over the plastic.  I used a \nLye compound (Easy Off Oven Cleaner) and an old toothbrush to remove the \npaint.  The Lye also broke down the glue so I was able to remove the \nSkull, the Rats, the Stones, and the Wolf Man from the base.  After \nprimering the model I painted a dark base coat of water-based acrylic \npaint over each different color area.  I then used a wash made of watered \ncolor ink and a few drops of the base color paint.  A two stage dry brush \nwith lighter colors was used to bring out the highlights.  Difficulty was \ntrying to keep the Wolf Man\'s fur, the Rocks and the Rats from bending in \nwith each other.  Detailing was done on the Wolf Man\'s eyes, belt, and \nthe name display among the rocks.  The model was sprayed with a matte \nsealer.'),(844,4880,'1997-07-08 13:48:28',3931,4880,'prisoner',0,'This is a remake kit that was done in 1994.  I added a flat\nplastic back to the wall part of the model for looks and stability.  I\nalso had a problem with the chains from the wall, so I had a friend of\nmine who makes chainmail make real links to attach the prisoner to the\nwall.  The entire model was dry brushed in stages over a black primer.\nNo wash was used and very little was detailed.  Paint was water-based\nacrylic, sealed with a spray matte sealer.'),(845,4881,'1998-01-12 16:14:12',3305,4881,'predator',0,'I used a process known as underpainting for the fleshtones and armor of the Predator. I first put base coats of reds and yellows in the undercoats and then applyed a thin layer of sand.For the armor, I used bronze and gold for the underpainting and then lightly applied aluminum.\n'),(846,4843,'1997-07-21 11:43:49',3932,348,'gallows',0,'Gallows is the ultimate warrior, the vampire hunting savior of the world as\nenvisioned by Comic, game and book illustrator, Tim Bradstreet.\nThe vinyl kit, sculpted by Mat Falls, is easy-to-assemble,\ncomes with an engraved statue base and complete painting\ninstructions created by noted figure painter, Tom Gilliland.'),(847,4843,'1997-07-21 11:57:00',3933,348,'demon',0,'This highly detailed, graphic vinyl model kit was sculpted by Mat Falls from a\npen and ink illustration by Clive. It comes complete with an engraved statue\nbase and in-depth painting instructions by noted figure painter, Tom Gilliland.\n'),(848,4843,'1997-07-21 13:12:15',3934,348,'robots',0,'This vinyl model kit, sculpted by Mat Falls, was created from the infamous\nillustration used on the cover of the Queen album, News of the World. The\nrobot figure is adjustable prior to gluing so that you can position him as either\nkneeling or standing. The kit includes a custom engraved statue base and\ncomplete painting instructions by noted figure painter, Tom Gilliland.\n'),(849,298,'1997-07-22 22:22:58',3935,298,'pitt',0,'Sculpted as a sample piece.'),(850,298,'1997-07-22 22:37:16',3936,298,'green',0,'Original Design'),(851,298,'1997-07-22 22:46:58',3937,298,'gen',0,'Original Design, 3rd in a Genie Series.'),(852,298,'1997-07-22 23:00:19',3938,298,'wiz',0,'Original Design'),(853,298,'1997-07-22 23:18:41',3939,298,'cutter',0,'Wendy and Richard Pini\'s Cutter from ElfQuest.'),(854,298,'1997-07-22 23:26:15',3940,298,'run',0,'Giant after the little guy'),(855,261,'1997-07-31 11:41:53',3477,261,'alien3',0,'Photo was touched up.'),(856,261,'1997-07-31 13:23:49',3941,261,'atat',0,'Photo was touched up.'),(857,261,'1997-07-31 13:41:31',3942,261,'ufo',0,'Originally this kit was produced in 89\' and represents the alien ship used in the 1970 British television show UFO.  The internal structure is made of vacuform and had to be reinforced with resin.  The ship is 4.75 inches.'),(858,261,'1997-07-31 14:58:58',3943,261,'martian',0,'This kit has a 8 inch wingspan and since the vacuform plastic was relatively thin it had to be reinforced with resin.  The neon light effect was achieved by using fluorescent paint and then illuminated with ultra violet light.  The photo was assembled in photoshop 3.0.'),(859,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3945,4885,'carnage',0,NULL),(860,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3946,4885,'anubis',0,NULL),(861,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3947,4885,'apatosaurus',0,NULL),(862,4885,'1997-07-31 16:00:07',3928,4885,'conan',0,'Added moss to the base for a little added touch of realism.'),(863,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3544,4885,'crow',0,NULL),(864,4885,'1997-07-31 16:20:22',3948,4885,'demoness',0,'This is my first attempt at sculpting a full figure.  Some of the body parts are out of scale but again it is my first attempt.  I used a wire skeleton and built upon that with super sculpty.  I\'m interested in feedback about it.'),(865,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3485,4885,'dredd',0,NULL),(866,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3949,4885,'freddy',0,NULL),(867,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3950,4885,'horus',0,NULL),(868,4885,'1997-07-31 16:42:35',3508,4885,'joker',0,'Dashed the base quite a bit.  Wanted to make the base look like more realistic surroundings.  Used Sculpt A Mold on the back to make the bricks.  Cut off the letters on the floor and cut in squares on the floor for tiles and marbleized them.'),(869,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3453,4885,'medusa',0,NULL),(870,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3731,4885,'pinhead',0,NULL),(871,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3455,4885,'pumpkinhead',0,NULL),(872,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3511,4885,'ra',0,NULL),(873,4885,'1997-07-31 17:09:18',3512,4885,'raptor',0,'Cut out the eyes and brought some eyes from a taxidermist, less than two bucks a pair.'),(874,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3543,4885,'spawn',0,NULL),(875,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3951,4885,'species',0,NULL),(876,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3516,4885,'spiderman',0,NULL),(877,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3528,4885,'venom',0,NULL),(878,4885,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3944,4885,'alien',0,NULL),(879,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3517,4887,'steel',0,NULL),(880,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3952,4887,'robin',0,NULL),(881,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3953,4887,'wolfman',0,NULL),(882,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3522,4887,'thing',0,NULL),(883,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3728,4887,'elvira',0,NULL),(884,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3954,4887,'green',0,NULL),(885,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3955,4887,'dracula',0,NULL),(886,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3956,4887,'riddler',0,NULL),(887,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3957,4887,'superman',0,NULL),(888,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3958,4887,'mommy',0,NULL),(890,4886,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3960,4886,'mummy',0,NULL),(892,195,'1997-08-07 15:11:30',3962,195,'demoness',0,'This is such a great sculpture I had to do something really different with her.  The base is carved from balsa foam.  The blood is \"Easy Water\" from a local model railroad store.'),(893,354,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3543,354,'spawn',0,NULL),(894,354,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3963,354,'bobbit',0,NULL),(895,354,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3964,354,'raider',0,NULL),(896,4888,'1997-08-04 11:55:46',3553,4888,'boba',0,'Kit was heavily modified nad resculpted. Blaster, cape,\nantenna etc were redone. Modelling source was Hobby\nJapan, painting source were the Star Wars Chronicles\nand the Laserdisc Collection.'),(897,270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3965,270,'dark1',0,NULL),(898,270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3664,270,'moon2',0,NULL),(899,270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3392,270,'night1',0,NULL),(900,270,'1997-08-05 09:59:21',3966,226,'meta',0,'Cellar Cast\'s \"Alien Desert\" base provides a backdrop for Tsukuda\'s classic Metaluna mutant.\nI\'m proud to have this beautiful buildup by Jay Adan in my collection.  '),(901,270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3967,270,'schreck',0,NULL),(902,270,'1997-08-05 10:12:51',3921,270,'oip1',0,'This is as nasty as they come folks.  The kit is already so far past the bounds of good taste and common decency, that you can\'t help but go further!  I added a ceramic tile base, a working surgical lamp, a nasty embalming pump, I.V. bags, bandages, and drippy bits of goo.\nIf Fewture kits are your bag, then this blood\'s for you!'),(903,271,'1997-08-05 10:25:42',3968,271,'gally',0,'This was Leannn\'s first full-blown garage kit!  She customized it by dremeling the face out of the spare head, and glueing the helmet into Gally\'s left hand.'),(904,176,'1997-08-05 10:51:05',3969,176,'girlscreen',0,'Painted with Floquil, shaded with pastels.'),(905,176,'1997-08-05 10:59:38',3970,176,'iyuka',0,'Painted with floquil, highlights from pastels.'),(906,176,'1997-08-05 11:05:21',3971,176,'ikuko',0,'Painted with Floquil, shaded with pastels.'),(907,4896,'1997-08-05 11:27:47',3972,4896,'peace',0,'This is one great kit to build.  The entire kit hand painted with acryics (yes, that means no airbrushing).  The base was created from epoxy putty and some odd skulls and flowers.  This kit won 1st place in the Anime class at mad model party 3.  It\'s height is 11 inches tall.'),(908,330,'1997-08-05 11:44:39',3973,330,'sinbad',0,'Arm and back detail was dremeled in as sculptor gave him a smooth Ken Doll look.'),(909,330,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3974,330,'junglebettie',0,NULL),(910,330,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3975,330,'franky',0,NULL),(911,330,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3952,330,'robin',0,NULL),(912,330,'1997-09-04 10:20:26',3977,330,'marsattack',0,'It is a casting from a Maquette Casting.'),(913,330,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3549,330,'wolfman',0,NULL),(914,4849,'1997-08-26 15:30:53',3978,212,'barbrlla',0,'<b>\"This is one girl kit guaranteed to send you into orbit...recommended!\"</b><br>\n-Terry Webb<br>\n<p>\n<b>\"The best Barbarella kit I\'ve seen.  It\'s stunning!  I\'m very \'Fonda\' this kit.  Don\'t hesitate!\"</b><br>\n-David Fisher<br>\n<p>'),(915,4849,'1997-08-14 13:20:41',3979,215,'igor',0,'$95 with variant hands carrying abnormal brain.'),(916,4849,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3981,215,'id4',0,NULL),(917,4849,'1997-08-12 14:13:09',3982,149,'queen1',0,'Assembled and Painted $140.00.'),(918,4849,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3983,215,'pris1',0,NULL),(919,4849,'1997-08-14 13:18:41',3984,215,'eman',0,'Wig and variant hand included.'),(920,4898,'1997-08-17 21:16:58',3990,4898,'sailor',0,'  This was a rushed job-I built it in a hurry as a birthday present.  \n  This was also the first resin kit I had completed, and the first I had mostly airbrushed (I was still experimenting with my airbrush).\n  Paints used were mostly from Citadel Miniatures acrylics range, and Tamiya acrylics.  The metal staff was painted with Humbrol\'s Polished Aluminium metalcote.\n  Humbrol\'s Maskol masking paint proved invaluable for masking off finished areas before airbrushing a different colour.  It paints on easily, and afterwards it peels off in a single piece, without marking, lifting or damaging the paint underneath.  I found two coats were necessary to ensure that each area was properly masked though.\n  Brushes used for Maskol need cleaning afterwards in cellulose thinners-this stuff stinks and is likely very toxic...use with care!\n  Small sections of brass rod were used to pin and reinforce most of the joins between each section of the model.  The neck in particular would have been too weak, having to support the head and all that hair.\n  Incidentally, these G-Port kits are a JOY to build!  They are beautifully and accurately moulded, and require very little work during actual contruction.  The faces anime characters.'),(921,4900,'1997-08-13 13:39:42',3247,4900,'tabitha',0,'An Alpine challenge...and an Olympian reward!  Pictures alone cannot convey the beauty, presence and charm Tabitha exudes...even unpainted.\nThe customer service of Azimuth Designs is unparalleled.'),(922,296,'1998-05-26 13:48:28',3992,296,'jeanie',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(923,296,'1998-05-26 13:46:22',3993,296,'batman',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(924,296,'1998-05-26 13:39:57',3544,296,'crow',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(925,296,'1998-05-26 13:33:22',3517,296,'steel',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(926,296,'1998-05-26 13:31:02',3505,296,'ghostrid',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(927,4867,'1997-08-13 19:25:26',3994,4867,'bluelady',0,'Catwoman is and always will be one of my favorite female villians.  I tried to put my own feel in to the character.  Because after all there is plenty of kits and figures of this character offered so why do what is already done.'),(928,4867,'1997-08-13 22:32:36',3995,4867,'redman',0,'DareDevil is one of the great silver age heros, and in my opinion he does not receive the same treatment as Spiderman or any of the other heros of that time period.  \nSo I wanted to pay much needed respect to a comic hero who is well under rated.  So here he is I hope my work does him well.'),(929,4867,'1997-08-13 19:00:19',3996,4867,'goofy',0,'Goofy was a piece I had made for my brother in law who is Head of security at Madasion Square Garden so I decided to make his favorite character portray him.  He is also one of my early pieces when I first started out sculpting.  '),(930,4867,'1997-08-13 19:21:35',3997,4867,'ranger',0,'The Mark Messier was an early peice of mine as well, I no longer own him but I still have the sculpture I have done of Messier as a real person.\ncaricature'),(931,4867,'1997-08-13 20:22:38',3998,4867,'3pics',0,'Opus, Mildtoast the roach, and Mr. Peter were my first sculptures ever and they were done in that order.  I still own them.  They turned out pretty well for a first try.'),(932,4867,'1997-08-13 20:24:38',3999,4867,'3pics',0,'Opus, Mildtoast the roach, and Mr. Peter were my first sculptures ever and they were done in that order.  I still own them.  They turned out pretty well for a first try.'),(933,4867,'1997-08-13 20:28:39',4000,4867,'3pics',0,'Opus, Mildtoast the roach, and Mr. Peter were my first sculptures ever and they were done in that order.  I still own them.  They turned out pretty well for a first try.'),(934,4867,'1997-08-21 11:00:42',4005,4867,'devil',0,'Valerie The She Demon was a figure I made up as I went a long she is a completely original idea.  The color scheme was determined after several color changes were made.  She is not related to any known persons living or dead.'),(935,4867,'1997-08-14 23:45:49',4004,4867,'beast',0,'The Beast was a gift I made for my best friend, my sister.  He is one of my earlier works.  When I was asked to make him my sister asked me if I could make him the way I see him because after all there a lot of figures of this character available.  So she wanted something original so there you have it.'),(936,4867,'1997-08-14 23:49:01',4003,4867,'robin',0,'This Robin figure was completed in a matter of one day.  That meant sculpting and painting, he was also the second super hero piece I had done at the time.  I guess that shows in the end result but it was nice at the time.'),(937,4867,'1997-08-14 23:52:25',4002,4867,'spiderman',0,'I do not know what possessed me to make this figure before doing one of the real Spider man.  Once again he was one of my earlier peices I think he was like the third or fourth Super hero I made.  He was also completed in a matter of one or two days.'),(938,4867,'1997-08-14 23:54:32',4001,4867,'bugs',0,'Bugs Bunny was my fifth attempt at sculpting.  I made the figure to represent myself doing what I enjoy most, airbrushing.  '),(940,354,'1997-08-15 16:00:54',4006,354,'violator',0,'This kit is a modelers nightmare.  Ohhhh but when he\'s done he do be lookin good!'),(941,238,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4012,238,'barb',0,NULL),(942,238,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4013,238,'batman',0,NULL),(943,238,'1997-08-20 13:14:51',4014,238,'bruce',0,'I added some extras on the kit, like a cigarrette, real \"broken window\"-glass or a plastic-bag for the dynamit.  The only problem were the eyes:  Only if Bruce looks right-up, they look really cool...'),(944,238,'1997-08-20 16:39:24',4015,238,'metal',0,'High quality kit with lots of extras-thats the way kits should be!'),(945,238,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4016,238,'mummy',0,NULL),(946,238,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4017,238,'t-1000',0,NULL),(947,238,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4018,238,'rambo',0,NULL),(948,238,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4020,238,'at-st',0,NULL),(949,238,'1997-08-20 16:33:28',4021,238,'wars',0,'The Deathstar-Display I made of a lot of plastic trash, like McDonalds coffee-spoons, cups, pencils (guns), and everything cool I found...-It is about 3 feet x 2 feet big and it took me about 4 weeks to build it.'),(950,4907,'1997-08-20 16:47:11',4007,4907,'predful',0,'There was not much to do here, cut away the excess, sand and thats it.  I first gave it a few coats of ivory black and then washed it in bronze.  After that I applied a thin coat of laquer (for shine) and added a few scratch detail here and there.'),(951,238,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4019,238,'speed',0,NULL),(952,4906,'1997-08-20 13:03:50',3515,4906,'del2',0,'Represents a role-playing character developed by a friend.  The clothes are built up with epoxy putty and model magic filler (a light weight filler made for R/C aircraft).  The swords were ground useing a 1\' belt sander from 1/4\" brass bar stock with guards carved from .06 sheet styrene and pommels made form decorative necklace beads.  The jewel on the necklace is a red marker lens (available wutg nodel railroad supplies).  The figure was painted using Model Master Acrylic, Tamiya and Gunze Sanyo paints.'),(953,4904,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4008,4904,'elvira',0,NULL),(954,4904,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4009,4904,'flash',0,NULL),(955,4904,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4010,4904,'missto',0,NULL),(956,4904,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3635,4904,'agenda',0,NULL),(957,4903,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4011,4903,'pred',0,NULL),(958,354,'1997-08-26 12:34:53',3553,354,'bfett',0,'Best Boba Fett likeness out there.  I recomend this kit to every Star Wars fan out there.  That is if you can find it. '),(959,4910,'1997-08-26 12:52:46',3508,4910,'jokermodel',0,'Kit based on classic killing Joke graphic novel.'),(960,4909,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4025,4909,'whorg',0,NULL),(961,140,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4024,329,'dd-1',0,NULL),(962,140,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4022,329,'7-seal',0,NULL),(963,4912,'1997-08-26 13:53:14',4026,4912,'arbror',0,'This kit is a solid resin kit that sells for $35.00.  Yes only $35.00 for a 1/6 scale resin model!!  If you are interested in buying one contact Kevin at kevin96@jno.com.  The models will shipping on September 15, 1997.'),(964,4920,'1997-08-28 10:22:12',4027,4920,'pumpkinhead1',0,'If you got the room, this is one cool kit.  The eyes are clear glass and painted from the inside.  Working in this scale opens up a whole new set of painting styles to master.  A heck of a lot of fun to do.  '),(965,200,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4028,200,'ap4',0,NULL),(966,4921,'1997-08-28 12:38:33',3522,4921,'thing',0,'This is my first attempt at a model kit.  I chose the Thing because it is such a great looking kit.  I bought it from you guys last year.  I\'ve been thinking about getting into model kits for a long time.  Now that I\'ve tried it I\'m hooked.  Thanks Guys!'),(967,215,'1997-08-28 12:30:06',3829,215,'silene2',0,'My first resin kit.  Her name is acturally \"Siren,\" and though she may look like an angel, she\'s a real bad girl!  The \"egg\" is a glass sculpture I found at a crafts show, underlit with fluorescent light.  A beautivul kit, if you can find it.'),(968,286,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4029,286,'twoface',0,NULL),(969,4924,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4030,4924,'martian',0,NULL),(970,4925,'1997-09-04 10:15:03',3954,4925,'green1',0,'This is the oil painted head of the Horizon\'s Green Goblin.'),(971,4925,'1997-08-29 10:41:05',3726,4925,'tales',0,'Crypt Keeper oil painted head.'),(972,4926,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4031,4926,'misato',0,NULL),(973,4849,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3980,149,'monster',0,NULL),(974,265,'1997-09-04 16:08:23',4032,265,'stormtrooper',0,'Pactra Acrylic and Citadel paints used.'),(975,265,'1997-09-05 10:38:09',4033,265,'asuka2',0,'Pactra Acrylic, Citadel, ad Tamyia paints used.'),(976,265,'1997-09-04 16:13:59',4034,265,'misato2',0,'Pactra acrylic, Tamyia, and Citadel paints used.'),(977,265,'1997-09-04 16:16:54',3611,265,'belldandyred',0,'Pactra Acrylic, Tamyia, and Citadel paints used.'),(978,265,'1997-09-04 16:22:55',4035,265,'rei2',0,'Pactra Acrylic, Tamyia, and Citadel paints used.'),(979,265,'1997-09-04 16:24:03',4036,265,'reiwhite',0,'Pactra Acrylic, Tamyia, and Citadel paints used.'),(980,4933,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4037,4933,'am_cop',0,NULL),(981,4903,'1997-09-16 23:48:54',4039,4903,'bubbles',0,'This is the first in a series of limited designs that I will be offering.  Most are original creations, like the one you see here.  She comes with a base, which is not shown.'),(982,4911,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4038,4911,'warmachine',0,NULL),(983,346,'1997-09-17 22:05:12',3249,346,'kiko',0,'Nude and with Swim Suit.'),(984,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4044,346,'katsuragi',0,NULL),(985,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3445,346,'neptune',0,NULL),(986,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4043,346,'uranus',0,NULL),(987,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4042,346,'saturn',0,NULL),(988,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3990,346,'sailor',0,NULL),(989,4937,'1997-09-17 22:42:09',4040,4937,'label',0,'It comes from the Bubble Gum Crisis Japanese anime shows.'),(990,4936,'1998-04-02 10:08:11',4041,4936,'queen2',0,'My first figure model.'),(991,4939,'1997-09-22 19:44:09',4045,4939,'jeanne',0,'She has resculpted hair, thighs, calves, removed cloths, and added female parts.  I call her \"Jeanne Honey\".  '),(993,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4046,4940,'alien3',0,NULL),(994,4940,'1997-09-25 18:46:10',3769,4940,'stalking_xenomorph',0,'A very huge kit, I converted the mouth and added a scratchbuild tongue.'),(995,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3703,4940,'aliens',0,NULL),(996,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3303,4940,'alien',0,NULL),(997,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3661,4940,'drchannard',0,NULL),(998,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4047,4940,'zoanoid',0,NULL),(999,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3614,4940,'guyver',0,NULL),(1000,4940,'1997-09-25 13:15:17',3418,4940,'iria',0,'I did not like the face of this version, so I replaced it with the head from the first Iria kit.'),(1001,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3417,4940,'vszeram',0,NULL),(1002,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3572,4940,'vszeram',0,NULL),(1003,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3598,4940,'skullsoldier',0,NULL),(1004,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3454,4940,'preddio',0,NULL),(1005,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3277,4940,'decapitator',0,NULL),(1006,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4048,4940,'aulbath',0,NULL),(1007,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4049,4940,'xfiles',0,NULL),(1008,4940,'1997-09-25 13:31:47',4050,4940,'wrightsons',0,'This is a nice diorama kit, with a lot of options to convert.'),(1009,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3543,4940,'spawn',0,NULL),(1010,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3613,4940,'devilman',0,NULL),(1011,4940,'1997-09-25 13:38:01',4051,4940,'stalkerpred',0,'I used the Cellar Cast Predator Base a bit of imagination, to create the diorama.'),(1012,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3817,4940,'predator',0,NULL),(1013,4940,'1997-09-25 13:42:12',3272,4940,'vsalien',0,'I used the G-Force Alien base to give them a place to battle.'),(1014,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3306,4940,'pred2',0,NULL),(1015,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4053,4940,'jack',0,NULL),(1016,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4054,4940,'gkar',0,NULL),(1017,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3453,4940,'medusa',0,NULL),(1018,4940,'1997-09-25 19:46:59',4055,4940,'pumpkin',0,'Scratchbuild Diorama base.'),(1019,4940,'1997-09-25 20:01:25',4056,4940,'pumpkin',0,'Scratchbuild Diorama base.'),(1020,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3455,4940,'pumpkinhead',0,NULL),(1021,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4057,4940,'alien',0,NULL),(1022,354,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4061,354,'trooper',0,NULL),(1023,4947,'1997-09-29 16:01:42',4060,4947,'fool',0,'This is a character in an epic saga of an elder planet redefining itself and inhabitants.  This character is called \"The Fool\" for more information contact me at pineya12@aol.com.'),(1024,349,'1997-09-29 16:14:49',4058,349,'star_blazers',0,'I found this kit at a toy show in Denver several years ago. As usual in my\nexperience with Bandai kits, this spaceship was nicely packaged, well\nsculpted and precisely molded. Little cleanup work and filling was required\nduring construction as the parts fit nicely and were undistorted. It was a\npleasure to build. \n<p>\nThe kit was finished with Aleene\'s Premium Coat Acrylics (Duncan Enterprises)\nthinned with window cleaner and applied with in a Testors Aztek 3000\nairbrush. Details were highlighted using a crow quill ink pen and blue\npermanent drawing ink.\n<p>\nThe finished kit was entered in the IPMS Colorado Classic Model Show and\nContest held in Denver over Father\'s Day weekend 1997. After seeing the other\nkits at the Show, I was surprised but VERY pleased to have won a second place\naward!\n\n'),(1025,195,'1997-10-01 12:55:43',4062,195,'comlee2',0,'This is a killer kit if you can just take your time.'),(1026,280,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4063,280,'kong',0,NULL),(1027,296,'1998-05-26 13:26:03',4064,296,'docsav',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1028,296,'1998-05-26 13:41:58',3613,296,'devilman',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1029,296,'1998-05-26 13:45:31',4079,296,'talos',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1030,296,'1998-05-26 13:33:49',4066,296,'creature',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1031,296,'1998-05-26 13:25:09',4067,296,'frank',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1032,296,'1998-05-26 13:47:51',3737,296,'tusken',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1033,296,'1998-05-26 13:47:18',4068,296,'ming',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1034,296,'1998-05-26 13:43:20',4069,296,'cynin2fr',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1035,296,'1998-05-26 13:45:02',4070,296,'cynin2',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1036,296,'1998-05-26 13:42:49',3615,296,'guyvzoan',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1037,296,'1998-05-26 13:41:03',3598,296,'skull',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1038,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3476,4950,'alien11',0,NULL),(1039,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3944,4950,'alien2',0,NULL),(1040,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3477,4950,'alien3',0,NULL),(1041,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4071,4950,'aliena',0,NULL),(1042,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3478,4950,'alienq',0,NULL),(1043,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4013,4950,'batman2',0,NULL),(1044,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4072,4950,'chestb',0,NULL),(1045,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3480,4950,'facehu',0,NULL),(1046,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3479,4950,'foetus',0,NULL),(1047,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4073,4950,'haniba',0,NULL),(1048,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4074,4950,'id4',0,NULL),(1049,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3489,4950,'predat',0,NULL),(1050,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4075,4950,'sil',0,NULL),(1051,4950,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3518,4950,'t800',0,NULL),(1052,18,'2004-02-28 10:15:18',4076,282,'http://jamesart.com/cricket.html',1,NULL),(1053,4951,'1997-10-20 17:58:40',3758,4951,'goro',0,'This is a very nice kit. Kit gives you extra hands so you can pose Goro however you like.\nYou will have to do some major putty work to blend the joints. I painted mine with acrylic \npaints and finnished him off with oils.\n'),(1054,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4077,4951,'phantom',0,NULL),(1055,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3512,4951,'raptor',0,NULL),(1056,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4079,4951,'talos',0,NULL),(1057,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3925,4951,'stego',0,NULL),(1058,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4080,4951,'sentry',0,NULL),(1059,4953,'1997-10-20 18:27:11',4081,4953,'wolverine',0,'They require a good bit of work to make them look good, but with some determination and quite a bit of Squadron Green Putty, you can get some good results.'),(1060,4953,'1997-10-26 10:18:25',3258,4953,'xm01',0,' This was built straight out of the box.  The only thing I did was add a base\nmade from a RTV mold of a rock I found and cast with Durham\'s Water Putty, a\nplaster like mix that is much more durable than Plaster of Paris and lighter\ntoo.\n'),(1061,354,'1997-10-20 18:59:32',4082,354,'hellspawn',0,'This kit was sculpted by Toby A. Sells and Tony Spangler.  \n8 piece resin kit standing 12\". ordering info can be found at http://users.intermediatn.net/s&s.htm\n'),(1062,279,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4083,279,'redcat',0,NULL),(1063,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3408,4906,'lister',0,NULL),(1064,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4087,4906,'cat',0,NULL),(1065,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4086,4906,'saxon',0,NULL),(1066,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4085,4906,'lyra',0,NULL),(1067,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4084,4906,'hussar',0,NULL),(1068,4957,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4090,4957,'hunchback',0,NULL),(1069,4957,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4088,4957,'nefarious',0,NULL),(1070,4957,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3917,4957,'wings',0,NULL),(1071,4957,'1997-10-28 21:30:48',3664,4957,'moonsinger',0,'Psinted with Polly S and Liquitex acrylics and Polytranspar Taxidermy paints. '),(1072,4957,'1997-10-28 21:34:51',3752,4957,'alex',0,'Painted with liquitex and Polly S acrylics and with braided theatrical crepe hair pony tail.  '),(1073,157,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4091,211,'girl',0,NULL),(1074,4772,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4094,299,'jimmy',0,NULL),(1075,4772,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4092,299,'cthulhu',0,NULL),(1076,4772,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4093,299,'spider',0,NULL),(1077,269,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4095,269,'lando',0,NULL),(1078,269,'1997-11-10 19:02:23',4096,269,'predat',0,'The spots are done with a fine Sharpie black pen and the bust painted \nwith Horizon acrylics. The entire bust is sealed with a semigloss\nacrylic clear coat.\n'),(1079,4963,'1997-11-10 20:29:10',3521,4963,'thor',0,'  I try to use the traditional color scheme when painting comic book\ncharacters, and ignore the box art.  I was unsatisfied with the plastic cape\nprovided so I used it as a mold and stiffened some fabric with diluted white\nglue instead, creating a much more \"life-like\" cape.  This model needed a\nbase to keep it from tipping over, so a little sculpty painted as carved\nstone did the job.  This was all done with brushwork, I\'m still resisting\nbuying an airbrush.\n\n'),(1080,4962,'1997-11-10 20:33:11',4097,4962,'superman',0,'\"This Superman model was patterned after the one painted in the\nKingdom Come series, which is a good series of itself.  My thanks to Mike\nJames and Vance Thomas to their articles in the gremlins\' and to the Great\nGremlin himself..\"'),(1081,4906,'1997-11-10 20:36:22',4098,4906,'knight',0,' Modified kit using scratchbuilt belts, scabbard and shield\n'),(1082,4961,'1997-11-10 20:52:54',4100,4961,'beetjack',0,' This is an original sculpture by Dan Perez, entitled \"We\'ve\nCome For Your Daughter, Chuck.\"  Inspired by the movie \"Beetlejuice,\" the\nsculpture depicts Beetlegeuse in his Beetlesnake form.  The base is a\njack-in-the-box with batwings.\n'),(1083,4965,'1997-11-10 20:56:44',4099,4965,'vamp',0,' This is an original sculpture by Gabriel Marquez, entitled\n\"River Bottom Blackheart.\"  Inspired by a comic book cover, the sculpture\ndepicts Lestat, the vampire from Anne Rice\'s \"Interview With the Vampire,\"\nrising up out of the river.  Lampreys and skeletal piranhas are\nincorporated into the base.\n'),(1084,4966,'1997-11-12 19:17:15',4101,4966,'guyver',0,' The base is totally scratch built using epoxy putty, pvc, and copper piping, various sizes of screening, etc.\n'),(1085,37,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4102,149,'death',0,NULL),(1086,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3967,4951,'vamp',0,NULL),(1087,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4105,4951,'mcbeth',0,NULL),(1088,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3358,4951,'kato',0,NULL),(1089,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4104,4951,'elf',0,NULL),(1090,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4103,4951,'brave',0,NULL),(1091,270,'1997-11-15 14:22:04',4110,270,'rose',0,'   Not to put to fine a point on it, out of the box,\nRose is a disturbing kit.  She\'s a realistic take on\nfemale undead - emmaciated and really repulsive.\nSo repulsive, in fact, as to be considered unaesthetic!\nI decided to rework her by reposing the figure slightly,\nand sculpting on a long flowing shroud.  That and a warmer fleshtone scheme w/ some makeup and a shock of punkish hair made for a very cool looking female kit IMHO!\n\n'),(1092,270,'1997-11-15 14:24:24',4109,270,'gun',0,'This and Boris were my two favorites at MMP4.\nThe MBPFX busts are a wonderfully imaginative,\nnicely detailed and cast, and a bargain at the\nprice.  The size alone makes any of them an\nimpressive display piece, and the gunslinger\nis my favorite of the lot.\n\n'),(1093,270,'1997-11-15 14:26:46',4108,270,'zombie1',0,'A tip for those building this one: Reinforce\nthose legs!  They might as well be pipecleaners\nfor all the support they provide, so ram rod\nup in there and fortify it w/ resin, epoxy,\nor plaster.  Likewise, the base needs bulking\nup.  I used Bondo.\n'),(1094,270,'1997-11-15 14:29:23',4107,270,'gamera',0,'I can\'t say enough about this kit.  First,\nhe\'s 1:100 which is BIG for a Kaiju kit.  He\'s\nalso noteworthy for having been pulled off\nthe animatronic prop from Gamera 2.  If you are\na fan of the new Gamera, this is THE kit to get.\n\nI was foolish enough to go for a diorama\ndepicting a scene in the film where Gamera has\njust thwarted the Legion, and is about to face\nits wrath in the form of 1000\'s of Legion warriors.\nMy dio only has about 70 individually cast & painted\nbugs, but that was PLENTY!  The base was fully scratch\nbuilt from wood, bondo, sculpey, plaster, and pretty\nmuch anything else I got my mitts on.  The gap in the\nrear wall, through which one of the Legio plant roots is\nprotruding, is lit w/ a weird strobing glow.\n\nKudos to Gremlin Leann for service above an beyond.\nShe sculpted the gorgeous G2 nameplate, and assembled\nand painted every one of those bugs.  (Each was a three\npiece casting, and a kit in itself.)  And just think\nhoney, you\'ll get to do more when I get around to\ncasting the others!!! \n'),(1095,270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4106,270,'debbie',0,NULL),(1096,270,'1997-11-15 16:34:56',3877,270,'boris1',0,'This one was built out of the box, the only\naddition being some doggie drool.  I went for\na slightly ruddier color scheme than Tom\'s\nway-cool pale Chihuahua approach.  Paints\nincluded airbrush acrylics, taxidermy paints,\nand watercolors.\n'),(1097,4974,'1997-11-16 19:15:57',3417,4974,'iria',0,'The tricky part is building the gun i sugest using a hair dryer or a heat gun to soften the part. I used acrylic paint and oils. The back wall is stratch built. '),(1098,4974,'1997-11-16 19:19:02',4012,4974,'bwire',0,'It  was done the same way the black \non the corset is painted using modern master paint (not to be confused with \ntestors model master paint) i painted it on with brush. The flesh tones was \ndone using horizon flesh tone #3.  after the basic colors are done i start \nusing oil paints for the hights and shadows.\n'),(1099,4974,'1997-11-16 19:23:49',3302,4974,'spec',0,'38 special w/ the dressing partetion pic.#2 is the same thing with out the \npartetion.  It is a resin kit.\nthe flesh tone is air brushed on in acrytlic paint and finished with oils.\n\n'),(1100,4974,'1997-11-16 19:28:04',4111,4974,'shecrow',0,'The she crow (real name is crow hoe) is air brushed using horizon flesh tone \n#3 then painted with oils for the highlites and shadows the boots did not come \nwith laces so i driled them and added my own.  The back wall is scratch built \nusing a plastic called simtra its like sheet stireen and balsa wood combined \ntogether its very strong. it also has two sides so the piece can be displayed in front of a mirror.\n'),(1101,4974,'1997-11-25 22:26:57',3957,4974,'superman',0,'This is a discontinued horizon kit its made of vinyl and filled with plaster \nof paris.   The base  has a hand painted emblem on it and is high glossed \nusing floor finish.'),(1102,4974,'1997-11-16 19:32:08',3822,4974,'comando',0,'The commando was painted all back then high glossed with floor finish the \nsilver was done with horizon silver its the brightest silver paint on the \nmarket then i used black oil paint to show shadows. '),(1103,4974,'1997-11-16 19:36:18',4015,4974,'heavy',0,'Heavy metal was a real challenge to build it was a lot of fun.\nAll the floors and walls that apper in the fictures are stratch built using \nsimtra ain plastic sells it.  The store is in new york city.  the next pics i \nsend will include lights.  Some of my work can be seen at \namok time inc. in long island new york i will also be at the chiller theater \nshow at the amok time table.  Look for neo new york. \n\n'),(1104,4975,'1997-11-16 19:54:26',4112,4975,'alien',0,' I cut the legs off and made it appear to be coming out at you from\nunder some sewer water kind of like in the movie \"Aliens\". I just used a\nbunch of clear epoxy mixed with various amounts of different colors for the\nwater effect.\n'),(1105,4790,'1997-11-16 21:47:47',4113,215,'ttman',0,'Comes with lightening bolt talisman base and guitar cord for super-detailing.'),(1106,4790,'1997-11-16 21:49:59',4114,215,'grandpa',0,'Comes with awesome labratory diorama base and cob webs for super-detailing.'),(1107,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3543,4951,'spawn',0,NULL),(1108,4951,'1997-11-17 12:06:13',3545,4951,'loncha',0,'This is a very good quality kit. All parts come together\nwith no fit problems. I painted this kit using acryilic \npaints as a base and then finished it with oils.\n'),(1109,4953,'1997-11-17 13:35:24',4115,4953,'brave',0,'It is based on the movie, so the figure looks a little\nlike Mel Gibson.  No modifications were done to the kit.  I painted the\nfigure pimarily with Polly-S paints, except for the flesh areas which were\ndone with oils.\n'),(1110,330,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4116,330,'myths',0,NULL),(1111,319,'1997-12-04 21:49:46',3725,319,'chewi',0,' I created a latex rubber mold from the original Screamin\' vinyl model. Then poured a plaster casting. Please note: I did this as a test for the paint/colour layout, I do not support recasting for profit purposes.\n'),(1112,319,'2000-08-17 17:58:00',4117,319,'hoth',0,'Note: kit box lid was used for backdrop in these pics.'),(1113,319,'2000-08-17 17:50:27',3506,319,'hulk',0,'Base and backdrop created with a combination of artist plaster, coat hanger wire and wood. For a larger clearer picture of this kit please visit Ryan\'s Hobbies Gallery <a href=\"http://www.islandnet.com/~grealyrk\" target=\"_blank\"><B>HERE</B></a>\n'),(1114,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4162,316,'werewolf',0,NULL),(1116,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4160,4987,'templar',0,NULL),(1117,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4158,155,'resurrected',0,NULL),(1118,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4149,4987,'gargoyle',0,NULL),(1119,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4146,316,'fire',0,NULL),(1120,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4143,4987,'spawn',0,NULL),(1121,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3965,4988,'darkness',0,NULL),(1122,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4119,4987,'evil_ash',0,NULL),(1123,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4156,316,'witch',0,NULL),(1124,37,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4172,299,'jobpit',0,NULL),(1125,4763,'1998-01-11 22:15:33',4164,316,'zombie1',0,'(c) 1990 S.K.A.I Original Design.'),(1126,4763,'1997-12-18 23:28:36',4140,4988,'nosferatu',0,'(c) 1995 S.K.A.I Original Design.'),(1127,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3990,346,'spluto',0,NULL),(1128,346,'1997-12-19 22:11:42',4076,346,'cricket',0,'I name this kit Cricket-san because I went with a whole different idea from the ones Mike offered.\nI enjoy Japanese girls and especially when they where school uniforms. The tie and sailor flap are felt cloth\nand the skirt belt is felt.\n'),(1130,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4174,346,'star',0,NULL),(1131,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4176,346,'tiedup',0,NULL),(1132,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4177,346,'igrat',0,NULL),(1133,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3771,346,'pretty',0,NULL),(1134,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3217,346,'dancer',0,NULL),(1135,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3218,346,'dancer2',0,NULL),(1136,346,'1997-12-20 07:53:03',4179,346,'makoto',0,'Makoto Kusanagi is a android in the anime movie, \"Ghost in the Shell.\"\n'),(1137,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4180,346,'pussnb',0,NULL),(1138,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3613,4951,'devilman',0,NULL),(1139,4951,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4181,4951,'gallows',0,NULL),(1140,4994,'1997-12-20 09:06:14',4183,4994,'bron',0,'A one of a kind sculpture of the prehistoric mammal, brontotherium.\n'),(1141,4994,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4182,4994,'yeti',0,NULL),(1142,4996,'1997-12-20 10:27:10',3289,4996,'eldar',0,'This figure placed 3rd in the Sci Fi and Fantasy Figures and\nCreatures (50mm and smaller) section of the 1996 IPMS Model Expo in Melbourne, Australia.\n\n'),(1143,4996,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4192,4996,'gangers',0,NULL),(1144,4996,'1998-04-02 18:16:13',4187,4996,'teclis',0,'This figure placed 1st in the Sci Fi and Fantasy Figures and Creatures (50mm and\n            smaller) section of the 1998 IPMS Model Expo in Melbourne, Australia. '),(1145,4996,'1997-12-20 10:30:39',4184,4996,'scum',0,'This figure placed 2nd in the Sci Fi and Fantasy Figures and\nCreatures (50mm and smaller) section of the 1996 IPMS Model Expo in Melbourne, Australia.\n'),(1146,4996,'1997-12-20 10:32:11',4190,4996,'mortificator',0,'This figure won 1st place in the Science Fiction and Fantasy\nFigures and Creatures (less than 120mm) section of the 1995 IPMS Model Expo in Melbourne, Australia.\n'),(1147,4996,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4189,4996,'sorceress',0,NULL),(1148,4996,'1997-12-20 10:35:00',4191,4996,'ogryn',0,'This figure won 1st place in the Science Fiction and Fantasy\nFigures and Creatures (less than 120mm) section of the 1994 IPMS Model Expo in Melbourne, Australia.  The banner was designed on my computer, printed out in black and white then hand painted.\n'),(1149,5002,'1997-12-20 11:46:44',4194,5002,'power',0,'This buildup of the Dorvack PAM-74C Dunc & F-12 Cupid \nis around 10 years old, but somewhat timely now, in its \nsimilarilty to Robert A. Heinlein\'s Mobile Infantry \ncombat suits and the cinematic release of Starship Troopers.\n'),(1150,5004,'1997-12-20 11:49:18',4193,5004,'cammy',0,'This is a nice little kit from the Korean manufacturer Elfin.  The model was painted with an airbrush using Gunze Sanyo acrylics, and washed with oil paints.  The dry-brushing was done with '),(1151,5003,'1997-12-20 11:55:01',4195,5003,'warprin',0,'This is a four part kit, painted with Humbrol enamels. One of a series of\nwhite metal figures of characters from film and TV.  Photograph by David Trelfer\n'),(1153,5004,'1997-12-20 12:49:31',3418,5004,'iria',0,'The kit had some serious fit problems, especially where \nthe upper body joined the waist.  A heater gun was used to reshape the parts for a better fit.  The model was painted with Gunze Sanyo \npaints.\n'),(1154,279,'1997-12-20 12:51:46',4197,279,'littlewolf',0,'The kit was airbrushed & hand painted using Humbrol enamels.  The base was detailed with epoxy putty and static grass. As always Tim Richard\'s imagination & sculpting talent made this figure a joy to paint.                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n'),(1155,5009,'1997-12-20 13:10:34',4196,5009,'falcon',0,'This is 32\" long, 24\" wide. about 4000 parts. Light up cockpit and engine. Same scale as original ILM model made for The Empire Strikes Back.\n'),(1156,275,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3967,275,'vamp',0,NULL),(1157,5011,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4198,5011,'keepfit',0,NULL),(1158,5011,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4199,5011,'triv',0,NULL),(1159,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3819,346,'vampirella',0,NULL),(1161,5015,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4203,5015,'groo',0,NULL),(1162,4910,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3508,4910,'joker',0,NULL),(1163,5016,'1998-01-05 16:41:25',4202,5016,'star_wars',0,'Made In U.S.A. Price: $150 - Only in Argentina (it Includes shipping and handling).  Other countries consult, rodrigor@satlink.com.ar           \n'),(1165,5017,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4201,5017,'spgirl',0,NULL),(1166,5014,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4205,5014,'genie',0,NULL),(1167,5017,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4200,5017,'cupid',0,NULL),(1168,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4152,316,'lamia',0,NULL),(1169,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4123,316,'saw',0,NULL),(1170,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4153,5057,'lost',0,NULL),(1171,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4133,4987,'gorgo',0,NULL),(1172,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3226,4988,'slayer',0,NULL),(1173,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4141,149,'nosferietta',0,NULL),(1174,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4161,316,'king',0,NULL),(1175,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4155,4987,'paramour',0,NULL),(1177,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4206,316,'deadite',0,NULL),(1178,4940,'1998-01-08 13:23:47',3817,4940,'predvdutch',0,'I was a bit unhappy with the existing Confrontation kit, so I did my own diorama, using these wonderful sculpted pieces.  Base is scratchbuild using Clear Resin.  The  movie scene is when the Hunter is showing his face for the first time.'),(1179,4940,'1998-01-08 13:21:45',4209,4940,'predvdutch',0,'I was a bit unhappy with the existing Confrontation kit, so I did my own diorama, using these wonderful sculpted pieces.  Base is scratchbuild using Clear Resin.  The  movie scene is when the Hunter is showing his face for the first time.'),(1180,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3561,4940,'gremlin',0,NULL),(1181,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4207,4940,'redbaron',0,NULL),(1182,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3476,4940,'alienh',0,NULL),(1183,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4208,4940,'alieng',0,NULL),(1184,4900,'1998-01-08 13:31:25',4181,4900,'gallows',0,'An absolute blast to paint!  Rifle strap was omitted due to extremem weight of white metal hands/gun piece.  This is my favorite model ever and I give it my highest recommendation.'),(1185,5020,'1998-01-08 13:48:26',4212,5020,'maidmer',0,'\"Maidmer\" is an original cration.  I used the odd bit of lead and wire and a pair of taxidermy eyes.  '),(1186,5020,'1998-01-08 13:50:25',4211,5020,'pirate',0,'It has been lightly convereted Phoenix figure and if you don\'t find this funny at first glance, look again.'),(1187,204,'1998-01-08 14:00:16',3859,204,'luke',0,'I scratch built bridles, stirrups, light saber, belt pouches and an unseen shoulder pouch.  The snow is a ceramic called \"brush on snow\".'),(1188,204,'1998-01-08 14:27:06',3213,204,'quark',0,'The cup is a lid (cap) from a \"Superglue\" tube.'),(1189,5021,'1998-01-08 14:48:33',4214,5021,'predator',0,'I bought this kit at the 1997 San Diego comic con, it is the special sneak preview edition Predator Model.  I started by airbrushing the base coat in Createx dark brown on the head and black on the rest of the body, then dry brushing on a Delta ceramic coat flesh tan over the head and body, and applying the dots and netting with a sharpie pen the teeth are Delta light ivory with dark brown plaque stains.  The armor was painted in Tamiya color gunmetal, then I dry brushed the gun metal mixed with white on top of that.  The knives were Tamiya color chrome silver, the necklace was painted black then dry brushed with white, and the blood on his left leg that you can\'t see in the picture was florescent green mixed with yellow.'),(1190,307,'1998-01-08 14:55:44',4215,307,'bella',0,'Based on photos of a clients girlfriend from Italy.  Everything was going well until I was slated to recieve the final payment for the commistion.  I think I\'ve been had.'),(1191,280,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4208,280,'smallalien',0,NULL),(1192,208,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4216,208,'victim',0,NULL),(1193,208,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3731,208,'pinhead',0,NULL),(1194,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4124,316,'dracula',0,NULL),(1195,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4131,4987,'egg',0,NULL),(1196,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4168,197,'melt',0,NULL),(1197,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4145,4987,'beast',0,NULL),(1198,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4148,4988,'freebooter',0,NULL),(1199,4763,'1998-03-23 09:28:53',4217,316,'anna',0,'Included with the kit are a set of glass\neyes for added realism.'),(1200,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4147,149,'fish',0,NULL),(1201,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4139,149,'nile',0,NULL),(1202,5024,'1998-01-15 09:43:13',4218,5024,'motoko',0,'\n'),(1204,157,'1998-01-12 19:44:27',4220,211,'esmeralda',0,'Sculpted by E. Luis & A. Lopez<br>\nDesign by Eli Raphael<br>\nrepresentative:\nPuff & Stuff, 703 Lowry Ave, Jeannette PA 15644<br>\nph (412)523-8444 or fax them at (412)523-6979<br>\n'),(1206,4797,'1998-01-15 22:33:47',4219,5029,'gene',0,'Also included are small paper guitar pics scanned from an actual concert\npick that was given to Scott by Gene.\nThe Bass Guitar is a rare version of Gene\'s custom 1975\n- 1976 design.\nThe model base is from the cover of the album \"Rock and Roll Over\"\n'),(1207,5032,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4221,74,'mask',0,NULL),(1209,4843,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4223,348,'schlitzie',0,NULL),(1211,4994,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4225,4994,'rhed',0,NULL),(1212,4936,'1998-01-20 21:31:21',4224,4936,'bryn',0,'Outstanding sculpt, highly recommended!\n'),(1214,4864,'2006-06-09 12:52:42',4226,4864,'creature',0,'For more Creature models, visit my site,\r\nwww.monsterjones.com'),(1215,4864,'1999-03-11 13:15:35',4227,4864,'curse',0,'Scratchbuilt base with Geometric\'s stumps and things.  Gargoyles from Toy Joy.'),(1216,4864,'1998-01-24 10:54:44',3265,4864,'dracula',0,'Custom base'),(1217,176,'1998-01-24 12:50:14',4230,176,'catwoman',0,'Painted using Floquil and Tamiya paints, shadded with pastels, treasure chest added from pet fish supply store.'),(1218,176,'1998-01-24 12:51:30',4228,176,'renwolf',0,'Painted using Floquil and Tamiya paints, shadded with pastels.'),(1219,176,'1998-01-24 12:52:43',4229,176,'boobira',0,'Painted using Floquil and Tamiya paints, shadded with pastels.'),(1220,176,'1998-01-24 12:53:40',3249,176,'kiko',0,'Painted using Floquil and Tamiya paints, shadded with pastels.'),(1221,4842,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4231,149,'rise',0,NULL),(1222,4994,'1998-01-26 18:45:20',4232,4994,'martian',0,'  A one of a kind sculpture based on Ray Harryhausen\'s martian for his unmade War of the Worlds film. Rendered in super sculpey and painted with acrylics.\n'),(1223,5002,'1998-01-29 13:47:15',4233,5002,'c3po',0,'The much maligned Screamin 1/4 C3PO is nevertheless an impressively sized kit, especially to the non-hobbyist.  I reinforced the upper torso with a shell of Super Sculpey and \"wired\" the waist with solder and stripped wire.\n'),(1225,5002,'1998-01-29 12:49:00',3613,5002,'devilman',0,'I always thought Devilman looked more sporty with wings.\nLuckily, Takeya provided wings in the Geometric Pumpkinhead 2 kit.\n'),(1226,5042,'1998-01-29 12:50:35',3731,5042,'pinhead',0,'Painted in Acrylics and Inks.\n<p>\nThe main image was photographed with lighting effects and then digitally composited onto a Photoshop background.\n'),(1227,245,'1998-01-29 13:03:38',4234,245,'batbust',0,'This is a kit bash of Sugitas Batman.  The Torso was converted into a bust and stuck on an appropriate base.  The paint up was for a friend but I managed to get some pics before I handed it over.\n'),(1228,5043,'1998-01-29 13:17:05',3530,5043,'wolverine',0,'This is a great kit for advanced modelers.  A unique pose and good detail make this kit fun to build.  I attached Wolverine to a styro base, then added some foliage and a small tree branch to finish this kit.\n'),(1229,5043,'1998-01-29 13:19:31',4235,5043,'thor',0,'This kit was wonderful to put together and paint.  The model\nhad very few flaws, excellent detail and great pose.  The only thing about this kit I would change is the cape, it is flimsy and poorly made.  Overall this kit is great for more advanced modelers.\n'),(1230,5043,'1998-01-29 13:21:04',3528,5043,'venom',0,'This is a great kit for beginners.  A wonderful pose and good detail make this kit fun to build.\n'),(1231,5043,'1998-01-29 13:22:42',3517,5043,'steel',0,'This is an awesome kit for advanced modelers.  A wonderful pose and great detail make this kit fun to build.  The kit once finished looks incredible.\n'),(1232,5043,'1998-01-29 13:24:58',3497,5043,'cable',0,'This is a great kit.  A wonderful pose and good detail make\nthis kit fun to build.  I added Horizons Brick Wall Base to make this model stand out.\n\n'),(1233,5043,'1998-01-29 13:26:20',3506,5043,'hulk',0,'This is a great kit for beginners.  A wonderful pose and good detail make this kit fun to build.\n\n'),(1234,4936,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4236,4936,'carina',0,NULL),(1235,4886,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4237,4886,'hulk',0,NULL),(1236,5045,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4238,5045,'grotesque',0,NULL),(1237,269,'1998-02-02 16:36:58',4245,269,'spock1',0,'The face detail is excellent and as usual the entire kit fits extremely well.  Not very many parts in the kit 4 to be exact.  The price is about $49.95 at your local hobby shop.  The face and tunic are done with Horizon acrylics and it is sealed with Poly-S clear coat.\n'),(1238,4974,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4239,4974,'lura',0,NULL),(1239,4974,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3418,4974,'iria2',0,NULL),(1240,4974,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4240,4974,'amazon',0,NULL),(1241,4974,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4257,4974,'alien',0,NULL),(1242,4974,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4242,4974,'rei',0,NULL),(1243,286,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4243,286,'freeze',0,NULL),(1244,286,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4246,286,'batgirl',0,NULL),(1245,286,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3494,286,'batman',0,NULL),(1246,286,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3513,286,'batboy',0,NULL),(1248,286,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3888,286,'mbpeng',0,NULL),(1249,5011,'1998-02-02 17:36:06',4247,5011,'tguard',0,'This is my original Fantasy Figure.Masterpiece made by Waterclay.and it convert to resin.  Painting by artist\'s oil.\n'),(1250,5048,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4248,5048,'cobra',0,NULL),(1251,296,'1998-05-26 13:26:31',3432,296,