ww.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1263,296,'1998-05-26 13:45:57',3671,296,'deunan',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1265,286,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4244,286,'riddler1',0,NULL),(1266,5052,'1998-03-01 13:57:35',4262,5052,'thething',0,'\"The Thing\" by billiken on the base by Mike Parks\n(that I picked up from him at Wonderfest 95).  This is one of my favorites.'),(1267,5052,'1998-03-01 14:13:42',4263,5052,'cyclops',0,'This a kit that I picked up last spring for $40 and restored it.\nI really enjoyed doing this kit as I had this kit when\nI was a kid.'),(1268,5054,'1998-03-01 14:37:22',4264,5054,'machiko',0,'Original kit is the Virtual Fighter - Sarah.\nConverted using sculpey 3 to look like Alien Hunter. Predator armour concept used.'),(1269,205,'1998-03-01 14:52:03',3752,205,'alex',0,'This kit is excellent!  My wife hates it because it\'s so scary!\nSpecial features: he glows in the dark! I found a translucent glow in the\ndark paint that added that dead skin effect perfectly. The chains are gold.'),(1270,205,'1998-03-01 14:59:59',4265,205,'mj12',0,'Nice elegent design, easy to build.  Should be resin - the vinyl needs to be very re-inforced due to the slender legs.'),(1271,5052,'1998-03-14 23:26:38',4266,5052,'warlord',0,'This is my first attempt of sculpting kits.  The Warlord is my favorite comic\nbook hero and for years I had hoped somebody would make a kit of it.  Well it\nnever happened.  Fleagore talked me into making it myself so I did.  I\'m just\nsurprised that it turned out so good (at least I think so).  But to everybody\nit\'s only far to say - you be the judge!  Only 75 will be made.  If this kit turns out to be a hit I\nwill do The Warlords enemy Deimos (on a small base), and attach the two bases\ntogether.\n'),(1272,224,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3206,224,'eggs',0,NULL),(1273,268,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4240,268,'amazon',0,NULL),(1274,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4121,4987,'binky',0,NULL),(1275,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4122,4909,'cat12',0,NULL),(1276,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4125,316,'curse',0,NULL),(1277,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4128,4987,'victim',0,NULL),(1278,4763,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4129,4987,'doug',0,NULL),(1279,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4278,4906,'spectra',0,NULL),(1280,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4272,4906,'rhonda',0,NULL),(1281,4906,'1998-03-22 11:04:43',4273,4906,'lyta',0,'Modifed from Soldat\'s Female Federation Crew figure.'),(1282,4906,'1998-03-22 11:04:53',4274,4906,'ivanova',0,'This was a modified Geometrics ST-TNG Troi.'),(1283,4906,'1998-03-22 11:05:03',4275,4906,'dragn2',0,'This was an extensively modified AMT/ERTL Capt. Kirk with sheet brass helmet\nand armor, extensive body work with epoxy putty, lead foil belts, brass wire\nbuckles and fine lace for the trim.'),(1284,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4277,4906,'draco',0,NULL),(1285,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4271,4906,'bwarrss',0,NULL),(1286,4906,'1998-03-22 11:06:36',4270,4906,'bard',0,'Scratchbuilt lyre was added to the figure.'),(1287,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4276,4906,'angel2',0,NULL),(1288,4906,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4269,4906,'ahuntrs',0,NULL),(1289,4911,'1998-03-22 11:41:52',4279,4911,'borg',0,'I made this model from Star Trek First Contact.  I built it from scratch using ABS, Styrene, rubber, and metal.  It has moving fingers and blinking lights.  I will also sell the plans to build one to anyone who wants one.'),(1290,4994,'1998-03-29 14:04:21',4280,4994,'grif',0,'A one of a kind sculpture of the Griffon from \"The Golden Voyage of Sinbad\".'),(1291,5067,'1998-04-02 14:30:35',4282,5067,'alien',0,' It was sculpted with eye sockets and a brow ridge that I didn\'t like, so I puttied them in and sanded it smooth.'),(1292,5067,'1998-04-02 15:03:44',4283,5067,'crow',0,'I resculpted the boots and added some hair to the top of his head.'),(1293,5067,'1998-04-02 15:55:28',4284,5067,'iria',0,'I detailed her outfit with a .005 Pigma Micron pen. I also scratch built the base from sheet metal and Elmers wood putty (because it cracks when you dry it really fast with a hair dryer or heat gun).'),(1294,5067,'1998-04-02 21:26:37',4286,5067,'bane',0,'I scratch built the sidewalk from styrofoam and lightweight spackle. The drain is made from balsa wood, and the asphalt was made using woodland scenics black medium ballast. I did keep the manhole cover from the original base though.'),(1295,5067,'1998-04-03 01:21:05',4287,5067,'bith',0,' I made this little spawn of my imagination from a 6 inch wooden sculptors maquette. I sculpted a face on him and gave him some angel wings I found at a craft store. I made the cracks on him using cracklin\' paint. I used a toothbrush to spatter the blood on his hands and a little on his wings, the blood strings under his hands are clear epoxy. I scratch built a desert style base to finish him off.'),(1296,5078,'1998-04-04 07:15:21',4288,5078,'aurg',0,'This is the Monogram re-issue of  the Aurora Godzilla kit. I had several of these models\nas a child and they got played with to the point of oblivion. I bought this kit at the Spring \'97 Chiller\nshow for about $60. It was complete and unbuilt in an open box. To see more of my Godzilla\ncollection check out my <a href=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\"> Godzilla Room </a>. '),(1297,5078,'1998-04-04 07:14:01',4292,5078,'bara',0,'Baragon is the antagonist in Toho\'s Frankenstien Conquers the World. He also had a\nbrief appearance in Destroy All Monsters. The monster suit was recycled over the years in several\nUltra Q and Ultraman episodes. I picked up this kit at the \'94 Fall Chiller show. At the time I had no\nclue how to build a vinyl model. I did some research and dove right in. I guess my efforts paid off,\nBaragon won a second place prize at G-Con\'96. To see more of my Kaiju Collection check out my <a href=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\"> Godzilla Room </a>.  '),(1298,5078,'1998-04-04 07:16:50',4289,5078,'gigan',0,'Gigan appeared in two Godzilla movies in the early seventies. He also made an\nappearance on the Japanese television show Zone Fighter. I custom built the base using a N-scale\nbuildings and a ready-made wood base. To see more of my Godzilla collection visit my <a href=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\"> Godzilla Room </a>. '),(1299,5078,'1998-04-04 07:11:20',4291,5078,'gvsmoth',0,'The Kaiyodo Godzilla \'64 kit was sculpted in a very dynamic pose. I decided to add a\nBandai Mothra figure to G\'s tail to re-enact the classic battle at the end of the film. I plan on one day\ncreating a diorama with this piece and a second Mothra caterpillar. This kit won second prize in a\nKit Builders Magazine contest. To see more of my Godzilla collection visit my <a href=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\"> Godzilla Room </a>. \n\n'),(1300,5078,'1998-04-04 07:18:48',4290,5078,'swing',0,'This a resin recast of the Paradise vinyl kit. I am aware of the current controversy over\nrecasts, as a result this will be my first and last recast kit. This kit required a lot of prep work just to\nbegin building it. I even had to resculpt one of  Godzilla\'s spines. My hard work paid off because it\nwon a second place prize at G-Con \'96. To see more of my Godzilla collection visit my <a href=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\"> Godzilla Room </a>. '),(1303,5080,'1998-04-04 10:32:46',4298,5080,'bob',0,'This kit was painted using Liquatex and Tamiya acrylics, and detailed with Humbrol and Testors enamels. This was my 3rd figure kit since starting the supercool hobby (thanks to this web site).'),(1304,5080,'1998-04-04 14:29:54',3278,5080,'bil',0,'This kit was purchased from Monsters In Motion for $100.00 and included an autographed picture of Bill Hinzman.  The kit was finished with Humbrol enamels, Tamiya acrylics, and Winsor and Newton artists oil colors.'),(1307,5079,'1998-04-26 19:15:17',4301,5086,'nest',0,'Lil Monsters is the exclusive distibutor of this kit. This base is not going to available at wonderfest. Do not look for it there, not gonna happen.'),(1310,5077,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4293,5077,'Jke',0,NULL),(1312,5061,'1998-04-06 07:57:00',3878,5061,'mars4',0,'Scratch built base ( First try )'),(1314,5061,'1998-04-19 23:23:52',3216,5061,'emp3',0,'Build up done with flat black and Horizon paints. Flesh tone was done using number 5 and working to a number 1. His cane was done using a combination of green,brown and dark red and finished with a clear gloss.'),(1324,5088,'1998-04-09 17:52:10',4308,5088,'jason',0,'My first attemp at building a base. It\'s kind of a joke with good ol\' Jason ready to welcome you to Camp Crystal Lake.'),(1325,5088,'1998-04-09 17:50:11',4308,5088,'JasonV',0,'Here\'s Jason again, this time without the mask.'),(1327,5088,'1998-04-09 18:02:14',4309,5088,'michael1',0,'The base isn\'t finished since I will later add grass and some flowers near the gravestone. Thanks to my good friend Steve for the idea.'),(1330,204,'1998-04-10 14:55:16',4310,204,'dragonkiller',0,' The Screamin\' Red Dragon was a straight build-up. I changed, however the verlinden \"Black Prince\" to a tuetonic knight. Just some color changes and the \"Iron Cross\" emblems. The base is a mix of florists foam, Durhams water putty, Woodland Scenics, kitty litter, and a bunch of other stuff.'),(1333,5067,'1998-04-12 14:19:35',4311,5067,'c3po',0,' As you can see from the photo I added L.E.D lights to his eyes. The diameter of his eyes is the exact diameter of a whole punch so I scribed some lines into clear blister pack and punched them out to create a \"lens\" over the L.E.D. I also discarded the vinyl belly and created a new one out of Black cloth and real wires. To finish him properly, I scratch built a desert base with a trail of footprints behind him. '),(1334,5067,'1998-04-18 23:50:58',4312,5067,'spidey',0,' Airbrushed with ceramcoat paints, I did the lines on his suit with a pigma micron pen, I used Tamiya gloss Black for the spider on his chest and the black around his eyes. I didn\'t do a base for him because this was for a customer and he had a display case designed for it.'),(1336,5061,'1998-04-19 22:43:36',4308,5061,'jason3',0,'Jason was done with much care to the waist and upper torso, I had a very poor fit. Jason was base coated black. I use an olive green for his shirt and pants.Dry bushing a small bit of black to give an oily look. The mask was done with an off white and dry brushing of dark grey and black.'),(1337,5067,'1998-04-19 22:52:26',4314,5067,'zen',0,' I did this one a while ago, so it\'s not as good as the recent build-ups I\'ve posted, but I didn\'t see one in the gallery so I figured what the hell. The base is a piece of bass wood; Painted black and spattered with white paint to simulate stars.'),(1338,5061,'1998-04-19 23:08:58',3629,5061,'Phant4',0,'Done with enamel paints,This build up was done before any knowledge of putting a primer on or filling seams.'),(1339,5106,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4327,5107,'hellraiser',0,NULL),(1340,5109,'1998-06-07 12:01:50',4331,5108,'aquarius',0,'This is one of the first Headhunters Studios new line of resin kits.  These very unique sculptures are unlike anything else on the market.  Original and extremely detailed, these creatures are sure to make any room come alive!'),(1341,5109,'1998-06-07 12:03:01',4330,5108,'treedog',0,'The Forests of Zandaria are home to a variety of unusual species. Among them \nis the rarely seen Zandarian Treedog. The Treedogs main habitat is the highest treetops. They\nare almost never seen on the ground The average weight of a full grown male is roughly 1500\npounds, making it huge for a tree dweller. What makes this possible is the strength of the\nHerculi Trees in which they live. Twice the size of Earth’s largest redwoods. These giants can\neasily hold the weight of even the largest Treedog and his entire clan. The Treedogs live so\nhigh in the trees that the average native Zandarian never sees one. Even when a Treedog dies,\nthe body rarely makes it to ground level. Treetop scavengers take care of everything but the\nbones. True hunters themselves, the average Zandarian Treedog averages 30 kills a day. Bird\nlike creatures and squirrel like creatures makeup the majority of their menu. The unique lower\njaw of the Zandarian Treedog, along with its powerful sense of hearing and sight, is what\nmakes them such effective hunters. The lower jaw splits in a scissor-like action to grasp it\'s\nprey. Once impaled by the huge tusks, there is simply no escape. Quick for it\'s size, the\nTreedog can leap from tree to tree with the agility of a Spider Monkey. Sure to make any\nroom come alive. This species is brought to you in 1/2 scale.'),(1342,5109,'1998-06-07 12:03:29',4329,5108,'darter',0,'At twilight the swamps come alive with a sea of Denjrite eyes darting about, competing for the\nrising microscopic food that grows from the warmth of Aquams two suns. Their chameleon like eyes skim the top of the water keeping watch for enemies from the sky. The hinged outer shell of the Denjrite Darter protects it from most predators and it\'s armadillo-like ability to curl into a ball protects it\'s soft underbelly. The inside of each shelled hinge is lined with gills, making it capable of breathing under water. With a rhythmic waving motion, the Denjrite Darter uses it\'s shells spiked ends as oars. On the power stroke, the shell opens up, increasing the resistance against the water. On the return stroke, the shell bends at the base and lies flat along the sides of the underbelly making it almost a perfectly equipped swimmer. Male Denjrites patrol constantly, relying on their acute vision to detect other interloping males. Territory ownership is decided by a violent fight often resulting in death. Larger Denjrites may over time gain exclusive rights to a small pond. With larger bodies of water, several males may have adjoining territories. Males also have the responsibility of watching over the eggs which incubate within his territory, the bigger your territory the bigger the colony. Thousands of colonies are scattered throughout the Swamp lands of Aquam, the different sects vary slightly in coloration and basic structure. Sure to make any room come alive. This species is brought to you in 1/3 scale.'),(1343,5109,'1998-06-07 12:03:54',4328,5108,'alienus',0,'This insect of the galaxy is known to travel from planet to planet abducting, sampling, and genetically mutating hybrid species of the strangest kind. Often described with an eerie grey skin tone and large black eyes. It’s motives are unknown. Lack of gravity has withered this species body into somewhat of a pencil neck geek. So physically weak are the Allen Greys, that on some planets they must wear mechanical exoskeletons just to get around. This species has become so dependant on it’s mechanical wizardry, that if left stranded, they can not live long on their own. Usually the abductor, this time he\'s the abducted. Brought to you in 1/3 scale and scientifically termed, \"ALIENUS GREYNESS.\"'),(1344,73,'1999-10-13 22:24:32',4332,149,'mst3k',0,'MST3K:TMK depicts the bridge of the Satellite of Love with Mike Nelson steering the ship while Tom Servo, Crow T. Robot and Gypsy express their confidence in his piloting skills by screaming \"WE\'RE ALL GONNA DIE!\"  '),(1347,5118,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4339,5118,'monster',0,NULL),(1348,184,'1998-05-03 21:51:04',4340,184,'pumpknhd',0,'I discovered this model in a local hobby store. It had no name, \nbox, or anything to use as a reference as to where it came from. It is made \nout of solid resin. If anyone has a similar model or has any information \nconcerning it, I would appreciate the information.'),(1349,184,'1998-05-03 21:51:36',4341,184,'conan1',0,'This was a fun model to build. I customized the way Conan holds the \naxe and added a shield to his arm.'),(1350,184,'1998-05-03 21:52:03',4342,184,'ogreking',0,'I purchased this model from a hobby store via mail order. It had no \nname, box, or anything to use as a reference as to where it came from. It is \nmade out of solid resin.'),(1351,184,'1998-05-03 21:52:34',4343,184,'frankie',0,'I purchased this model from a vendor at last year\'s Mad Model Party \nin Pasadena. I customized the neck bolts as the originals were too small in \nproportion to the bust (in my opinion).'),(1352,184,'1998-05-03 21:53:01',4344,184,'freddy',0,'I discovered this model in a hobby store in Edmonton, Canada. The \nsalesman said it had been on the shelf for a very long time and sold it to me \nat a 25% discount. It came in a box with a few letters (Chinese/Japanese \ncharacters) on the outside. A friend translated it for me and it appears to \nsay \"Ghost Factory\". If anyone has a similar model or has any information \nconcerning it, I would appreciate a message. My step-daughter really likes it \nand wants me to make one for her - so I would like to find another kit if one \nis available.'),(1353,5122,'1998-05-04 22:41:07',4345,5122,'frankenberry',0,'I saw a Frankenberry model for sale in Toy Scouts newspaper,\nbut it was $125 and I couldn\'t afford it.  So I got some air drying clay\nand made my own for under $20.'),(1354,282,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4076,282,'pink_cricket',0,NULL),(1355,282,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4076,282,'purple_cricket',0,NULL),(1361,4995,'2011-01-04 07:34:02',4346,4995,'blood',0,'<b><br>note : my email is giuseppe.cico@bcico.com (cannot update here...)<br>Both figures are Verlinden 150mm from the fantasy series.<BR>\r\nThe priestess \"Ursona\" is built just as from box cover, while \"the prisoner\" is modified to be the victim.<BR>\r\nThe cavern is homebuild, with working lights driven by electronic circuits.<BR>\r\nMore pictures can be seen on my web site browsing <A href=http://www.bcico.com/modeling/html/fant_01.htm>here</A>.</b><BR>\r\n<b>(refer to <A href=http://www.bcico.com>http://www.bcico.com</A> for full web site)</b><BR>\r\n'),(1368,4995,'2011-01-04 07:32:53',4347,4995,'cyclecop',0,'<b>note : my email is giuseppe.cico@bcico.com (cannot update here...)<br>Sexy cop is a modified \"the Prisoner\" (Verlinden 150mm).<BR>\r\nMotorcycle is the Yamaha XV1000 Virago by Tamiya (1/12).<BR>\r\nMore pictures can be seen on my web site browsing <A href=http://www.bcico.com/modeling/html/fant_06.htm>here</A>.</b><BR>\r\n<b>(refer to <A href=http://www.bcico.com>http://www.bcico.com</A> for full web site)</b><BR>\r\n'),(1371,5123,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4349,5130,'betty',0,NULL),(1374,5121,'1998-05-13 08:39:59',4350,5121,'cacelvam',0,'Excellent figure to paint.  Artists oils used for entire flesh areas and Humbrol Enamels for the cape and chains.  Gold plated copper wire was used for the bracelets on the left wrist.'),(1380,4887,'1998-05-14 14:15:26',3815,4887,'Bruce',0,'Add 2 metal Dragon to the base and sculpted a Nunchaku for the base too.'),(1381,4931,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4351,4931,'clint',0,NULL),(1388,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4352,4887,'Karen',0,NULL),(1389,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4009,4887,'Flash',0,NULL),(1390,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4353,4887,'Jeannie',0,NULL),(1391,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4354,4887,'Genne',0,NULL),(1392,201,'1999-11-04 08:24:19',4360,201,'joe',0,'My name is Joe - my butt is pink!\n<p>\nMuch thanks to Vance for sculpting this figure for us!'),(1393,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4361,4887,'Ace',0,NULL),(1394,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4362,4887,'BatmanB',0,NULL),(1395,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4363,4887,'CapitainA',0,NULL),(1396,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3544,4887,'Crow',0,NULL),(1397,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4277,4887,'Draco',0,NULL),(1398,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4364,4887,'Gorila',0,NULL),(1399,4887,'1998-05-15 13:14:30',4365,4887,'Holmes',0,'Sculpted an Archet for the violin. And a carpet for the floor'),(1400,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4366,4887,'Submariner',0,NULL),(1401,4887,'1998-05-15 13:31:21',4367,4887,'Lea',0,'chain not include and sculpte the 2 water hole in front'),(1404,5137,'1998-05-17 16:29:41',4369,5137,'boys',0,'Silver award winner at Wonderfest 98.'),(1405,5136,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4368,5136,'sms',0,NULL),(1407,5080,'1998-05-16 19:45:34',4333,5080,'work',0,'The kit was purchased for $125 from villiage comics in N.Y.C. It comes in 4 solid cast resin pieces including a base and nameplate.After cleaning up the kit and priming with floquil grey, I airbrushed it with liqutex and tamiya acryilics, and detailed with humbrol and testors enamels.The axehead was painted with testors buffable stainless steel.The hedgemaze was created with cell foam, woodland scenics Polyfilla, and Turf, and tech star snowflakes.'),(1409,5137,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3484,5137,'judge',0,NULL),(1410,5137,'1998-05-16 21:22:55',4371,5137,'sandman',0,'Horizon spiderman combined with scratchbuilt sandman.Won silver at Wonderfest 98.'),(1411,5137,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4372,5137,'curse',0,NULL),(1413,5112,'1998-05-16 21:55:50',4336,5115,'comstar',0,'This is taken from the back so that you can see the antennas. The gold \'sheets\' in front of them represesent the horizontal and vertical polarizers.'),(1414,5112,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4337,5115,'tdrss',0,NULL),(1415,5112,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4335,5116,'intelsat6a',0,NULL),(1416,5112,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4334,5115,'intelsat4a',0,NULL),(1417,5137,'1998-05-16 22:23:58',4373,5137,'munsters',0,'Diceman Uncle Herman and half of Dicemans Granpa in Electric chair were used for this scene.'),(1418,5137,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3543,5137,'spawn',0,NULL),(1421,138,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4386,138,'lara',0,NULL),(1423,138,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4388,138,'steve',0,NULL),(1424,138,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4385,138,'wisepenny',0,NULL),(1425,5137,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4390,5137,'connery',0,NULL),(1426,4996,'1998-05-19 19:25:53',4391,4996,'battle',0,'This figure placed 2nd in the Sci Fi and Fantasy Figures and Creatures (50mm and smaller) section of the 1998 IPMS Model Expo in Melbourne, Australia. The cast strap on the weapon was replaced with lead foil and a base was constructed from Milliput over plastic forms. '),(1429,268,'1998-05-20 16:29:15',4392,268,'centerfold',0,'I took the pictures of the kit with an Apple Computer digital\ncamera,  then uploaded them to my computer.'),(1430,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3495,4887,'BatmanH',0,NULL),(1431,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4393,4887,'Hercules',0,NULL),(1432,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4394,4887,'Kirk',0,NULL),(1433,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3888,4887,'Penguin',0,NULL),(1434,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4395,4887,'PeterParker',0,NULL),(1435,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4077,4887,'Phantom',0,NULL),(1436,4887,'1998-05-22 13:27:29',4018,4887,'Rambo',0,'Added the necklace.'),(1437,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4396,4887,'Robocop',0,NULL),(1438,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4245,4887,'Spock',0,NULL),(1439,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4397,4887,'Supergirl',0,NULL),(1440,4887,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3521,4887,'Thor',0,NULL),(1441,18,'2004-02-28 10:15:29',4398,282,'http://jamesart.com/venus.html',1,NULL),(1444,346,'1998-05-31 07:29:02',4410,346,'pfil',0,'This kit was originally called Standing Pretty but, the character closely resembled Pfil, an Adult Anime character, from the comic New Bondage Fairies. I used the dremel tool to creat some pointed ears and antennas from resin residue.  The wings were cut from thin sheets of plastic.'),(1445,346,'1998-05-25 20:53:04',4409,346,'hoot',0,'This kit came missing a lot of small pieces and the straps had to be made from cloth.'),(1446,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4405,346,'venusd',0,NULL),(1447,346,'1998-05-31 06:38:47',3867,346,'shampoo3',0,'This kit was found on www.animeplus.com and is made by Musasiya.'),(1450,346,'1998-05-31 07:09:16',3413,346,'madame',0,'This kit was extremely enjoyable to build and by far one of the easiest.  This company knows how to put a kit together. I highly recommend this kit.'),(1451,346,'1998-05-31 06:46:53',4399,346,'chibi',0,'This kit came from G-Port and arrived with two right arms.  I took the dremel tool and switched the fingers and thumb around.  Then with some body puddy managed to make it look like a left hand.'),(1456,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4402,346,'lum',0,NULL),(1457,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4059,346,'batgirl',0,NULL),(1458,346,'1998-05-31 07:22:51',4384,346,'wrapped',0,'This is another kit from Moir which came directly from Japan.  The kit was extremely easy with the head, body and two bows.'),(1459,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4382,346,'sophia',0,NULL),(1460,346,'1998-05-31 07:02:53',4381,346,'slavem',0,'This kit was ordered through Rainbow Sportscards and Collectables here in Sioux City, Iowa. Alot of these kits come directly from Japan with no names of the companies on the box or with the name written in Japanese.'),(1461,346,'1998-05-31 06:49:54',4380,346,'sailormars',0,'This G-Port product was the easiest I\'ve ever found. Only 4 easy pieces and then just a pleasure to paint.'),(1462,346,'1998-05-31 06:56:33',4379,346,'sailorb',0,'These G-Port kits were the most challenging ever.  It was unusual to have so many pieces that didn\'t match up correctly. Sailor Moon, Mars, and Venus were the hardest when it came to their hair.  It required alot of body puddy and sanding but, the final results were worth the effort. Long live Sailor Moon and the Sailor Scouts.'),(1463,346,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4376,346,'akaneonice',0,NULL),(1464,296,'1998-05-26 13:50:36',4413,296,'cobra',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1465,296,'1998-05-26 13:39:16',3530,296,'wolverin',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1466,296,'1998-05-26 13:51:14',4415,296,'kaneda',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1467,296,'1998-05-26 13:28:20',3484,296,'janderso',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1468,296,'1998-05-26 13:29:12',3485,296,'jdredd',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1469,296,'1998-05-26 13:28:46',4416,296,'jdeath',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1470,296,'1998-05-26 13:23:18',3277,296,'decap',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1471,296,'1998-05-26 13:51:46',4417,296,'spiritli',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1472,296,'1998-05-26 13:46:52',3920,296,'cylena',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1473,296,'1998-05-26 13:40:31',3579,296,'guin',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1474,296,'1998-05-26 13:48:59',4418,296,'sengir',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1475,296,'1998-05-26 13:30:34',3500,296,'cyclops',0,'Please visit my personal site, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1477,5171,'1998-06-07 21:25:22',4311,5171,'c3po',0,'Painted with airbrush using Badger Air-Opaque pigments.'),(1481,138,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4387,149,'missivy',0,NULL),(1482,138,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4424,149,'dirtyharry',0,NULL),(1483,5177,'1998-06-08 22:48:24',4425,5178,'gorilla',0,'A 31\" tall mountain gorilla called Silverback!'),(1484,5177,'1998-06-08 22:47:30',4426,5179,'ashlyn',0,'A quarter scale kit of adult film star Ashlyn Gere.'),(1486,5182,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4427,5182,'bro',0,NULL),(1488,5182,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4429,5182,'Cam',0,NULL),(1489,5182,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4430,5182,'fau',0,NULL),(1491,5182,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4431,5182,'Gan',0,NULL),(1492,5182,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4433,5182,'Lum',0,NULL),(1493,5182,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3423,5182,'Gil',0,NULL),(1495,5182,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3972,5182,'Nic',0,NULL),(1496,4867,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4436,4867,'south_park',0,NULL),(1497,4867,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4435,4867,'daredevil',0,NULL),(1498,4867,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4360,4867,'gremlin',0,NULL),(1499,5067,'1998-06-24 01:29:42',4437,5067,'prisoner',0,' The kit comes in 3 pieces, body, head and base. The body had a minimal seam line and not a single air bubble, but it has visible brush strokes from when the sculpture was brushed down and I had to get rid of Mike Hills signature that was hidden in his crotch, otherwise very clean casting. The head was a different story altogether! The hair was riddled with pin holes, and there was a moderate seam up the side. I tried as hard as I could to find a round wooden base that I could stain and attach to the bottom of the resin base, to make it look more finished, but everything that I found was just not big enough. But it was a gift for my dad, he loved it, so I guess that\'s all that matters.   '),(1500,5188,'1998-06-26 10:59:27',4438,5188,'MonKing',0,'This is my second try on super sculpey.'),(1508,4848,'1998-06-26 13:54:11',4439,348,'cedrick',0,'Cedrick The Zombie is the completion of the trilogy.\nHe has a similar yet different base to Alex and Boris. The kit is 13\" tall\nand comes complete with certificate  of authenticity, metal name plate and\nassembly instructions.'),(1510,5132,'1999-06-19 23:19:43',4444,5132,'Cera',0,'A composite ceratopsian style Mechanosaur. Made from multiple materials, approx. one foot long'),(1511,5132,'1998-07-10 14:13:24',4443,5132,'diatryma',0,'A giant prehistoric flightless bird that lived about 50 million years ago.'),(1512,5078,'1998-07-04 20:09:37',4440,5078,'g62hl',0,'This is one of four Godzilla busts released in Japan by Kyosho.\nThis kit represents the 1962 \"King Kong vs Godzilla\" version and features an iceburg background (that\'s how I interpreted it anyway) and metal name plate.\nThe kit is approximately 12 inches tall. To see more of my Godzilla collection visit my <a href=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\">Godzilla Room</a> .  '),(1515,5187,'1998-07-07 00:27:17',4441,301,'Cindy',0,'Cindy: the Vampire. She\'s beautiful, She bad, She doesn\'t get out in daylight much and she\'ll drink your blood. She\'s Cindy the Vampire. Cindy is approximately 12\" tall, cast in white resin and includes a base with a groovy gothic cross. She\'s perfect for display with any of your other ghoulish creatures but don\'t turn your back on her when she\'s hungry or you might find yourself a pint short. \nVital Stats:\n 12\" tall \n Cast in high quality white resin \n Includes base and Cross \n'),(1516,4931,'2000-04-27 18:44:32',4442,5439,'moreau',0,'6\" x 7\" resin bust.  Limited to 100 castings.  Officially licenced by New Line Cinema.<BR>\nNEW APRIL 2000:  Only 10 kits remain!  Get yours today!'),(1518,205,'1998-07-13 08:37:32',4446,205,'relic',0,'This is \"Kuthoga\" From \"The Relic\"\nit\'s hangin on a wall as it should be\n- not walking as shown on the box.\nI added real hair for the mane and whiskers\nusing the cinefex article on the movie as reference.'),(1519,5198,'1998-07-14 20:02:55',4445,5198,'trooper1',0,'Backpack and shoulder gear scratchbuilt.  Painted with Tamiya Acrylics and drybrushed with pastels, enamels and oils.  Arms modified to more relaxed position.  For more pics, check out http://bigfoot.com/~michael_tay'),(1527,5201,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4448,5251,'abe',0,NULL),(1531,4824,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4450,5147,'slaine',0,NULL),(1533,5203,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3484,5203,'JudgeAnderson',0,NULL),(1535,5203,'1998-07-18 10:09:14',3752,5203,'AlexTheVampire',0,'This is one of my favorite kits I ever worked on.  It was very clean, easy to assemble and a blast to paint.  I airbrushed \"Alex\" with acrylics and deepened some of the shadow areas witw watercolor washes.'),(1536,5203,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4451,5203,'Iria',0,NULL),(1543,5203,'1998-07-19 07:43:53',3516,5203,'Spiderman',0,'Although I don\'t care for using liquid masking when airbrushing a kit, some times it just has to be done.  The kit was airbrushed with acrylics and the webbing was painstakingly hand brushed in.  This kit one first place in the \"comic book\" catergory at the Orlando \"Monster Modelfest\" in Feb. 1998. '),(1545,5203,'1998-07-20 10:19:05',3494,5203,'Batman',0,'With the exception of his face and the bat logo the entire kit was airbrushed.'),(1546,5203,'1998-07-20 10:26:56',3746,5203,'WrightsonsFrankie',0,'This kit is a major project, I had some difficulties with the assembly of this monster kit, but once it was all together it is one nice looking piece to add to a collection.'),(1547,5203,'1998-07-20 10:31:29',3613,5203,'Devilman',0,'The base for this kit was made out of expanding foam. Anthony Mestas describes the proess in his excellent article \"Making The Scene\" in issue #9 of AFM.'),(1548,5203,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3544,5203,'TheCrow',0,NULL),(1549,5203,'1998-07-20 10:37:25',3504,5203,'Frankenstein',0,'This was the first kit that I ever did. I got the bug hard from here on out.'),(1555,5207,'1998-07-20 12:17:29',4452,5207,'misa',0,'I completed this kit in August of 1996.  The painting was done with Testors Enamel, Pactra Water Based Enamel, and Ral Partha Water Based Paint.  The Stand is Stained Glass on a wood base.'),(1557,5207,'1998-07-20 18:31:52',4454,5207,'ohmu',0,'I completed this model around January of 1997.  The painting was done with Testors Enamel and Pactra Water Based Enamel.  The kit was molded poorly and inaccurately, so I had to greatly modify the Ohmu to make it and its wounds accurate to the movie.  I also had to invent a new color for its shell.'),(1562,5203,'1998-07-21 10:29:20',4070,5203,'CyberNinja',0,'  This was the first kit I ever did by Max Factory. If you have never built a Max Factory kit, I highly reccomend them to\n          you. There castings are fantastic, they do have a lot of parts, but if you take your time on the trimming they go together\n          needing almost no putty work.'),(1563,5198,'1998-07-23 22:01:43',3739,5198,'yoda',0,'built out of the box.  For more pics, goto http://bigfoot.com/~michael_tay'),(1564,5198,'1998-07-23 22:14:00',3553,5198,'boba',0,'Out of the box.  This kit is great!!  very accurate and highly recommended.  For more pics, go to http://bigfoot.com/~michael_tay'),(1565,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3317,193,'ol01',0,NULL),(1566,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3337,193,'ol02',0,NULL),(1567,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3374,193,'ol03',0,NULL),(1568,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3338,193,'ol04',0,NULL),(1569,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4455,193,'ol05',0,NULL),(1570,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3325,193,'ol06',0,NULL),(1571,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3406,193,'ol07',0,NULL),(1572,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4456,193,'ol08',0,NULL),(1573,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3315,193,'ol09',0,NULL),(1574,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4457,193,'ol10',0,NULL),(1575,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4458,193,'ol11',0,NULL),(1576,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4459,193,'ol12',0,NULL),(1577,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3380,193,'ol13',0,NULL),(1578,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4460,193,'ol14',0,NULL),(1579,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3352,193,'ol15',0,NULL),(1580,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3403,193,'ol16',0,NULL),(1581,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4461,193,'ol17',0,NULL),(1582,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4462,193,'ol18',0,NULL),(1583,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4463,193,'ol19',0,NULL),(1584,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4464,193,'ol20',0,NULL),(1585,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4465,193,'ol21',0,NULL),(1586,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4466,193,'ol22',0,NULL),(1587,40,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4467,193,'ol23',0,NULL),(1589,5187,'1998-08-08 08:56:42',4468,301,'nosferatu',0,'NEW! Nosferatu is here, sculpted by Master Sculptor Randy Lambert, the same man that brought you the Midget Monsters now brings you the first in this new line of goulish creations from Screamin\' Lemur Models. Horror characters from Classic Literature and Film!  The Base is 8\" tall, The figure is 4 1/2\"  The kit comes in three pieces and is cast in white resin with very few bubbles.'),(1592,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4469,4940,'alia',0,NULL),(1593,296,'1998-08-10 10:13:21',4470,296,'aries',0,'Drop by my site see the rest of my work and comments on how I did it.  \nhttp://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1594,296,'1998-08-16 13:15:49',4471,296,'dare',0,'Drop by my site see the rest of my work and comments on how I did it.  \nhttp://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1595,296,'1998-08-10 10:15:46',4160,296,'temp',0,'Drop by my site see the rest of my work and comments on how I did it.  \nhttp://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1596,296,'1998-08-10 10:18:36',3423,296,'guil',0,'Drop by my site see the rest of my work and comments on how I did it.  \nhttp://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1597,296,'1998-08-10 10:20:50',3664,296,'moon',0,'Drop by my site see the rest of my work and comments on how I did it.  \nhttp://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/'),(1598,5203,'1998-08-17 10:06:55',3954,5203,'GreenGoblin',0,'This kit along with the \"Spiderman\" kit are in my opinion Horizon\'s two best kits based off Marvel characters.  There are quite a few pieces to this kit, whick looks a little bit intimidating at first, but actually this kit went together very easily. I highly recommend this kit to any Marvel Comics fan.'),(1599,5203,'1998-08-17 09:54:46',3506,5203,'TheHulk',0,'This is the second kit that I ever did (it is a great kit for beginners). The muscle texture was really fun to airbrush, I used a lot of different transparent colors in the shadow area. One aspect of the paint job that I am very unhappy with is the colors on the face are more intense then the rest of the body. I keep thinking about repainting this kit but so far I haven\'t had the time for it.'),(1600,5203,'1998-08-17 09:58:44',3451,5203,'Locutus',0,'On this kit I base coated the entire kit with flat black, I then added all the color and shading on his uniform with pastels. After that I drybrushed in all the metalics. Lastly all the skin tones were painted in with oils.'),(1601,5203,'1998-08-17 10:02:39',3759,5203,'Guy',0,'Guy was painted with airbrushed acrylics, and his partner Raina was finshed with oils.'),(1603,4940,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4474,4940,'Lara',0,NULL),(1604,5164,'1998-09-29 13:53:01',4476,5164,'tankgirl',0,'This kit was an exclusive from the Film and TV Model Club in England and is no longer availiable.'),(1606,5189,'1998-09-06 19:34:13',4479,5189,'endo',0,'Highly detailed and chrome-plated parts produce a very realistic look.'),(1608,5240,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4482,5255,'spk',0,NULL),(1609,5240,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4480,5255,'qt',0,NULL),(1611,5201,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4473,5251,'molluck',0,NULL),(1613,5241,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4483,5241,'Milesdragon',0,NULL),(1616,5201,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4472,5251,'arnie',0,NULL),(1617,204,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4485,204,'Dracbat',0,NULL),(1618,5237,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4488,5237,'DOGBURSTER',0,NULL),(1619,5215,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4487,5215,'belldandy',0,NULL),(1620,5215,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4245,5215,'AmbassadorSpock',0,NULL),(1622,5256,'1998-09-13 13:10:34',4489,5256,'Karnsten',0,'Excellent cleavage Mike!'),(1630,5235,'1999-05-05 23:44:09',4490,5261,'MrSmith',0,'This kit is huge! Weighs in at 10 pounds of solid resin. Stands almost a foot tall and wide. Kit comes with certificate, reference photo, full color box art. What a deal! Shipping is included'),(1636,5237,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3476,5237,'Alien2',0,NULL),(1637,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3884,5270,'saucermen',0,NULL),(1639,354,'1998-09-15 17:09:34',4492,5271,'tspred',0,'1/3rd scale Pred