is titled \"Mary Ann\" and is $45.00.'),(1697,5102,'1998-09-20 19:12:30',4348,5128,'n-138',0,'310-391-3052. N-138 is actually titled Tracy and is $35.00'),(1698,5102,'1998-09-20 19:19:22',4348,5128,'N-149',0,'310-391-3052. N-149 is actually titled \"Wendy\" and is $40.00.'),(1702,5206,'1998-09-21 07:11:01',4449,5206,'mhulk',0,'Special thanks to Marc Liljegren of Internet Business Solutions for assistance with the photo graphics.'),(1703,4864,'1999-03-12 13:14:07',4522,4864,'ymir',0,'Added plastic 1/35 soldiers and glass eyes.'),(1704,4864,'1998-09-21 08:19:37',4521,4864,'godzilla',0,'Airbrushed cotton flames on base bought at Wonderfest\'96.'),(1705,4864,'1999-04-30 12:39:07',4520,4864,'cyclops',0,'Added fur to Cyclops and rocks to base.\nThe base is from Mad Labs.'),(1706,4864,'2006-06-09 12:56:53',4519,4864,'cftbl',0,'visit my site\r\nwww.monsterjones.com'),(1707,4864,'2000-08-29 10:12:13',4518,4864,'bigswing',0,'Fur was added to Kong. Small pagoda added to base. Won First Place AlamoFiesta show and Bronze at Wonderfest 1998.'),(1708,5237,'1998-09-21 15:59:28',4525,5237,'Spider',0,'Resin with pewter legs\nMade by Grendel UK'),(1709,5237,'1998-09-21 16:00:19',4524,5237,'Gladiator',0,'Verlinden 120mm '),(1710,5237,'1998-09-21 16:01:10',4523,5237,'PWH',0,'Almond Sculptures 90mm scale '),(1711,5237,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3472,5237,'Terronious',0,NULL),(1712,5237,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3470,5237,'FG',0,NULL),(1713,5237,'1998-09-21 16:07:07',4526,5237,'FemailVampire',0,'Creative Castings UK'),(1714,5237,'1999-01-09 21:09:46',4528,5237,'RLH',0,'Herts Models 120mm \nDeleted'),(1715,5241,'1998-09-21 20:31:09',4527,5241,'MILESOBIE',0,'The Willis Harold \"Obie\" O\'Brien life cast\nmemoriam piece was created from a partial \nfacial casting made of Mr. O\'Brien apparently\nin the 1940\'s. The complete kit comes in three\npieces. The resin lifecast is prepainted\nin a bronze finish, the oak stained and laquered\ndisplay plaque, and the custom engraved\nbrass nameplate. This piece is limited to\n100 sets and sells for $150.00 AND $5.00\nfor shipping and handling. 50% of the proceeds\nfor this piece is being donated to the L.A.\nMotion Picture Hospital in the names of \nWillis and Darlyne O\'Brien.'),(1716,5241,'1998-09-22 14:20:29',4529,5241,'MILESEARTH',0,' This piece was created from one of the original\n3\" stop-motion saucers from the movie. When assembled the disks of the saucer spin and rotate just like the ones in the movie. It comes\nendorsed by Ray Harryhausen and licensed through\nColumbia Pictures. The price is $75.00 each plus\n$5.00 for shipping and is available for immediate\nshipping.'),(1717,5241,'1998-09-22 14:41:19',4530,5241,'MilesBeetleman',0,' This piece was created from original 1:1\nscale photo\'s taken in 1979 at the great stop-motion\nand special effects company C.P.C. Associates at which\ntime the original puppet was being restored and animated\nfor a simulator ride project entitled\n\"Space Ride\". The sculpting of this piece was painstakingly\nrecreated over a 2 year period of time by master sculptor Kevin Thomas\nand supervised by Hal Miles. Each kit sells for $100.00 and $5.00 for shipping\nand handling and is available for immediate shipping. The license is pending\nthrough Howard Ziehm.'),(1719,5241,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4531,5241,'MilesJoe',0,NULL),(1720,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4532,5270,'wolf',0,NULL),(1721,5277,'1998-09-30 09:08:57',4533,5277,'BirthOfaLegend',0,'Airbrush acrylics for the figure, drybrush acrylics for base, drybrush acrylics and pastels for the statue, and auto lacquer for the marble gloss on the base'),(1723,5277,'1998-10-01 02:37:15',4534,5277,'DarkKnight',0,'The model is counter-shaded, that is dark on top and light on bottom, like the 2nd edition cover of Miller\'s graphic novel. It\'s also lit from the bottom and the background is run through Photoshop.\nFigure is airbrushed in acrylics. Base has pastels for weathering.'),(1724,5277,'1998-10-09 02:22:56',4535,5277,'Storm',0,'I couldn\'t use the terrible hair piece that comes with the kit so I sculpted this cropped look with Milliput instead. I also found an alternative \"look\" in one of my son\'s comics. I used an airbrushed Dioxazine Purple & Black mix for the body. A new belt and earrings were made from some lead strip from a wine bottle. I Photoshopped out the horrible cartoon base, which is still present in reality because my daughter likes it.'),(1725,5277,'1998-10-01 05:31:37',4536,5277,'SilverSurfer',0,'It takes quite a bit of Milliput and sanding to get this kit streamlined, but I think I makes a very dynamic kit. Difficult to photograph because of all the reflections, which give it a tint. Kit is sprayed with Auto Acrylic Chrome spray and washed with black acrylic.'),(1726,5235,'1999-05-05 23:37:23',4490,5261,'PsychoWolf',0,'Production Design from film \"Hollow\" which the Mr. Smith character is from'),(1727,5277,'1998-10-02 04:09:39',3664,5277,'DonalsMoonsinger',0,'OK, so I Photoshopped & reversed the image to make it different. Airbrushed acrylics, drybrushed, washed, then drybrushed again in about 12 layers.'),(1728,5277,'1998-10-09 02:20:22',4538,5277,'Batsandcats',0,'54mm white metal Grenadier comic Batman, \"ears\" slightly changed, acrylics. Catwoman is a re-painted ERTL movie die-cast toy.'),(1729,5277,'1998-10-02 04:17:18',4539,5277,'Alf',0,'Converted from a plastic keyring. Sofa is Das Promo. I\'d like to add a Doll\'s House TV sometime. Scale\'s about 90mm'),(1730,5276,'1998-10-03 19:06:06',4540,5276,'newsupes',0,'Even though I didn\'t care for this version\nof the \"Man of Tommorow\", I was compelled\nto add this to all the other renditions\nin my collection.  Painting is straightforward\nbrushed acrylic.'),(1733,5276,'2000-02-27 22:16:58',4541,5276,'kcsuper',0,'Couldn\'t miss this excellent repaint opportunity!\nRoss\'s sculpting is superb.  Hope this pleases the\nfanboys who wanted a \"realistic\" approach to this\nwonderful figure. Removing the cape for painting \nwas the tough part. Now all I say each time I look\nat this is: WOW!  This is a must have!\nHave more pics at:\nhttp://alpinetek.netfirms.com/statues/kingdom.htm\n'),(1734,5203,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4546,5203,'TimeTraveller',0,NULL),(1735,5203,'1998-10-05 21:44:05',4545,5203,'FemaleCenobite',0,'All of the skin tones on this kit were painted with oils.  All other blending was done with artist pastels over a black base.'),(1736,5203,'1998-10-05 21:47:16',4544,5203,'Supergirl',0,'I really liked the design of this kit. The sculpting on the body was done perfect, although the hands and face were rather crude.  All of the painting was done with airbrushed acrylics.'),(1740,5206,'1998-10-14 10:28:36',4447,5206,'judge1',0,'Special thanks to Marc Liljegren of Internet Business Solutions for assisting with the photo montage.  The diorama is titled: Tagitus Interruptus'),(1742,5279,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4547,5279,'sandplane',0,NULL),(1743,4995,'2011-01-04 07:36:02',4550,4995,'angelina',0,'<b>note : my email is giuseppe.cico@bcico.com (cannot update here...)<br>More <A href=http://www.bcico.com/modeling/html/fant_12.htm TARGET=\"_window\">pictures</A> and a <A href=http://www.bcico.com/modeling/step_by_step.htm TARGET=\"_window\">\"step-by-step\"</A> on my web site.</b><BR>\r\n<b>(refer to <A href=http://www.bcico.com>http://www.bcico.com</A> for full web site)</b><BR>\r\n'),(1744,5237,'1998-10-16 08:37:36',4551,5237,'IGUANA',0,'Sculpted and cast by Oswaldo Merchor a Wildlife Artist\nVery limited and very expensive but the detail is phenomenal'),(1745,5237,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3978,5237,'BARB',0,NULL),(1747,5237,'1998-10-16 09:00:53',4553,5237,'EL',0,'Andrea Miniatures 54mm kit'),(1749,5201,'1998-11-29 01:50:23',4554,5251,'pinhead',0,'\"He\'ll tear your soul apart\"'),(1752,296,'1998-11-13 20:41:50',4555,296,'sm99',0,'Please visit my website, Doc Roc\'s Valley of the Supermodels at http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Dimension/8075/.'),(1753,296,'1998-11-13 20:42:21',3515,296,'shulk',