ption to use the 1992 style head (on the 1954 style body, I went with the \'54). To see more of my collection visit <a href=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\"> The Godzilla Room </a>.'),(1777,5078,'1998-11-29 20:04:32',4567,5078,'64b',0,'I added a demolished N-scale building and rubble for the base. To see more of my collection please visit <a href=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\"> The Godzilla Room </a>.  '),(1778,5078,'1998-11-30 20:22:21',4568,5078,'gam',0,'This kit is part of Bandai\'s Kaiju Series. To see more of my collection please visit <a href=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\"> The Godzilla Room </a>'),(1779,5278,'1998-12-06 17:05:31',3442,5278,'rei',0,'This was my first resin kit done mostly with an airbrush. The kit is very well formed and fun to put together.'),(1780,5278,'1998-12-02 17:06:43',3442,5306,'rei',0,'This kit was mostly done with an airbrush.'),(1781,5278,'1998-12-02 18:37:05',4570,5306,'Jup',0,'This is my very first resin kit I did. It was done all by hand brush.'),(1782,5278,'1998-12-05 18:17:27',4573,5306,'reichan',0,'This kit was a little tricky to built. Took alot of sanding and filling where the legs meet the body.'),(1784,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3500,5270,'cyclops',0,NULL),(1786,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3515,5270,'she',0,NULL),(1787,5270,'1998-12-11 14:55:40',3245,5270,'munsters',0,'This is the Polar Lights re-issue '),(1788,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4574,5270,'mars',0,NULL),(1789,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3544,5270,'crow',0,NULL),(1790,5270,'1998-12-12 05:07:23',4575,5270,'herman',0,' Kit produced by Diceman Creations'),(1791,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3453,5270,'medusa',0,NULL),(1793,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4108,5270,'back',0,NULL),(1794,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4245,5270,'spock',0,NULL),(1795,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4485,5270,'bat',0,NULL),(1796,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4576,5270,'flash',0,NULL),(1797,5203,'1998-12-14 22:41:01',4208,5203,'GeometricAlien',0,'Another fantastic kit from Geometric Design.'),(1798,5203,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3512,5203,'Raptor',0,NULL),(1799,5203,'1998-12-14 22:47:57',4577,5203,'GeometricPhantomBust',0,'Geometric Designs line of bust are exceptional.  My personal favorite is this Lon Chaney Phantom Of the Opera.  The only work required before painting was sanding some very minor seem lines and filling a couple of air holes.  I painted the entire kit with oil paints.'),(1800,5203,'1998-12-14 22:54:08',3561,5203,'Gremlin',0,'This has got to be one of the finest kits available to our hobby.  Steve Wang did a fantastic job capturing all the detail on this little monster.  Everything on this kit was airbrushed freehand, except for the eyes which were painted with a round sable brush.'),(1801,5203,'1998-12-14 23:06:37',4578,5203,'FrankensteinBust',0,'Another great bust from Geometric Design.  I spent about an hour sanding and filling this kit before I painted it using acrylics, watercolors and pastels.'),(1802,5203,'1998-12-14 23:34:22',4579,5203,'HorizonVelociraptor',0,'Chistopher Darga\'s sculpting on this kit is IMHO perfect.  Although there is quite a few pieces on this model, it was very simple to put together.  I filled the leg with plaster and ran a steal rod through it, but I was still unable to get it to stand on its own.  Entire piece was airbrushed with acrylics.'),(1803,5270,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3953,5270,'woof',0,NULL),(1805,5237,'1999-01-09 20:57:47',4583,5237,'AQN',0,'This is supplied as a comlleted item with a lamentable paint job\nSo i added to the base so it doesn\'t look like a cow pat\nand repainted it '),(1806,5237,'1999-01-09 20:45:49',4582,5237,'Dentist',0,'This was a Ral Partha conversion I made\nfor a very good client of mine as a Christmas present'),(1807,5237,'1999-01-09 20:51:33',4580,5237,'AH',0,'Original by Jay-Dee.\nI\'ve added the bulkhead wall which was made from 2mm acrylic sheet stretched \nand burnt through with a blow torch. The slobber is made from the same stuff\nwith epoxy dribbled over it as it hardened'),(1808,5237,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4057,5237,'GA',0,NULL),(1810,5237,'1999-01-24 20:01:02',4584,5237,'BOGMONSTER',0,'Creative Castings Kit\nAka \"Close Encounters of the Turd Kind\"\n\n'),(1811,4864,'2006-06-09 12:54:38',4592,4864,'CreaVJul',0,'Horizon Creature with Lunar Model\'s Julie Adams base. Used railroad EZ water on base.\r\nThis buildup won Best of Show - Figures , at the Austin Scale\r\nModel Show 2000.\r\nvisit www.monsterjones.com'),(1815,4864,'1999-03-11 14:26:40',4593,4864,'GodzvKG',0,'Incredible kit to build. Base scratch built with Doyusha buildings\nadded and destroyed. My build-up here won 1st place\nat 1999 Modelfiesta, TX'),(1816,4864,'1999-01-30 20:34:12',4594,4864,'DancingG2',0,'This kit by Japan\'s M-1 is from the movie\n\"Monster Zero\". This is Godzilla\'s victory dance\nafter beating King Ghidora in a fight on planet X. Wahoo!'),(1817,4864,'1999-03-11 14:25:19',4595,4864,'medusa',0,'classic mythological creature\nHarryhausen style.Model was repsitioned with a straighter back.\n Figure won 1st place at 1997 Modelfiesta Texas'),(1818,4864,'1999-03-11 13:29:05',4596,4864,'frankst',0,'Billiken Frankenstein with skull and\nsolder used for bolts on neck. Dimensional Designs\ndoor on base'),(1820,4864,'1999-01-31 07:55:13',4597,4864,'guyver',0,'Max Factory Guyver from movie of same name\nsculpted by the great Steve Wang. Base was custom made by Javier Rios'),(1821,4864,'1999-01-31 07:40:56',4065,4864,'talos',0,'Geometric\'s unofficially released Talos\nfrom \"Jason and the Argonauts\". Base was scratch built with N scale Argonauts in \nscratchbuilt Super Sculpty Argo. I used railroad EZ water on base and toothpics for oars. Rocks are Magic Sculpt.'),(1823,4940,'1999-02-21 09:56:20',4599,4940,'horny',0,'This is my first figure sculpture, it\'s the Horned Reaper hunting for an Imp. Both characters belong to Bullfrog\'s Dungeon Keeper PC game.\nPlease visit my homepage to view some more images of my Horned Reaper sculpture.\nhttp://members.aol.com/brunneng2/index.html'),(1824,5316,'1999-03-10 23:53:53',4602,5224,'thor',0,'Thor is DarkStorm Studios\' first model kit.  Please feel free to visit our website, www.darkstormstudios.com to see the complete Thor gallery as well as all the exciting and new model kit releases for 1999.'),(1825,5316,'1999-03-10 18:24:08',4603,5224,'fantazia',0,'Fantazia is DarkStorm Studios\' second model kit.  Please feel free to visit our website, www.darkstormstudios.com to see the complete Fantazia gallery as well as all the exciting and new model kit releases for 1999.'),(1826,4953,'1999-03-11 08:30:57',4604,4953,'burns',0,'This is a kits of Mr. Burns from the tv show, The Simpsons, as Old Dracula from thier Halloween special'),(1831,4864,'1999-03-12 20:36:35',4606,4864,'SinbadVsKali',0,'From the film \"Golden Voyage of Sinbad\", Kali was\nbrought to life by Ray Harryhausen. Base was extended with added containers and temple well.'),(1833,5354,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4609,5354,'Hawkgirl',0,NULL),(1834,5237,'1999-03-15 10:24:00',4610,5237,'FIN',0,'A reworked Phantom kit '),(1835,5237,'1999-03-15 10:29:19',4611,5237,'DOMINIQUE',0,'Artistic License kit\nhttp://www.members.home.net/garagekit/kits.htm\nthanks to Tony Spangler for swapping it for a Dawn kit'),(1839,280,'1999-03-17 19:43:47',4612,280,'Desire',0,'KIt was suppost to be in a clear acrylic tube. I decided to made a \"new\" base and give it a Satanonic look,'),(1843,5363,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4613,5363,'Crow',0,NULL),(1845,280,'1999-03-18 07:05:37',4614,280,'Kongvrex',0,'One of the last of the original casts of this kit and it showed. I lot of cleanup was required, but painting it was worth the effort.'),(1846,4864,'1999-03-19 20:27:44',4615,4864,'SinbadVskel',0,'I bought these two figures separately from a show and Hogan\'s Bones.\nBase was scratchbuilt with balsa steps on cardboard cylinder and covered\nwith bondo. Skeleton had to be pinned to base. This is my favorite movie!'),(1849,4864,'1999-03-20 09:10:31',4618,4864,'BurgerKingGodzi',0,'Elvis aka \"The Burger King\" tempts Kayiodo\'s 1955 Godzilla.\nSort of a East meets West thing.'),(1851,4864,'1999-03-20 09:09:06',4619,4864,'BGhidra',0,'A great plastic kit a King Ghidrah - Godzilla\'s main foe.\nThis kit is 1/350 scale, I think and comes with a small\nPlanet X figure'),(1852,5344,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4323,5369,'Chan2',0,NULL),(1853,5344,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4621,5369,'Mars1',0,NULL),(1854,280,'1999-03-21 06:29:13',4622,280,'BarbarellaFF',0,'Probably the best rendition of Jane Fonda as Barbarella ever done in resin.'),(1855,280,'1999-03-21 08:51:30',4623,280,'AlieninStatis',0,'A small but nicely detailed model of the \"Alien Queen Fetus\" that I felt should be kept in a jar.'),(1856,280,'1999-03-25 22:51:52',4635,280,'Queen2',0,'A very nice little kit that I got from Jim Stelling, because we both agree that she\'s the most beautiful actress ever.'),(1857,5363,'1999-03-21 09:22:47',4625,5367,'Slaine',0,'This kit is perfection. The material is one of the finest I\'ve used.\nEverything about it says quality so I would try to get one now as it is a limited run peice. The painting guide is excellent to...especially if you think that tartan looks daunting.\nLee Ames has definatley got his act together.\n(p.s.  it costs £75 not $)'),(1858,5363,'1999-03-21 09:43:21',4626,5367,'Speeder',0,'This is a stunning kit. The Biker Scout Armour really shows itself off against the used look speeder.\nA bit of work had to be done to the arms so there were\'nt gaps but for the price it\'s madness not to buy one!'),(1859,5344,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4627,5369,'Chat',0,NULL),(1860,5344,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4308,5369,'Jason',0,NULL),(1861,5344,'1999-11-30 21:37:16',4520,5369,'Cyclops',0,'Feel free to visit my webpage @\nhttp://home.swbell.net/barkley5'),(1863,5368,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4630,5373,'group',0,NULL),(1865,5368,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4631,5373,'variation',0,NULL),(1866,280,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4624,280,'Iria1',0,NULL),(1867,5323,'1999-03-25 06:26:46',4633,5323,'BUMBLE',0,'The Bumble was completely handbrushed with artist\nacrylics. The key to making this kit look\n\"right\" was the correct placement of\nthe Bumble\'s slighty crossed irises. '),(1868,5323,'1999-03-25 08:18:30',4634,5323,'FRANK',0,'Restored 1964 Aurora Frankenstien was\nhand-brushed entirely with artist acrylics. This kit is probably still the largest\nselling figural/horror model kit of all time.\nThe face is an interesting cross of a Karloff/Strange likeness\n(I\'d say about 70:30% ). Not for the purist, but still a classic.\n '),(1869,5323,'1999-03-25 10:29:28',4629,5323,'CYCLO',0,'Seams were left unfilled to allow for posability\nwith a diorama (picture update coming soon). Cylops was entirely hand-brushed\nwith artist acrylics. A classic Ray Harryhausen monster and film.\n'),(1873,5119,'2002-10-16 09:07:26',4639,6489,'berns',0,'This is a new release from Critical Mass.  Mr Berns as Count Dracula on the Simpson?s Halloween Special.  It is a 3 piece kit with a roto-cast body. Total height of 6\"'),(1874,5350,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4640,5350,'EgyptianGoddess',0,NULL),(1875,5350,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4637,5350,'GargoyleWithCat',0,NULL),(1876,5350,'2002-06-24 18:39:49',4644,5350,'Cleopatra',0,'Large image below shows optional LION STATUES, WHICH ARE SOLD SEPERATLY.\r\n\r\n'),(1881,5201,'1999-03-31 02:44:39',4641,5251,'largepred',0,'Kit comes coplete with wooden head spines and seperate teeth, the kit was painted with Humbrol flat enamels and finished with glass eyes'),(1882,5363,'1999-04-01 09:18:44',4645,5367,'bruce',0,'I searched high & low for a decent look alike of Bruce, in the end this Deformed model from Comet Minatures was the best I found.\nThere are no instructions with it or painting guide and only a line drawing to go by. Good luck with the nunchukas (patience required).\nThanks to Colin (work mate) for all the help with scans.'),(1883,5336,'1999-04-06 15:21:40',4646,5336,'WAR',0,'This is my first try at a bust. I painted this great peice with Badger Freak-Flex paints and a Aztec Airbrush. The gun, chain  and shoulder spikes are cast metal polished with a dremel tool.'),(1889,5363,'1999-04-07 12:45:51',4647,5367,'leon',0,'Another wonderful casting from Lee Ames. Anybody who has not tried one of his kits before should because the material is a joy to work with. The glasses were tricky with not enough wire to do the job, but it\'s amazing what you can do with a paper clip.\nThanks again to Colin for scanning the photos.'),(1890,5363,'1999-04-07 12:55:31',4648,5367,'pam',0,'This is supposed to be Pamela Anderson, although I thought the face looked more like Rene Russo. It was riddled with holes, so patience is required. If you want one Comet Minatures is the place.'),(1891,5363,'1999-04-08 10:18:16',4649,5367,'arnie',0,'For the price this was a must...and I thought it was a good likeness.'),(1892,5363,'1999-04-08 10:25:34',4650,5367,'mech',0,'Everybody should try one of these kits. They have incredible detail, are fully poseable and come with many customizable options. I did\'nt follow any of the detailed painting guides but wanted to give it a current military look.'),(1893,5363,'1999-04-08 10:35:47',4651,5367,'elvira',0,'I dont think this kit is available any more but if you can get hold of one, it truly is a stunning model. It came with a poster too.'),(1894,5386,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4653,5386,'bell',0,NULL),(1895,5363,'1999-04-09 12:51:13',4654,5367,'akira',0,'This is the worst moulded kit I have ever built. There were lumps the size of the rider that had to be hacksawed off. Having said that the bike is impressive when painted. You will need access to a computer to typeset the front fender stickers. The rider is ill fitting and needed lots of work just to get him in the seat. He does\'nt reach the floor properley (use a stone or something) and his other hand did\'nt reach the handlebar (what can you do?). If your feeling brave try one but it\'s a struggle.'),(1896,5386,'1999-04-09 12:26:19',4655,5386,'sakura',0,'sakura from sakura war'),(1897,5363,'1999-04-09 12:37:39',4656,5367,'storm',0,'If you call youself a Star Wars fan & havent got this model call youself something else. A great model, some of the gun is actually cardboard.\n(Colin hurry up & get your computer fixed...I need more scans)'),(1898,5363,'1999-04-09 12:43:22',4657,5367,'clint',0,'UKGK describes this kit as \"Perfection\". What else can you say.'),(1899,5363,'1999-04-09 12:49:48',4658,5367,'alien',0,'When these 2 kits became available again for £20 each doing this diorama was a must. Sorry, the photos dont do this diorama justice at all. Ripley is the weak link in these models and needs lots of work.'),(1900,5386,'1999-04-09 20:15:11',4659,5386,'shampoo',0,'pretty old kit of Shampoo from Ranma'),(1901,5386,'1999-04-09 20:29:06',4660,5386,'peroth',0,'Peroth From Ah! My Goddess, she is the \nrival of Belldandy.'),(1902,5363,'1999-04-12 11:13:15',4661,5367,'cable',0,'This was an end of line sale, (from Comet Minatures), I loved the pose but wanted to do my own colour scheme.\nIt was hard to get him to stand up though, you have to put something under his feet at an angle.'),(1908,5336,'1999-04-13 01:28:59',3877,5336,'Boris',0,'This kit was painted by hand using Windsor and Newton artist oils, sprayed will a dullcote and then drybrushed with testor enamels mixed slightly with the oils.'),(1910,5336,'1999-04-13 01:40:20',3493,5336,'executioner',0,'This is a pic of my first figure kit ever, i painted it by hand with Windsor and Newton artist oils, the blade is cast metal polished on a dremel tool.'),(1911,5363,'1999-04-15 10:30:49',4663,5367,'chow',0,'If you like John Woo films this is a model for you. But if you dont like lots of blood soaked clothing, bullet holes, this is not the model for you.'),(1912,5386,'1999-04-16 09:47:21',4664,5386,'cammy',0,'Cammy I from Street Fighter, one of \nthe earliest Cammy released'),(1913,5386,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4665,5386,'amg',0,NULL),(1914,4864,'2000-08-29 10:02:14',4666,4864,'kong',0,'Geometric\'s 8th Wonder of the World: KING KONG.\nIncludes scratchbuilt base made of balsa foam, doors are balsa wood, gong is old dog tag\nand added 1/72 scale natives.Nameplate is from Cellar cast. Also used taxidermy eyes on Kong.\nThis buildup won First Place at the Austin Scale Model Show 1999. '),(1915,4864,'1999-04-18 13:49:30',4667,4864,'Drac',0,'I have always loved Christopher Lee as DRACULA and this is an excellent likeness\nto that British \"Prince of Darkness\". The figure is a companion piece\nto the Van Helsing kit which I also have in the gallery.'),(1916,4864,'1999-04-18 14:00:43',4668,4864,'VanH',0,'Dracula\'s arch emeny, Dr. Van Helsing- Peter Cushing\'s best known role\nas the vampire hunter. This is a companion piece to the Dracula figure which is also in the Gremlins Gallery.\nIt took alot of repositioning to get him to face the \"Prince of Darkness\"\ncorrectly but justice won out and the vampire is in trouble.\n'),(1917,5336,'1999-04-27 09:50:06',3752,5336,'alexthevampire',0,'This is Specral Motions Alex the Vampire kit, i painted it with an Aztec Airbrush and Badger Freak-Flex paints.'),(1920,5401,'1999-04-27 11:02:01',4320,5401,'RexCombo',0,'This is the Horizon vinyl cast of Stan Winston\'s original maquette of the T rex from JURASSIC PARK. This model won the Silicon Valley IPMS Best in Show 1996 against a field of about 600 models.'),(1921,5336,'1999-04-27 14:34:46',4669,5336,'krazyhorz',0,'This is Hogans Bones\' Krazy Horz kit. I painted the Horse creature and rider\'s skin tones using an Aztec Airbrush and Badger Freak-Flex paints, the horse creature\'s mane was done with washes of testors enamels using red blues and beiges. The axe handle was made by carving down a 3/4 inch wooden dowl rod and detailing it with a dremel tool, the axe handle is cast metal polished with a dremel tool. The detail areas, like the armor and tassels were drybrushed using testors acrylics.'),(1922,5336,'1999-04-27 10:17:31',4670,5336,'gremlin',0,'This is Michael Burnett Productions Gremlin Bust, it stands approx 14 inches tall and is hollow cast resin. I painted it using an Aztec Airbrush and Badger Freak-Flex paints.'),(1923,4864,'2000-08-29 09:58:05',4946,4864,'It',0,'Billiken\'s \"It Conquered the World\"\'s, Behula and Chris Walaas\' Bob Burns figure\nwith scratch-built base. Added LED lights behind taxidermy eyes. Resin 7-Up soda machine (Chimmneyville?) Bob Burns dropped his MONSTERSCENE\nmagazine with himself on the cover. Scene takes place at Wonderfestival, the yearly garage kit mecca\nin Louisville ,KY. Also Bob Burns assisted in creating the orignal Behula. Very fun to build.\nKit now resides in the Bob Burns grueseum!'),(1924,5411,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4678,5411,'Nosferatu',0,NULL),(1925,4864,'1999-05-04 16:56:06',4680,4864,'MaskRedDeath',0,'From the original Phantom of the Opera silent film\'s only color scene is The Masque of the Red Death.\nLon Chaney Sr\'s legendary role. Jewels were basecoated white then painted with clear red.\nMetal staff skull was polished  with fine grit sandpaper to shine and snake\nwas painted black then drybrushed with interference green and gold.\nBase was basecoated beige and sponged stamped with greys and browns to simulate marble.'),(1926,5314,'1999-05-04 21:15:32',4601,5314,'uranusmodel2',0,'This is a great kit to build!  I made it without any problems whatsoever!  In addition, it is a great rendition of Sailoruranus, one of my favorite senshi.  As an extra touch, I used gold rubbing on her tiara and earring.  I highly recommend this one!  Have fun!'),(1928,5316,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4682,5224,'wolf',0,NULL),(1930,5403,'1999-05-16 14:21:51',4683,5420,'thingverzenden',0,'Scratchbuild base'),(1938,5402,'1999-05-23 14:47:17',4684,5402,'vamwolfpire',0,'This is a large kit with a 20inch wingspan. despite it\'s gravity defying pose it requires no extra pinning.'),(1946,5403,'2