.Box 160859\nNashville\nT.N. 37216-0859'),(2070,5435,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4785,5438,'gremogre',0,NULL),(2071,5323,'1999-12-08 22:18:20',4578,5323,'ghost',0,'This outstanding sculpture was finished with Liquitex acrylics,\nTestors Acryl enamels, and pastels. Mike Hill did a superb job\nof capturing Lon Chaney\'s likeness as the monster, and\nGeometric Design followed through with\nsuper-clean castings. A must have for any\nFrankenstein fan or lover of fine, pop-art\nsculpture. '),(2072,5323,'1999-08-30 16:19:19',4786,5323,'hyde',0,'Another outstanding sculpture from\nMike Hill and Geometric Designs. Bust was\nfinished with Freak Flex, Liquitex and\nTestors Acryl paints.'),(2073,5078,'1999-08-30 18:38:49',4787,5078,'kyg62',0,'The 1962 Godzilla (from King Kong vs Godzilla) is my all time favorite version of the big guy.\nI built this kit for an article in Issue #11 of <A HREF=\"http://www.kaijufan.com/\"> Kaiju Fan</a>. \nYou can see more of my collection at <A HREF=\"http://www.geocities.com/Area51/Corridor/8705/index.html\"> The Godzilla Room</a>.'),(2074,5336,'1999-09-04 19:30:22',3877,5336,'newwolf1',0,'My wife has been bugging me to repaint my old Boris build-up, so here it is. The old version was one of my first kits, let me know which one you like.'),(2075,5336,'1999-09-04 19:40:50',3804,5336,'predator',0,'1/3rd scale Predator i bought at the I.P.M.S Nationals from the Doll&Hobby Shoppe. This kit stands over 2 feet tall!'),(2077,5336,'1999-09-04 20:20:32',4577,5336,'phantom',0,'This kit was a great value, incredible detail for only 40 bucks!'),(2078,4864,'2000-08-29 10:00:34',4790,4864,'Dragon',0,'Custom base with balsa foam rocks, magic sculpt floor and  Mad Lab\'s Sokura the magician\nfigure(Dragon\'s master) added. This is my favorite film and sort of a \"holy grail\" garage \nkit for me.\nI\'d like to thank fellow Gremlin, Marcus Wiedenhoeft, \nfor allowing me to add this really rare\n Geometric kit to my collection of 7th Voyage kits.\nThis buildup won First Place at The San Antonio, TX\nAlamoFiesta Model Show 2000.'),(2080,4864,'1999-09-05 17:46:35',4791,4864,'Creach',0,'Great kit!! Added water float for the Creech\nso he can chill out at Barton Springs pool!'),(2081,5435,'1999-09-06 07:19:49',4372,5438,'gremwolf',0,'This is a re-cast of the Jeff Yagher sculpt, \"Curse of the Werewolf\".'),(2082,4864,'1999-09-06 09:46:25',4794,4864,'spaceg',0,'Very cool kit with a fifties look and a java\nflavor....yum!!! Added a STARBUCKS coffee logo to martian beatnick. I followed David Fisher\'s\npainting guide in Amazing Figure Modeler magazine.'),(2083,4864,'1999-09-06 10:41:04',4795,4864,'Godz92',0,'Godzilla 1992 version by Max Factory is reposed\nwith head crooked to right. Custom scratch built\nbase with Acrylic Gloss Gel for water and railroad\nturf for landscaping. Statue of Liberty was bought at local collectors show.'),(2084,18,'2004-02-28 10:16:03',4796,282,'http://jamesart.com/guinevere.html',1,NULL),(2085,204,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4646,204,'WAR',0,NULL),(2087,5131,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4797,5131,'louder',0,NULL),(2088,204,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4222,204,'Wolfspirit',0,NULL),(2090,204,'1999-09-12 20:09:27',4442,204,'Sayer',0,'One of the best sculpts I\'ve ever seen.\nGreat detail. If this figure had nose hairs,\nyou could count them. Straight up build\nusing acrylics,tinted gell medium and \nmake-up.'),(2091,204,'1999-09-12 22:35:55',4798,204,'SPACEBORNE',0,'Added the wires to look like tubing and the visor.'),(2092,204,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3510,204,'Molepeople',0,NULL),(2093,204,'1999-09-12 22:47:41',4799,204,'Deadeye',0,'The rifle scope is scratch built and the railroad scale brush added'),(2094,204,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4800,204,'SPIDEY',0,NULL),(2095,5073,'1999-09-27 05:07:53',4801,5515,'Littlered',0,'I painted this kit by hand using acrylic paints. I also wanted to show how the young women died so I added claw marks to her throat to show that the Wolf Man had gotten a little too friendly.'),(2104,5201,'2001-01-03 