cribes this - no artwork reference\nor transfers'),(2132,4863,'1999-10-09 15:09:07',4832,5431,'jennifer1',0,'Jennifer, JJ Models Sexy Series n°9\nGold Edition! Real Hair and Skirt!!\nHigh Quality details\nOnly 1.000 pcs. A)Certificate B)Card to Collect c)Comics Introducing!!\nPre-Order your copy by E-mail!\nwww.JJMODELS.com\n'),(2133,5557,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4834,5557,'rs',0,NULL),(2134,5557,'1999-10-10 11:55:53',3243,5557,'kg',0,'This is the LUMINATORS Version.'),(2135,5561,'1999-11-01 16:33:43',4598,5561,'talosb',0,'GEOmetric Designs\'s \"Talos\" was apparently only available at GEO booths at conventions.  I picked mine up at Wonderfest \'96 and just got around to building it in the summer of \'99.  The paint scheme is very simple, bronze that\'s gone \"blue\" in spots, and is really a lot more subtle than it photographed.  The base is from a Revell Velociraptor \"JP-The Lost World\" kit and, yes, the lens-flare is done with Photoshop.\n--Truck'),(2139,4907,'1999-10-11 16:38:03',4835,4907,'Myers',0,'A Don Post Studios Shatner mask that was converted to look exactly like the image of Michael Myers mask from the Halloween 4 movie poster.'),(2141,5571,'2000-10-12 19:12:07',4363,5571,'CaptainAmerica',0,'For more model pics and detailed build-up descriptions, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS @ www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html (Click on my name for direct link)'),(2142,5547,'1999-12-07 17:45:47',4838,5547,'terminator',0,'This kit captures Arnold dead on!!\nShawn Nagle Rules!!'),(2146,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3508,5551,'joker',0,NULL),(2147,5561,'1999-10-21 05:04:40',4839,5561,'Pegalis',0,'On a quest to capture all of the Billiken Kaiju kits, I decide I must bite the bullet and land the goofiest looking one of all...or maybe that was the one with a clam for a head...but, seriously, Peguila is a monster from the old Japanese T.V. show \"Ultra-Q\" which was the forerunner of \"Ultraman\" and can only be described as \"X-Files with giant monsters\".  The suit was reused in an episode of \"Ultraman\", \"disguised\" with an extra horn on it\'s head...anyhow, he\'s done in grays and purples, and, in painting him, I learned never to use an airbrush outside on a day where the temp. is over 100 degrees F., windless or not...paint was drying before it hit the kit...--Truck'),(2151,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3495,5551,'batman',0,NULL),(2168,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3941,5551,'atat',0,NULL),(2169,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4488,5551,'burster',0,NULL),(2170,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3499,5551,'cat',0,NULL),(2171,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3477,5551,'alien3',0,NULL),(2172,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3553,5551,'fett',0,NULL),(2173,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3478,5551,'queen',0,NULL),(2174,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4019,5551,'speader',0,NULL),(2181,5571,'2000-10-12 19:17:01',4842,5571,'BatmanForever',0,'For more model pics and detailed build-up descriptions, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS @ www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html (Click on my name for direct link)'),(2182,5571,'2000-10-12 19:11:11',3496,5571,'BatmanReturns',0,'For more model pics and detailed build-up descriptions, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS @ www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html (Click on my name for direct link)'),(2183,5571,'2000-10-12 19:14:14',4844,5571,'JOKER',0,'For more model pics and detailed build-up descriptions, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS @ www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html (Click on my name for direct link)'),(2184,5571,'2000-10-12 19:09:56',4845,5571,'spock',0,'For more model pics and detailed build-up descriptions, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS @ www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html (Click on my name for direct link)'),(2185,5571,'2000-10-12 19:18:16',4846,5571,'starwarsc3po',0,'For more model pics and detailed build-up descriptions, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS @ www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html (Click on my name for direct link)'),(2175,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3215,5551,'vader',0,NULL),(2176,5551,'2000-04-21 11:45:01',4112,5551,'warrior',0,'The Base for this kit was scratch built with junk that i found at work & lots of Jiffycell foam and hot glue sticks'),(2177,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4766,5551,'gamepred',0,NULL),(2178,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4766,5551,'pred1',0,NULL),(2179,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3232,5551,'pred2',0,NULL),(2180,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4841,5551,'loader',0,NULL),(2186,5571,'2000-10-12 19:15:35',3521,5571,'TheMightyThor',0,'For more model pics and detailed build-up descriptions, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS @ www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html (Click on my name for direct link)'),(2187,5571,'2000-10-12 19:19:16',4848,5571,'thething',0,'For more model pics and detailed build-up descriptions, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS @ www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html (Click on my name for direct link)'),(2188,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4849,5551,'falcon',0,NULL),(2189,5538,'2000-04-30 06:49:55',5053,5812,'atpt',0,'According to Star Wars:  The Essential Guide to Vehicles and Vessels, this was the first one-man walker designed by the Old Republic.  \n\nScatchbuilt by Matt Hawkins out of styrene in 1:20 scale.  Based on original design by Rob Caswell and Doug Chiang. Visit my website for more info.  It is not available as a model kit.  Visit my website for more info...www.cygenus-studios.com '),(2195,5578,'1999-10-18 05:32:23',4851,5578,'Santa',0,'This is a 4 piece resin casting of my original sculpture. I sculpted Santa in Super Sculpey. He\'s my second try at sculpting. This was the first time I tried mold making and casting. Please contact me with any comments or suggestions.'),(2196,5557,'1999-10-19 17:24:18',3929,5557,'mumbw',0,'This is the TRU re-issue.'),(2197,5435,'1999-10-21 08:22:10',4852,5438,'gremgilator1',0,'A must have kit for the \"Creature\" or \"Predator\" fanatic!  The best of \"both\" worlds in one box.  M.I.M. informed me that there were only (15) of these kits made!!!  I offer my build-up and painting services to fellow collectors and manufacturers. \nI can be contacted by e-mail at:\ntarmin8or@parlorcity.com\n\n Thank you for your interest.'),(2200,5559,'2001-09-26 23:22:14',4854,5559,'littlegmen',0,'Our NEW web site is up and running!!! Little Green Man has been one of out top sellers and Will now be featured in the next issue of AMAZING FIGURE MODELER #20 Dont miss it!!!'),(2202,5551,'1999-10-24 12:11:16',3945,5551,'carnage',0,'PARTTIME PAINTERS BEWARE'),(2207,5561,'1999-11-01 09:46:41',4066,5561,'creaturea',0,'My take on the Gillman, based on Anthony Mestas\' fantastic article in AFM.  I owned two cats at the time and they had knocked the kit to the floor a half-dozen times, rending it all but irrepairable on the last attack.  As per Anthony\'s article, I cut it down, added a base and a log, and about nine layers of acrylic gloss medium for water. Problem solved.  Dave Cockrum went *nuts* over this build-up at the first Modelrama, but bemoaned cutting down one of his three copies of the kit -- Truck'),(2208,5561,'1999-11-02 16:48:54',4855,5561,'redkingb',0,'This guy is the favorite kaiju of a LOT of \"Ultraman\" fans.  I love him, too, however, I discovered that painting him can be a bear...if one watches the episodes that Red King appears in, the skin texture looks, very oddly, like gold spray-paint flaking off blue-gray foam rubber...hmmmmm...I tried to simulate that on my first attempt painting this kit and failed pathetically, second attempt, I toned the gold down to an earth-tan and was satisfied with the result.  Maybe not 100 percent accurate, but it sure displays keen.  \"Aiyeee! Run!  It\'s a giant corn-cob monster!!\" -- Truck'),(2209,5561,'1999-11-01 11:03:46',4856,5561,'gaboraha',0,'Brian Hugg released his first kaiju sculpt of the nasty red-headed monster from \"Godzilla\'s Revenge\" on a very limited basis.  The kit was later picked up for release by X-O Facto and these releases included a base.  A solid first kit on Brian\'s part, it came with a little packet of hair that he\'d trimmed off his daughter\'s unsuspecting \"Lion King\" stuffed toy for detailing.'),(2210,5587,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4857,5587,'REALPRD1',0,NULL),(2211,5587,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4857,5587,'REALPRD2',0,NULL),(2212,5587,'1999-11-01 18:35:54',4857,5587,'REALPRD2',0,'With due respect to the talented sculptor, the kit\'s legs appeared too long.  I made the attempt to sculpt the lower torso and here are the results.'),(2213,5587,'1999-11-01 18:34:28',4857,5587,'REALPRD3',0,'With due respect to the talented sculptor, the kit\'s legs appeared too long.  I made the attempt to sculpt the lower torso and here are the results.'),(2214,5587,'1999-11-01 18:40:46',4857,5587,'REALPRD4',0,'With due respect to the talented sculptor, the kit\'s legs appeared too long.  I made the attempt to sculpt the lower torso and here are the results.'),(2215,159,'1999-11-03 15:23:50',4858,159,'Barbarian',0,'Ral Partha lead cast.'),(2216,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4859,159,'BriteOgre',0,NULL),(2217,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4860,159,'ChickenHawk',0,NULL),(2218,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4861,159,'DwarfPirate',0,NULL),(2219,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4862,159,'GoblinBanner',0,NULL),(2220,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4863,159,'OrcCaptain',0,NULL),(2221,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4864,159,'OrcGeneral',0,NULL),(2222,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4865,159,'RenKnight',0,NULL),(2223,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4866,159,'Rider',0,NULL),(2224,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4869,159,'4eyeGoblin',0,NULL),(2225,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3856,159,'BruteKong',0,NULL),(2226,4863,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4870,5431,'alexandra1',0,NULL),(2227,5547,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4871,5547,'Chaney',0,NULL),(2303,5215,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4924,5215,'LadyDeath',0,NULL),(2228,5547,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4872,5547,'werewolf',0,NULL),(2229,159,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4867,159,'betty',0,NULL),(2230,5608,'1999-11-09 08:59:30',4579,5608,'raptor',0,'Horizon\'s big \'raptor.  Painted with taxidermy paints.\nEyes were replaced with glass coyote eyes.\nFilling the leg with resin and reinforcing with large \ngauge aluminum rod gets this bad boy dancing on one leg!'),(2233,5137,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4873,5137,'BandC',0,NULL),(2235,5137,'1999-11-09 18:19:45',4874,5137,'Boop',0,'Unfinished Rick Wyatt sculpt that I completed for Diceman.'),(2238,5137,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4875,5137,'wolfman',0,NULL),(2239,5137,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4876,5137,'KoF',0,NULL),(2240,5137,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4877,5137,'creature',0,NULL),(2241,5533,'1999-11-17 12:26:49',4878,5533,'WORMFULL',0,'8.25 inches tall. Sculpted and Painted by Dave Coughtry.'),(2242,5533,'1999-11-17 12:25:41',4879,5533,'MAXFULL',0,'8.5 inches tall. Sculpted and painted by Dave Coughtry.'),(2243,5131,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4880,5131,'jackcrow',0,NULL),(2244,5615,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4889,5615,'frankengirl',0,NULL),(2246,5323,'1999-12-08 21:23:38',4882,5323,'sonof',0,'Yet another superb classic monster kit\nfrom GEOmetric Design and\nmaster sculptor William Paquet. The likeness and\ndetail on this sculpture are just remarkable.\nAlso incuded here is Anthony Mestas\' resin\nbase which finishes the piece nicely.\nKit and base were finished with Liquitex (fleshtones applied with an Aztek A470),\nTamyia, and Testors \"Acryl\" acrylic paints, and\npastels. '),(2247,5633,'1999-12-09 21:11:34',3495,5633,'batman03',0,'This is the first model kit that I build.\nPainted with Acrilics colors. I try to take the advantage of the semi matt shine of the acrylic paints to reproduce the natural shine of the rubber of the real suit.\nPainted with paintbrush.\n'),(2248,5633,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3495,5633,'batman08',0,NULL),(2249,5633,'1999-12-09 21:26:06',3499,5633,'catwoman01',0,'This Michelle Pfiffer s model kit of Batman Return s Catwoman, has a exellent level of detail.\nPainted with Acrylic paints, the suit was lacquered with brillant acrylic varnish to archieve the texture of the Vinyl and the face almo