tions 1.000 pcs only! Including Warrantie,Card to collect and comics introdutions\nNOW AVAIALABLE!! Order Your copy by \nE-mail '),(2337,5415,'2000-03-17 17:47:59',4956,5415,'maxm2',0,'I purchased this kit through Frontier Models in the UK.  It is a bit rough but builds up beautifully with some work.  The kit is primarily resin, but includes aluminum tubing for the shotgun barrels, leather for the belt details, and sheet styrene for the leg brace.  I tossed out the styrene and scratch-built a new leg brace from aluminum sheet metal.'),(2338,5237,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4958,5237,'deck',0,NULL),(2340,5237,'2000-03-19 20:39:13',4919,5237,'tail',0,'what else can you do with those spare bits from previous conversions?'),(2341,5237,'2000-03-19 20:42:13',4959,5237,'smokin',0,'Plastic skeleton kit worked up with other bits and pieces'),(2342,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4961,5551,'battle',0,NULL),(2343,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4960,5551,'stap',0,NULL),(2345,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4620,5551,'channard',0,NULL),(2346,5551,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4962,5551,'ghost',0,NULL),(2348,5386,'2000-03-29 17:56:42',4964,5386,'wingzero',0,'HG-grade kit of the main robot from \nthe \"Gundam Wing: Endless Waltz\" OVA.\nSince it is a plastic kit, everything is movable. \nBut it took me years to sand \nand fill the gaps, etc. \nI should have gotten a resin version of this.  So far Wing Zero, Deathscythe, Sandrock, and Nataku are done.\nPending on Heavy Arm and Tallgeese III. '),(2349,5386,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4964,5386,'wingzero',0,NULL),(2350,5386,'2000-03-29 17:49:37',4966,5386,'shiki',0,'Main female character with two swords \nfrom the game \"Samurai Spirits\"  \nAlmost did not make it through the earth quake'),(2351,5386,'2000-03-29 18:39:20',4967,5386,'deathscythe',0,'HG-grade kit from the \"Gundam Wing: Endless Waltz\" OVA. Since it is a plastic kit, everything is\n           movable. But it took me years to sand and fill the gaps, etc. I should have gotten a resin version of this. So far Wing\n           Zero, Deathscythe, Sandrock, and Nataku are done. Pending on Heavy Arm and Tallgeese III.  '),(2352,5386,'2000-03-29 18:53:59',4968,5386,'nataku',0,'HG-grade kit from the \"Gundam Wing: Endless Waltz\" OVA. Since it is a plastic kit, everything is movable. But it\n           took me years to sand and fill the gaps, etc. I should have gotten a resin version of this. So far Wing Zero, Deathscythe,\n           Sandrock, and Nataku are done. Pending on Heavy Arm and Tallgeese III.  '),(2353,5779,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4965,5779,'WingedLioness',0,NULL),(2354,5386,'2000-03-31 00:49:56',4969,5386,'sandrock',0,'HG-grade kit from the \"Gundam Wing: Endless Waltz\" OVA. Since it is a plastic kit, everything is movable. But it\n           took me years to sand and fill the gaps, etc. I should have gotten a resin version of this. So far Wing Zero, Deathscythe,\n           Sandrock, and Nataku are done. Pending on Heavy Arm and Tallgeese III.  \n          '),(2357,5765,'2000-04-07 01:48:48',4971,5765,'saturn',0,'This model was my first attempt at a solid resin kit.\nOverall, I\'d say this was a pretty nice kit.  Minimal mold lines \nand quite easy to assemble.  I\'d recommend it to Sailor fans and\nAnime fans in general.'),(2358,5323,'2000-04-07 14:43:28',4973,5323,'wolf',0,'Entirely hand brushed with\nTestors and Liquitex acrylics.\nShaded kit and restored lost fur surface texture on\nlegs with pastels.'),(2448,5119,'2000-08-09 09:03:21',5104,5939,'Flandersgrem',0,'Kit stands 8\" tall and is in scale with \"The Count\" and \"Kang\".  Sells for $45 + 6SH and all US shipping icludes USPS tracking numbers. Contact mikepetryszak@hotmail.com for orders'),(2449,5119,'2000-08-10 10:11:01',5105,5940,'Huntress',0,'This Kit is huge!!! over 13\". Body and tree are ROTO-cast and light. Kit incudes base. All shipping in the US includes USPS tracking numbers. '),(2361,5592,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3881,5592,'mars',0,NULL),(2365,5592,'2000-04-16 19:19:03',3522,5592,'thing',0,'top pic was taken outside\nbottom was under artificial light\n'),(2366,5761,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',3880,5761,'wolfman',0,NULL),(2371,4864,'2000-04-25 09:24:01',5051,4864,'GvKCastle',0,'Paradise\'s 1962 GODZILLA (12\") and Billiken\'s Gorilla 2 (11\"), reposed with cut doll hair (several colors) added.\nOsaka Castle is by Doyusha, which was destroyed with sprue cutters and re-glued into place.\nAdded railroad scenery over base made of balsa foam and Durham\'s water putty. A true labor of love...one of my favorite films!!\nCheck out my website \"Attack of the Monster Garage Kits\":\nhttp://home.talkcity.com/TheDrag/bmonsterfan/index.html'),(2381,5338,'2000-05-12 01:16:29',5057,5142,'WEBnew',0,'Here is the latest in the \'Hammers Horrors\', sculpted by Mike Hill the bust is now available direct from us.'),(2383,4864,'2000-05-14 19:28:19',5058,4864,'GodzMothi',0,'Kaiyodo\'s 1/450 scale kit, reposed with custom base.\nTail dragging scene from 1964\'s \"Godzilla vs the Thing\".'),(2384,4864,'2000-05-14 19:52:38',5059,4864,'Saucermen',0,'Great diorama, with railroad scenery\nadded and two extra saucermen.'),(2385,4864,'2000-05-14 20:02:34',5060,4864,'GodzvLarva',0,'Great 1/200 scale vinyl kit from Paradise of Japan.\nAdded custom base. From 1964 film \n\"Godzilla vs the Thing\" final scene.'),(2386,233,'2000-05-14 21:23:56',4974,5829,'kai',0,'Kaiju is a BIG kit limited to 500 castings.  Sculpted by Tony Spangler and cast by Mark Brokaw, this kit is sure to be a hit among Japanese monster fans!  Visit Artistic License Productions\' home page to order yours!'),(2388,5765,'2000-06-02 01:28:09',5062,5765,'spacewolf',0,'This is the resin Space Wolf kit manufactured by ForgeWorld.  Quite a nice kit to paint.  It\'s pretty detailed despite being only 2 pieces (the guy and the backpack).  I originally wanted to airbrush him but found that he was a little too small for that. So, he\'s totally hand painted.  I\'m pretty satisfied with the way he came out. '),(2389,5559,'2001-09-26 23:22:51',5063,5559,'pickledpunk',0,'New web site is up and running!!! The Pickled Punk is now availible!!! Drop us a line for all the details ! He will also be featured in the next issue of AMAZING FIGURE MODELER #20 '),(2390,5765,'2000-06-07 23:23:12',3610,5765,'resiniria',0,'My first 1/6 kit.  Absolutely lovely.  I really enjoyed painting this kit.  I did subtle grey shading on the armour.  I figured that with such a finely detailed kit, it would be a shame not to give that armour more attention!  The black lining defining the armoured plates were done with a fine brush with titanium white touch ups.  I should\'ve used a Gundam Marker because we all know how much fun it is to get a nice even coat of white over black!  Oh well, live and learn.  '),(2391,4931,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5066,5439,'mangalore',0,NULL),(2450,5411,'2000-08-16 08:10:46',4537,5411,'moon',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2451,5411,'2000-08-16 08:14:27',4350,5411,'vamp',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2392,5621,'2000-08-04 13:13:23',5067,5621,'mayumi',0,'Check my webpage : \nhttp://animefigurekit.com/\nLike the way I paint?  I can paint model for you!!  look my webpage.'),(2393,5621,'2000-08-04 13:14:41',5068,5621,'minami',0,'Check my webpage : \nhttp://animefigurekit.com/\nLike the way I paint?  I can paint model for you!!  look my webpage.'),(2394,5621,'2000-08-04 13:14:59',5069,5621,'yuka',0,'Check my webpage : \nhttp://animefigurekit.com/\nLike the way I paint?  I can paint model for you!!  look my webpage.'),(2395,5621,'2000-08-04 13:12:47',5070,5621,'ginreibase',0,'Check my webpage : \nhttp://animefigurekit.com/\nLike the way I paint?  I can paint model for you!!  look my webpage.'),(2396,4864,'2000-06-21 19:02:36',5071,4864,'CConquest',0,'Mars Attacks Contemplating Conquest\nTelian Piar the Martian Paeec, studies\nthe human species, contemplating the attack\non earth. Base by Avalon.'),(2398,5621,'2000-08-04 13:13:50',5072,5621,'kaede',0,'Check my webpage : \nhttp://animefigurekit.com/\nLike the way I paint?  I can paint model for you!!  look my webpage.'),(2399,5621,'2000-08-04 13:11:49',5074,5621,'rimeifon',0,'She\'s the heroine of Angel Links\nCheck my webpage : \nhttp://animefigurekit.com/\nLike the way I paint?  I can paint model for you!!  look my webpage.'),(2400,5621,'2000-08-04 13:14:05',5076,5621,'suzumi',0,'Check my webpage : \nhttp://animefigurekit.com/\nLike the way I paint?  I can paint model for you!!  look my webpage.'),(2401,5714,'2000-08-13 00:50:28',3252,149,'vpink2',0,'This is the violet vixen kit from azimuth with a little of my personal touch. I sponged powder pink, baby blue, white, and silver metallic to achieve the shimmery effect. If anyone wants to purchase this or wants me to paint their kit please contact me.I also left the eyes white to get the supernatural power effect'),(2402,5765,'2000-07-01 18:46:52',5077,5765,'misatogrem',0,'This model was a pretty fun and easy model to paint.  I put about 8 hours into it including cleaning and priming.  Very easy to assemble (what would you expect from an 8 piece kit?) although the arm that extends behind her back isn\'t quite level with where her legs rest on the mounting surface.  It tilts the model off balance a little and I almost had a heart attack while I was varnishing her as it almost toppled onto my garage floor!  I made a small NERV handbook out of some plasticard and slid it under her hand to balance the model. '),(2403,5765,'2000-07-01 19:05:00',5078,5765,'vashgrem',0,'Awesome.  If you have a DVD player and haven\'t seen the Trigun series, get it!  It\'s put out by Pioneer Animation.  Well, this model was really easy too.  The coolest part is the red coat with the scorched look at the bottom.  Just mist on some red mixed with black over the red basecoat.  Repeat with more black mixed into the red black mixture.  Easy yet so effective.  I experimented with a brand of airbrush paint that I wasn\'t familiar with for the red.  It\'s called Createx Opaque Red.  I hate it.  If anything, it\'s more of a pinkish red.  I had to mist on some Citadel Blood Red to get the colour right on the coat.  Oh well, live and learn.\n\"Love and Peace!!\"'),(2404,5824,'2000-07-05 09:15:42',5079,5824,'anguish',0,'Based on the art of Bernie Wrightson'),(2406,4863,'2000-08-29 12:26:29',5080,5431,'EVIL1',0,'New era Art Series Vol.2 The essence of the Evil!\nExtraordinary JJM Kit with pure resin, clear resin and metal parts!!\n\nYou can see more details of this Artistic model on www.jjmodels.com or www.anotherworlddesigns.com'),(2407,5329,'2004-02-20 21:38:52',4941,5771,'greenbeholder',0,'<B>Based on the many eyed Beholder monster from <I>Advanced Dungeons and Dragons</i>. I created this out of various materials I had hanging around.\r\nThe core is a styrofoam ball while the covering is <I>Model Magic</i> by <I>Crayola</i> (neat stuff).  \r\nBase is made of many different materials and depict treasures collected for and by this creature. \r\nDrips of resin simulate drool and slime. Painted in acrylics with a dark wash. <BR>\r\nAbout 2\" across and the base is 5\"x5\".\r\nI plan on producing a small kit similar to this. <BR>\r\n<BR>My others: \r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2407> <IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/greenbeholder_icon.gif alt=\"Baby Green Beholder - 1st one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2347><IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/bluebeholder_icon.gif alt=\"Baby Blue Beholder - 2nd one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2319><img src=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/beholder_icon.gif alt=\"Hatchling Beholder - 3rd one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2326><img src=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/redbeholder_icon.gif alt=\"Red Beholder - 4th one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2605><IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/greenbeholder2_icon.gif alt=\"Green Beholder - 5th one produced\" align=middle></a><A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=3042><IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/mottled_icon.gif alt=\"Mottled Beholder - 6th one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<HR>More info write:<A HREF=mailto:trekist@hotmail.com>trekist@hotmail.com</a>\r\n<BR> Pics are being updated.'),(2408,5270,'2001-01-03 11:46:29',3953,5270,'wolf',0,''),(2409,5538,'2001-11-15 04:54:18',4850,5812,'critterpnt1',0,'Critter is a 1:1 scale, 14\" tall, 7-piece resin kit.  It weighs about 3.5lbs and the kits sell for $165 + $8 domestic shipping.  Order online at www.cygenus-studios.com'),(2413,5015,'2000-07-13 16:51:48',5082,5906,'droid',0,'This is a scratchbuilt model of the Pit Droid, based on a pre-production                                                    \nsketch from the book \"The Making of the Phantom Menace\".  I was faithful \nto the drawing with the exception of a set of what look like eyes on the \nhead I thought made it look a little goofy. It was sculpted from REN shape \na carvable resin similair to Balsa Foam, except it is much harder and a \nlot more expensive.  The face is a piece of acrylic turned on a milling \nlathe and back painted.  The base is sculpted particle board covered with \nsand from my local volleyball pit.  I first used enamels before switching \nto the laquers we use at work, and what a difference it makes.  If you have \nthe facilities I recommend laquers.  Unfortunately the picture was taken with \na digital camera and I lost a lot of the detail when I lowered the resoultion.\nI weathered the model with chalk pastels which works great when your airbrush is \nout of order(mine is). Id love to answer any questions or hear your comments so \nfeel free to email me.  '),(2414,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5083,5914,'peorth1',0,NULL),(2415,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5083,5914,'peorth2',0,NULL),(2416,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5085,5914,'cloudknight1',0,NULL),(2417,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5085,5914,'cloudknight2',0,NULL),(2418,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5085,5914,'cloudknight3',0,NULL),(2419,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5086,5914,'mai1',0,NULL),(2420,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5086,5914,'mai2',0,NULL),(2421,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5086,5914,'mai3',0,NULL),(2422,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5087,5914,'freeman1',0,NULL),(2423,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5087,5914,'freeman2',0,NULL),(2424,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5088,5914,'rebirthofanangel1',0,NULL),(2425,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5088,5914,'rebirthofanangel2',0,NULL),(2426,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5088,5914,'rebirthofanangel3',0,NULL),(2428,5411,'2000-07-24 09:31:32',5090,5411,'abe',0,'Bust from Bowen design repaint using enamels'),(2429,5411,'2000-07-25 01:50:53',5091,5411,'esme',0,'Hand painted using enamels'),(2430,5411,'2000-07-25 01:53:53',5092,5411,'grave',0,'Graveyard statue from Moore creation, repainted using enamels.'),(2431,5411,'2000-07-24 09:46:11',4816,5411,'hellboy',0,'Hellboy bust from Boiwen design repainted using enamels'),(2432,5411,'2000-07-25 01:50:24',5093,5411,'lobo',0,'Small version of the 1/6 statue from DC-comics, repainted using enamels'),(2433,5411,'2000-07-24 09:53:01',5094,5411,'marvb',0,'The famous character from the comics Sin City, I repainted the bust using enamels'),(2434,5411,'2000-07-26 10:08:14',5095,5411,'marv',0,'I repainted this action figures from Marv using enamels'),(2435,5411,'2000-07-24 10:05:12',5096,5411,'cullo',0,'70mm scale figure painted using enamels'),(2436,5411,'2000-07-25 01:51:19',5097,5411,'culloden',0,'Hand painted using enamels'),(2437,5411,'2000-07-24 10:11:36',5098,5411,'celt',0,'Bust from a French compagny, painted using enamels'),(2438,5411,'2000-07-24 10:15:25',5099,5411,'crazy',0,'Bust of the famous Indian chief, painted using enamels'),(2439,5411,'2000-07-26 10:11:47',3813,5411,'bat',0,'painted using enamels'),(2440,5411,'2000-07-26 10:14:46',5101,5411,'bat',0,'painted using enamels'),(2441,5411,'2000-07-26 23:57:36',5102,5411,'orc',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2442,5411,'2000-07-26 23:59:36',4450,5411,'slaine',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2443,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5103,5914,'Belldandygod1',0,NULL),(2444,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5103,5914,'Belldandygod2',0,NULL),(2445,5575,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5103,5914,'Belldandygod3',0,NULL),(2452,5411,'2000-08-16 08:17:03',3277,5411,'decapi',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2453,5411,'2000-08-16 08:53:29',3814,5411,'dalakiel',0,'Statue repainted using enamels'),(2454,5411,'2000-08-16 08:59:33',5108,5411,'GI',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2455,5411,'2000-08-16 09:05:46',5109,5411,'cavalier',0,'120mm figure painted using enamels'),(2456,5411,'2000-08-17 01:18:30',5062,5411,'SWBC',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2457,5411,'2000-08-17 01:24:26',5110,5411,'Emp',0,'I converted this kit to obtain a figure of The Emperor of Mankind in the WH40k universe'),(2458,5411,'2000-08-17 01:27:54',5111,5411,'sister',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2459,5411,'2000-08-18 05:10:33',5112,5411,'comm',0,'I modified the cap and added a \'chainsword\' to the 54mm figure of a Russian line officer to obtain this representation of the Colonel Commissar Ibram Gaunt leader of the Tanith First (and only !) Imperial Guard in the WH40k universe\n(Painted using enamels).'),(2460,5411,'2000-08-17 01:59:49',5114,5411,'SW',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2461,319,'2000-08-17 17:47:28',4656,319,'troop',0,'Customized base, scratch built Mousedroid and a plaster casting of the head from Screamin\' Han Solo 1/4 kit. Addition of rubber ribbing, (black speaker wire), around neck. Note: recasting of Han Solo head done for personal use only . . . don\'t buy re-cast kits. For larger pics please visit Ryan\'s Hobbies Gallery <a href=\"http://www.islandnet.com/~grealyrk\" target=\"_blank\"><B>HERE</B></a>'),(2462,5411,'2000-08-18 00:47:11',5115,5411,'conan',0,'54 mm figure painted using enamels'),(2463,5411,'2000-08-18 00:54:50',5117,5411,'offhuss',0,'120mm figure painted using enamels'),(2464,5411,'2000-08-18 00:55:14',5116,5411,'huron',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2467,5767,'2000-08-23 01:12:31',5120,5767,'T800',0,'First portrait made for the sculptore Salvador Ali, second version in progress'),(2469,5767,'2000-08-23 01:25:46',5122,5767,'RHINO',0,'SCRATCH BUILD OF RHINO'),(2470,5841,'2004-01-28 08:52:11',5561,5841,'lyra',0,'Solarwinds Lyra, excellent Bust, well cats and no filling required.'),(2471,4864,'2006-06-09 12:50:04',5125,4864,'RevCreature',0,'An action packed resin kit of the famous Gillman of the Amazon seeking revenge.\r\nAdded clear tinted resin for water base- check out the hungry croc\r\nclosing in on victim in the water. Based on a Dave Cochran comicbook.\r\nFor more Creature kits, check out my website:\r\nwww.monsterjones.com'),(2472,4864,'2006-06-09 12:53:37',5126,4864,'microCreature',0,'Geometric\'s micro series Creature is my favorite!\r\nA super sculpt and fantasic casting.\r\nThis kit won First place - Science Fiction figures- at the\r\nAustin Scale Model Show 2000.\r\nFor more Creature kits, check out my website:\r\nwww.monsterjones.com'),(2473,5889,'2001-07-17 15:18:03',5132,5889,'reaper',0,'1/6 scale model kit based on the character from the hit PC game \'Dungeon Keeper\'. The kit comes well presented in high quality resin and white metal in a total of 13 pieces including the base. For more information and for ordering details please visit my website at http://anjaradesign.tripod.com or e-mail: anjaradesign@btinternet.com'),(2477,5934,'2000-09-11 05:43:54',5129,5934,'Quasimodo',0,'This scratchbuild of my favourite movie character is actually made of two materials.While the \'body\' is Super Sculpey, the head is entirely formed and carved from Milliput.\n'),(2478,5889,'2001-07-17 15:19:18',5130,5889,'maul',0,'1/6 scale model kit cleanly cast in 100% bubble free resin and white metal. For more information please visit our website at http://anjaradesign.tripod.com or e-mail: anjaradesign@btinternet.com'),(2482,5933,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5134,5933,'black1',0,NULL),(2483,5559,'2001-09-26 23:24:37',5133,5559,'voodoobuddy',0,'Our NEW web site is up and running!!!'),(2484,5559,'2001-09-26 23:25:10',5133,5559,'voodoo',0,'Voodoo Buddy is your very own voodoo doll... Who said there for the experts!!\r\nOnly $15.00 plus shipping Contact me for all the details...'),(2493,5559,'2000-12-30 00:15:20',5133,5559,'content',0,'Voodoo Buddy includes all kinds of goodies!!!!'),(2494,5363,'2000-09-14 10:37:46',5135,5367,'guns',0,'Converted water pistols that Toys R us was selling for £1.00. With peices added from my bits box.'),(2495,5363,'2000-09-14 12:00:36',5137,5367,'sub',0,'An unusual model, re-released with the remastered film it has had some changes to it that dnt quite make sense. Peices leftover and decals that dont fit markings. I guess you\'d have to see the origonal release. Still it\'s a fun kit.'),(2496,5363,'2000-09-14 12:07:53',5138,5367,'abc',0,'A fantastic kit, but make sure you get the origonal (Argonaut I think) and not the recast. Also it\'s crying out for bass wire to be added.'),(2497,5363,'2000-09-14 12:17:26',5139,5367,'atat',0,'I saw this pose in The Star Wars Chronicles book (the most expensive book I\'ve ever bought), it took two kits to make this pose and some of Nickys (my lovely wife) black cotton. But I much prefer this pose to the standard one.'),(2498,5363,'2000-09-15 10:35:17',5140,5367,'209',0,'A nice kit, I did\'nt follow the painting guide though, I thought a metallic blue would be nice. Also a big thanks to Bob (work mate) for all the scans.'),(2499,5363,'2000-09-15 10:38:38',5141,5367,'ciria',0,'A good kit but I\'m afraid my painting is not up to the same standaed as Han Lin, I think his stuff is first class.'),(2500,5363,'2000-09-15 10:42:13',5142,5367,'dee',0,'The bases are 2 candle holders my wife bought somewhere. T Hawk is also the first model I used metallic pens on, I have used them regularly since.'),(2501,5363,'2000-09-15 10:46:46',5143,5367,'die',0,'The main thing that troubled me about this kit is I did\'nt know what his tattoo was of, so I left it out. Glass was added from a nearby smashed bus shelter...kids!'),(2506,5884,'2001-02-04 14:28:34',5149,5884,'Shoarin1',0,'I am selling her on ebay Anime Painted Resin Kit Cute Shaorin\r\n                              Item #554473657.  I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2619,5884,'2001-02-12 18:46:53',5215,5884,'sakuragrem',0,'Please visit my web site to find out about my painting service and more detailed pictures of my other kits\r\n<A HREF=\"http://www3.ns.sympatico.ca/dawn.plante/\"><b> CLICK HERE</B></A>.'),(2507,5884,'2001-02-03 14:23:45',5147,5884,'maid2',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2508,4863,'2001-01-06 11:53:27',5145,5431,'shadreil1',0,'The New JJ Models Fantasy Series Kit!!\r\nShadreil The Sorceress!\r\nHigh Quality Resin kit with clear resin and metal parts included. \r\nLimited Editions Order your copy By E-mail Today!!www.JJMODELS.com or www.AnotherWorldDesigns.com (for US resident only)'),(2504,5973,'2000-09-20 01:50:29',5144,5973,'Musette',0,'Musette is the first offering from Fogger Studios.  Her price includes S&H if you are inside the continental US. She sits at around 7\" high, and standing would top 13\".  Given the fairy nature of the subject, the painting possibilities are endless!'),(2509,5314,'2000-09-25 16:25:51',5146,5314,'SDUrd',0,'This was not a Japanese kit, but a Korean one.  I think there is a difference in quality as some of the parts (mainly the hair) did not fit together well and required quite a bit of putty work.  However, the painting went smoothly and it\'s a nice sculpt.'),(2510,5761,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',4578,5761,'Frankenstein0002',0,NULL),(2511,5884,'2001-02-03 14:21:08',3443,5884,'sailormoondone',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2512,5884,'2001-02-03 14:21:39',5073,5884,'2',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2661,6209,'2001-07-09 15:12:02',5242,6209,'mummy',0,'This was handbrushed with acrylics.  I decided to go with a more earthy, brownish color scheme instead of the traditional gray.\r\n\r\n'),(2513,5363,'2000-09-30 00:41:17',4624,5367,'iria',0,'This is the bit left over from the excellent Iria kit. I just stuck it on a pole. It was better than throwing it away!'),(2514,5363,'2000-09-30 00:50:10',5151,5367,'Tank',0,'This was an impulse buy, mainly because it was only £10. I converted it, the barrel was soweedy looking, and I also added some leftover Warhammer bits.'),(2515,5363,'2000-09-30 00:57:50',5152,5367,'grom',0,'A Close Shave.'),(2517,4864,'2000-10-01 19:31:40',5153,4864,'MicroMutant1',0,'Geometric\'s 1/35 scale micro monster from the 1955\n Universal classic film \"This Island Earth\".'),(2518,4864,'2000-10-01 19:41:39',5154,4864,'McVeyMutant1',0,'Super resin kit of the Metaluna Mutant from Universal\'s 1955 film, \"This Island Earth\"!'),(2519,5363,'2000-10-02 10:26:51',5155,5367,'heroes',0,'You get 3 in a box, bargain!'),(2520,5363,'2000-10-02 10:30:33',5156,5367,'mars',0,'I picked this up at Comet Minatures in the bargain bucket for £20. There was no box or instructions, the helmet had a crack but it still came with multiple hands and guns. And lets face it, where are you going to get one of these kits for that price.'),(2521,5363,'2000-10-04 10:12:13',5158,5367,'sulaco',0,'This kit was recommended to me by my friend Steve, and I was\'nt dissapointed.'),(2522,5363,'2000-10-04 10:15:10',5159,5367,'safs',0,'This is an unusual kit, it looks like some WW2 German peice of machinery but it\'s a futuristic kit.'),(2523,5884,'2001-02-03 14:24:22',5157,5884,'Reigrem',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2524,5884,'2001-02-03 14:25:56',3830,5884,'siren1',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2525,5363,'2000-10-07 01:03:55',5160,5367,'nau',0,'Its a small person on a funny bird, but I liked it.'),(2526,5363,'2000-10-07 01:11:21',5161,5367,'maz',0,'I cant remember the name of this kit. Sorry, but it\'s a stunner. The base is courtesy of some lolly sticks.'),(2527,5884,'2001-02-03 14:22:53',5162,5884,'asuka3',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2528,5884,'2001-02-03 14:22:17',3643,5884,'akenminehim',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2529,5884,'2001-02-03 14:21:58',3612,5884,'bellgrem',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2530,5884,'2001-02-03 14:23:25',5163,5884,'linagrem',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2531,5884,'2001-02-03 14:24:40',5164,5884,'sarahgrem',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2532,5884,'2001-02-03 14:22:35',3656,5884,'shampoogrem',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2533,5435,'2000-10-12 05:19:11',4882,5438,'sonfrank',0,'Please check out some of my other gallery entries from the recent past.  Just check \"Painter\" instead of \"KIT\" and then enter name \"Tarr\", then \"Search\".\n I offer my build-up and painting services to fellow collectors and manufacturers. I can be contacted by e-mail at: tarmin8or@parlorcity.com Thank you for your interest. '),(2534,5435,'2000-10-14 00:26:55',5166,5438,'BWFranky2',0,'Please check out some of my other gallery entries from the recent past. Just check \"Painter\" instead of \"KIT\" and then enter name \"Tarr\", then \"Search\". I offer my build-up and painting services to fellow collectors and manufacturers. I can be contacted by e-mail at: tarmin8or@parlorcity.com Thank you for your interest. '),(2535,5435,'2000-10-14 06:24:56',5168,5438,'foxcret',0,'I offer my build-up and painting services to fellow collectors and manufacturers. I can be contacted by e-mail at: tarmin8or@parlorcity.com Thank you for your interest. '),(2537,5237,'2000-10-18 17:13:34',4470,5237,'Aries',0,'I didn\'t like the original paint job so I changed it and the haircut and the weapon'),(2538,5237,'2000-10-18 17:23:46',5170,5237,'arnie',0,'Andrea 54mm white metal kit with a bit of background added'),(2539,5237,'2000-10-18 17:24:48',5169,5237,'buffy',0,'guess who this is'),(2540,5435,'2000-10-20 18:15:21',5171,5438,'wolfy',0,'I offer my award winning, museum quality build-up and painting services to fellow collectors and manufacturers. I can be contacted by e-mail at: tarmin8or@parlorcity.com Thank you for your interest.'),(2541,4864,'2000-11-11 19:41:37',5172,4864,'PLwolfman',0,'Great styrene kit by Polar Lights.\nTree was reposed. \"Even a man who is pure at heart and says his prayers at night, may become\na werewolf when the wolfbane blooms and the autumn moon is bright\"!\nCheck out my website at:\n www.monsterjones.com'),(2542,4864,'2000-11-11 19:49:46',5173,4864,'AuroraWolfman',0,'Classic Aurora Wolfman kit!!! \nI\'ve probably built this one 15 times. \nAdded\ncut doll hair for fur. Visit my monster gallery website at:\nwww.monsterjones.com'),(2545,5884,'2001-02-03 14:24:03',5174,5884,'nukucatgril1',0,'I have started up a resin kit painting service to find out more information pls click on my name to access my web page'),(2610,5559,'2001-07-02 23:47:49',5212,5559,'punkenstein1',0,'Ok guys and gals!!! Punkenstein is here!!! He now comes cast in a translucent green resin and includes a brain, daisies, chains and his very own storage container. Punkenstein retails for $80.00... Dont delay drop me a line for details!\r\n\r\nJohn  \r\nPinkerton FX \r\n  \r\n'),(2549,4953,'2000-11-26 12:34:35',4776,4953,'nos',0,'I decided to liven this kit up by adding some Giant Rats from Games Workshop to the base'),(2550,4953,'2000-11-28 09:10:12',5176,4953,'gor',0,'This was a miscast piece that a friend of mine was \nable to get.  I believe that it\'s from the full \nkit by Taylor Designs of the Silverback Gorilla.\nSince it was missing the lower torso and arms, I\nmade it into a bust.'),(2551,4953,'2000-11-28 09:18:55',5181,4953,'cro',0,'This is a kit by a Company called Tiny Troopers.\nOk, ok so it\'s not the true historical Davey \nCrockett.  It\'s John Wayne as Crockett from the\nMovie, the Alamo, but I think John Wanye\'s as much\na historical figure as Davey was.'),(2552,4953,'2000-11-28 19:21:22',5182,4953,'car',0,'This is a kit done by a friend of mine, Mike Petryzak, of Critical Mass Models, of Cartman from South Park.  It\'s available through Fatman Productions.'),(2553,4953,'2000-11-30 18:47:21',5183,4953,'xbi',0,'This ia a piece done by my friend Mike Petryszak of Critical Mass Models.  It\'s of a character from an independent Comic Book called Agent XBI.  Note the T-Shirt.  I painted it as an X-files T-Shirt.'),(2554,5459,'2000-12-02 18:43:09',5185,5459,'cyborg2',0,'This is a scratch built and one of a kind piece. It is sculpted in mainly promat with some Premo-Sculpey tossed in here and there.'),(2555,4953,'2000-12-03 19:52:52',5186,4953,'Rob',0,'This originally was a pewter display piece, that I got at Toys-R-Us.  I thought that it would look better painted.'),(2556,4953,'2000-12-03 20:03:32',5187,4953,'War',0,'Originally a prepainted display piece.  I didn\'t like the way it was painted, so I cleaned it up and repainted it.'),(2557,4953,'2000-12-04 09:24:18',5188,4953,'nin',0,'This is a Jaguar kit, that I painted.  The construction was straight \nforward.  I intended to paint the face in the style of Kabuki actors\nbut it turned out to look more like a futuristic version of a female\nCrow character.'),(2558,4953,'2000-12-04 09:32:54',5189,4953,'frz',0,'I think this is a kit from Japan by Hasegawa.\nIt\'s Mr. Freeze from the movie Batman and Robin.'),(2581,5999,'2001-01-02 22:08:07',4809,5999,'SlaveLeia',0,'The face was replaced with the one from the Kaiyodo Princess Leia. I thought it looked more like Carrie Fisher than the original'),(2562,5386,'2000-12-06 11:19:42',5192,5386,'carnage',0,'carnage from the marvel series'),(2563,5386,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5190,5386,'morrigan2',0,NULL),(2564,5386,'2000-12-06 11:08:51',5190,5386,'morrigan',0,'Morrigan from Vampire Savior'),(2565,5386,'2000-12-06 11:04:56',5191,5386,'rei3',0,'Ayanami Rei from Evangelion'),(2566,5386,'2000-12-06 10:59:54',5191,5386,'rei',0,'Ayanami Rei from Evangelion'),(2567,5386,'2000-12-06 11:02:23',5191,5386,'rei2',0,'Rei from Evangelion'),(2568,5386,'2001-01-03 11:20:40',5190,5386,'morrigan',0,NULL),(2569,5411,'2000-12-07 11:59:49',5195,5411,'Batbust',0,'Batman bust inspired from the Frank Miller comic \"Dark Knight\".\nPainted with airbrush, only for ther face enamels were used.'),(2570,5411,'2000-12-07 12:05:46',5197,5411,'kobike',0,'This chaos biker is a convertion to represent a fallen spacewolf of the wulfen company.\nPainted using enamels.'),(2571,5411,'2000-12-08 00:27:49',5193,5411,'templar',0,'Painted using enamels'),(2572,5411,'2000-12-08 00:29:51',5196,5411,'gorka',0,'Conversion from the standard plastic kit, I have added several pewter Ork figures...\nPainted using enamels'),(2574,5538,'2001-11-15 04:55:30',5198,5812,'maria2',0,'Maria can be purchased at www.cygenus-studios.com for $145 + $8 shipping.  The kit stands 14\" high and includes 57, resin, styrene, and metal parts.  Detail assembly instructions included.'),(2764,5319,'2001-11-16 12:48:33',4778,5319,'gorehound',0,'Great Kit. needs very little clean up. Excellent detail in the fur and the victim.'),(2575,5237,'2000-12-11 18:05:38',5202,5237,'elric',0,'90mm RAFM white metal kit'),(2576,5237,'2000-12-11 18:07:21',5201,5237,'NEY',0,'Elfin by any other name (even Sol) is still Elfin'),(2577,5237,'2000-12-11 18:07:51',5200,5237,'VERONA',0,'Elfin by any other name (even Sol) is still Elfin'),(2578,5237,'2000-12-11 18:12:29',5199,5237,'TTalienqueen',0,'This was once a Terran Trader kit. It took me a month of concentrated effort to sort it out and produce this. Only ever think of buying this kit when entertaining severe masochistic flagellation tendancies. In other words it\'s crap. '),(2579,4864,'2000-12-16 19:27:41',5203,4864,'Blackie',0,'Two Foot Tall Devonian Terror!! All resin\n Creature from the Black Lagoon with glass eyes!!! For more Creature kits check out my web-gallery:\nwww.monsterjones.com'),(2582,5999,'2001-01-02 22:18:37',4724,5999,'JJEva',0,'My first girl kit'),(2583,6062,'2001-11-08 15:19:24',4971,6062,'satkit01',0,'This beautiful Sailor Saturn model has 22 parts NOT 19, and is made by Kotobukiya. The bows are actually Scarlett Red, my digital camera isn\'t able to capture the red colors correctly.\r\n<p>\r\nIf you want to see pics of some other garage kits I\'ve made or if you are looking for a place to buy built and painted anime models, just go to <a href=http://www.otakuparadise.com/>www.otakuparadise.com</a>. If you already have a model and would like it to be built by somebody with experience you can contact me. I have been building models for clients from around the world since 1997.'),(2584,6062,'2002-07-08 10:42:02',3445,6062,'duo',0,'These 2 models are supposed to be sold together in the same box because they each have half part of the base. They are 1/8 resin models that have been produced by G-Port. Sailor Uranus has 10 parts and Sailor Neptune has 12 parts.\r\n<p>\r\nIf you want to see pics of some other garage kits I\'ve made or if you are looking for a place to buy built and painted anime models, just go to <a href=http://www.otakuparadise.com/>www.otakuparadise.com</a>. If you already have a model and would like it to be built by somebody with experience you can contact me. I have been building models for clients from around the world since 1997 :)'),(2585,6062,'2002-07-03 23:41:04',3445,6062,'samoukit',0,'I know this nakoruru model is not in the good categorie, but no categorie has been made for it yet so I\'m posting it here with my other Sailor Moon models. This was one of my first attempt on a garage kit and my skills have improved a lot since then. I made it around 8 years ago. It had around 30 parts and was produced by G-Port.<p>\r\n\r\nI didn\'t have an airbrush back then and I also didn\'t have any particular technique. If I had to build this same kit again today, it would look a lot more professional than the one you see on the pics below :)<p>\r\n\r\n'),(2604,4863,'2001-01-11 11:34:23',5206,5431,'veronica1',0,'A new Dangerous dream from JJ Models,\r\nVeronica,high quality resin kit, clear resin shoes! Limited Editions 1000pcs.\r\nOrder your copy! www.jjmodels.com and for US resident: www.anotherworlddesigns.com \r\n(censored edition)'),(2605,5329,'2004-02-20 21:35:51',4941,5771,'greenbeholder2',0,'<B>Based on the many eyed Beholder monster from <I>Advanced Dungeons and Dragons</i>. I created this out of various materials I had hanging around.\r\nThe core is a styrofoam ball while the covering is <I>Model Magic</i> by <I>Crayola</i> (neat stuff).  \r\nBase is made of many different materials and depict treasures collected for and by this creature. \r\nDrips of resin simulate drool and slime. Painted in acrylics with a dark wash. <BR>\r\nAbout 2\" across and the base is 4\"x4\".\r\nI plan on producing a small kit similar to this. <BR>\r\n<BR>My others: \r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2407> <IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/greenbeholder_icon.gif alt=\"Baby Green Beholder - 1st one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2347><IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/bluebeholder_icon.gif alt=\"Baby Blue Beholder - 2nd one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2319><img src=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/beholder_icon.gif alt=\"Hatchling Beholder - 3rd one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2326><img src=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/redbeholder_icon.gif alt=\"Red Beholder - 4th one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2605><IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/greenbeholder2_icon.gif alt=\"Green Beholder - 5th one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=3042><IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/mottled_icon.gif alt=\"Mottled Beholder - 6th one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<HR>More info write:<A HREF=mailto:trekist@hotmail.com>trekist@hotmail.com</a><BR>Pics are being updated.'),(2588,5633,'2001-01-09 13:33:41',3952,5633,'robin02',0,'ROBIN:\r\nFabricado por REVELL\r\nEscala: 1/6\r\nMaterial: VINYL\r\n\r\nPintado con aerografo.\r\ntanto el verde de los brazos y piernas como el fucsia del cuerpo estan mezclados con aluminio para lograr el efecto metalizado, luego sobre el cuerpo tiene una capa aguada de magenta para darle un tono mas fuerte ya que el aluminio neutraliza un poco el color.\r\nEl interior de la capa es una mezcla de Tierra Siena y dorado\r\nEste es un kit que se esta tornando dificil de encontrar ya que REVELL dejo de fabricarlo.\r\n'),(2589,5633,'2001-01-09 13:35:10',3952,5633,'robin04',0,''),(2590,5633,'2001-01-09 13:36:12',3952,5633,'robin06',0,''),(2591,5633,'2001-01-09 13:56:11',4396,5633,'robocop01',0,'Aunque no lo crean esta totalmente pintado a pincel.\r\nLo primero que hice fue trabajar la armadura con dos colores al mismo tiempo. un azul metalizado y un lila mezclado con plata. ambos aplicados al mismo tiempo por zonas intercaladas y mezclandolos entre si en el modelo mientras estaban frescos.\r\nUna vez cubierta toda la armadura aplique una capa de laca tornasol aguada para darle reflejos violetas y finalmente una capa de plata aguada para el aspecto metalico.\r\nLuego pinte de negro los guantes, abdomen y cuello aplicandole barniz brillante al negro y finalmente pinte la cara .\r\nEl arma tiene una mezcla de negro y plata con toque de aluminio con pincel seco'),(2592,5633,'2001-01-09 13:56:22',4396,5633,'robocop07',0,'Aunque no lo crean esta totalmente pintado a pincel.\r\nLo primero que hice fue trabajar la armadura con dos colores al mismo tiempo. un azul metalizado y un lila mezclado con plata. ambos aplicados al mismo tiempo por zonas intercaladas y mezclandolos entre si en el modelo mientras estaban frescos.\r\nUna vez cubierta toda la armadura aplique una capa de laca tornasol aguada para darle reflejos violetas y finalmente una capa de plata aguada para el aspecto metalico.\r\nLuego pinte de negro los guantes, abdomen y cuello aplicandole barniz brillante al negro y finalmente pinte la cara .\r\nEl arma tiene una mezcla de negro y plata con toque de aluminio con pincel seco'),(2593,5633,'2001-01-09 14:37:03',4252,5633,'greengoblin05',0,'The first thing that I made with the goblin was to paint the green skin. I began giving a dark green tone to the whole skin and then with the technique of dry paintbrush I applies a green but clearing to stand out the flakes, then with a mixture of green and yellow and always with paintbrush dry, I realce the musculature and finally with yellow I paint it in the way contrary to the drawing of the flakes to stand out the borders of these. As touch end I applies touches of flesh color on the muscles with airbrush (after all blood runs under that green skin!) \r\nPaint the skin first since the technique of dry paintbrush it is enough dirty as for borders it refers so then I cover the imperfections with the magenta of the clothes and stand out the pleats with a clear magenta. \r\nThe eyes were colored with gray and then white in the center to give them more volume finally, after painting the pupil has several layers of brilliant varnish to give him the humid and vitreous aspect. \r\n'),(2594,5633,'2001-01-09 14:38:03',4252,5633,'greengoblin08',0,'The first thing that I made with the goblin was to paint the green skin. I began giving a dark green tone to the whole skin and then with the technique of dry paintbrush I applies a green but clearing to stand out the flakes, then with a mixture of green and yellow and always with paintbrush dry, I realce the musculature and finally with yellow I paint it in the way contrary to the drawing of the flakes to stand out the borders of these. As touch end I applies touches of flesh color on the muscles with airbrush (after all blood runs under that green skin!) \r\nPaint the skin first since the technique of dry paintbrush it is enough dirty as for borders it refers so then I cover the imperfections with the magenta of the clothes and stand out the pleats with a clear magenta. \r\nThe eyes were colored with gray and then white in the center to give them more volume finally, after painting the pupil has several layers of brilliant varnish to give him the humid and vitreous aspect. \r\n'),(2595,5633,'2001-01-09 14:38:13',4251,5633,'greengoblin08',0,'The first thing that I made with the goblin was to paint the green skin. I began giving a dark green tone to the whole skin and then with the technique of dry paintbrush I applies a green but clearing to stand out the flakes, then with a mixture of green and yellow and always with paintbrush dry, I realce the musculature and finally with yellow I pai