h a mixture of green and yellow and always with paintbrush dry, I realce the musculature and finally with yellow I paint it in the way contrary to the drawing of the flakes to stand out the borders of these. As touch end I applies touches of flesh color on the muscles with airbrush (after all blood runs under that green skin!) \r\nPaint the skin first since the technique of dry paintbrush it is enough dirty as for borders it refers so then I cover the imperfections with the magenta of the clothes and stand out the pleats with a clear magenta. \r\nThe eyes were colored with gray and then white in the center to give them more volume finally, after painting the pupil has several layers of brilliant varnish to give him the humid and vitreous aspect. \r\n'),(2598,5633,'2001-01-09 14:38:49',3954,5633,'greengoblin08',0,'The first thing that I made with the goblin was to paint the green skin. I began giving a dark green tone to the whole skin and then with the technique of dry paintbrush I applies a green but clearing to stand out the flakes, then with a mixture of green and yellow and always with paintbrush dry, I realce the musculature and finally with yellow I paint it in the way contrary to the drawing of the flakes to stand out the borders of these. As touch end I applies touches of flesh color on the muscles with airbrush (after all blood runs under that green skin!) \r\nPaint the skin first since the technique of dry paintbrush it is enough dirty as for borders it refers so then I cover the imperfections with the magenta of the clothes and stand out the pleats with a clear magenta. \r\nThe eyes were colored with gray and then white in the center to give them more volume finally, after painting the pupil has several layers of brilliant varnish to give him the humid and vitreous aspect. \r\n'),(2599,5633,'2001-01-09 15:42:55',3504,5633,'frankestein5',0,''),(2600,5633,'2001-01-09 15:05:38',5205,5633,'frankestein5',0,''),(2601,5633,'2001-01-09 16:21:29',4019,5633,'speede