cture from the 2nd edition eldar codex.'),(2895,5411,'2002-09-04 08:44:53',5422,5411,'eldarhawk',0,''),(2896,5411,'2002-09-04 08:47:05',5423,5411,'elves',0,''),(2897,5411,'2002-09-04 08:50:05',5424,5411,'escher',0,'I have added the teddy bear to this figure...'),(2898,5411,'2002-09-04 08:59:37',5425,5411,'fam1',0,'Funny 10mm figures...'),(2655,5344,'2001-03-25 21:04:57',3453,5369,'Medusa1',0,''),(2656,5884,'2001-03-31 19:34:12',5233,5884,'kasumigrem',0,'Please visit my web site to find out about my painting service and more detailed pictures of my other kits\r\n<A HREF=\"http://www3.ns.sympatico.ca/dawn.plante/\"><b> CLICK HERE</B></A>.<P>\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(2657,4921,'2001-04-05 13:50:54',5235,4921,'phantom2',0,'I\'ve been doing kits for awhile now, and this one is one of the best I\'ve ever seen.  I drilled out the eye and replaced it with a life-like one I picked up from an online FX supply store.  It was painted with brushes only with water-based paint.  Contact me at jeffjl98@yahoo.com for more info.\r\n'),(2658,5665,'2004-01-20 14:41:27',5558,5665,'igor',0,'Igor from John Kovalic\'s Dork Tower'),(2662,5435,'2001-07-10 05:49:22',5246,5438,'HHUNTER',0,'We customized a bit by adding the skull to the left hand and spear in right,...just for spice and giggles.\r\nPlease visit HEAVY D\'s web site at:\r\nwww.parlorcity.com/dscreations/\r\nThank you!!!'),(2663,5435,'2001-07-10 05:50:29',5246,5438,'DHUNTER',0,'Please visit our web site for more commissioned museum quality build-ups at:\r\nwww.parlorcity.com/dscreations/\r\nThanks!'),(2680,6254,'2001-08-01 07:55:55',5263,6254,'kitblu2gr',0,'First kit in a five part series called \"Angels\".  The kit was not built to a specific scale, however, she is about 5\" from knee to head and rests on a 5\"x7\" oval wood base. The clear resin water pieces give it that truly realistic feel.  ANGEL BATH has a total of 8 pieces including the wood base. For ordering, shipping, and payment information contact hardycole@email.msn.com'),(2665,6102,'2001-07-10 12:14:46',5249,6102,'wolf',0,'Territorial: Sculpted out of sculpey and painted with acrylics. Werewolf is removable from base.'),(2666,6102,'2001-07-10 12:19:29',5250,6102,'toad',0,'Warrior Toad: Sculpted out of white clay and painted with acrylics. removes from base.'),(2667,6128,'2001-07-10 11:36:16',5240,6243,'Censtill',0,' Of all the strange creatures encountered on the Sinbad voyages, the Centaur was the most brutal.  \r\n Idolized by a primitive tribe in its homeland, it was considered to be a God; The God of the Single Eye.\r\n However, a sailor\'s dagger, driven deep into the neck makes mortality all too real, even to a God.'),(2668,6128,'2001-07-10 11:22:11',5239,6243,'TrogStill',0,' Of the many creatures encountered on Sinbad\'s famous voyages, the Troglodyte was the most gentle.\r\n Being an ancestor of man, this strange creature reflected the passive side of humanity.\r\n However, the deep slash of giant cat claws will bring out the animal, even in the gentlest of creatures.'),(2669,6128,'2001-07-10 11:23:35',5238,6243,'CyStill',0,'After finding the drowned remains of Sinbad washed ashore, is this savage beast displaying sorrow over the loss of a respected opponent, or merely disgust over a missed meal?'),(2670,6102,'2001-07-10 11:21:48',5251,6102,'nuclear',0,'MP-Plutonium Blaster: is just a mock up piece, for display or prop.\r\nThe power pack is a 17\" long honda gas tank from a lawn mower, with found objects attached.The gun it self is an old toy gun I had laying around, then I modified and retooled it, adding a lot of found objects, including a Darth Vader light saber. The gun its self measures 20\" long. Most of the found objects are from an F-16 cockpit.The ball to the right of the power pack (Giant Marble) is to represent the nuclear core that can be placed in the power pack. The cable around that, connects from one end of the gun, and the other to the power pack. To the left of the gun and power pack is a shoulder strap, wich connects to the power pack. The end of the barrel light\'s up. (Nuclear Green).\r\n'),(2671,6102,'2001-07-10 12:17:31',5252,6102,'dino',0,'Saddle Up: Sculpted out of sculpey and painted with acrylics. All accessories are removable to reveal just the dinosaur. Dinosaur is Removable from base.'),(2672,6102,'2001-07-10 11:45:37',5254,6102,'quill',0,'Quill the Stealth Archer: Sculpted out of sculpey and painted with arylics. measures 9\" with base. \r\n'),(2679,5559,'2001-09-26 23:23:47',5212,5559,'punkenstein3',0,'New web site is up and running!!!'),(2678,6127,'2001-07-24 21:26:14',5261,6268,'clint',0,'This kit has a dead on likeness to Clint Eastwood.'),(2677,6102,'2001-07-10 12:27:29',5255,6102,'frank',0,'Karloffs Monster: with permission from Sara Karloff, I sculpted this bust of the monster. It stands 11 1/2\" with out base. Sculpted out of white clay and painted with acrylics. Neck bolts are from the ends of two pen torches.\r\n\r\n'),(2681,6254,'2001-08-01 07:42:36',5263,6254,'kitblu3gr',0,'Another cool angle on a front yard scene we would all love to see.'),(2693,6127,'2001-07-24 21:24:45',5276,6268,'GLAD',0,'10 pieces including base '),(2683,5571,'2001-07-12 20:48:30',5267,5571,'retrobat',0,'For more model pics and detailed build-up descriptions, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS @ www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html (Click on my name for direct link)'),(2697,6152,'2001-07-31 19:14:06',5302,6152,'kong2',0,'Interested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2699,6152,'2001-07-31 18:57:56',3884,6152,'saucerman',0,'Billiken again produced an incredible kit - posability with hidden joints is a must for us modelers who want to... (I almost said Play with them!)... Reposition them.\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com\r\n\r\n'),(2687,6175,'2001-09-18 19:33:23',3495,6175,'batmanfull',0,'To view this kit in greater detail go here\r\nhttp://hills.ccsf.cc.ca.us/~gfaust01/'),(2688,6127,'2001-07-12 21:25:33',5261,6268,'PICS',0,'20 pieces of resin the likeness to clint is right on.'),(2689,6175,'2001-09-18 19:35:35',3499,6151,'catfull',0,'To view this kit in greater detail go here\r\nhttp://hills.ccsf.cc.ca.us/~gfaust01/'),(2690,6175,'2001-09-18 19:34:26',3530,6175,'wfull',0,'To view this kit in greater detail go here\r\nhttp://hills.ccsf.cc.ca.us/~gfaust01/'),(2698,6152,'2001-07-31 18:54:16',4292,6152,'baragon',0,'I will \"Bring Your Kit To Life\" - email me @ tomcabarts@aol.com for details - or visit my ebay store at:http://www.ebaystores.com/tomcabsfantasticartshop'),(2694,6254,'2001-07-13 21:20:08',5263,6254,'conten2grem',0,'Wanted to giva a good look at the kit contents.  To get an idea of size, the oval wood base measures 5\"x7\".'),(2695,6259,'2001-07-17 17:23:09',5277,6259,'alien',0,''),(2696,6259,'2001-07-17 17:22:23',5277,6259,'alien2',0,''),(2700,6152,'2001-07-31 19:09:23',3966,6152,'metalutant',0,'Tsukuda\'s Mutant is in scale with the little BEM Saucer Man from Billiken. They make a great team, but for all that brain tissue, they\'re not too bright.\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2701,6152,'2001-07-31 19:01:08',3885,6152,'teenwolf',0,'This was the film I picked to introduce my son to the 50\'s B flix. The scene after the party in the woods scared the CRAP outta him and now I watch them alone again....\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2702,6152,'2001-07-31 19:05:07',3887,6152,'teenfrank',0,'The model is much better than the movie! \r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com '),(2703,6152,'2001-07-31 19:01:55',3453,6152,'medusagreencu',0,'Interested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2704,4863,'2001-07-31 08:33:21',5281,5431,'valerie1',0,'Amazing model with real mirror included!\r\nGreat Job!'),(2705,4921,'2001-07-31 15:11:51',5282,4921,'phantom2',0,'I drilled out the right eye socket and replaced it with a glass eyeball.  The kit was painted with water colors and brushes only.  Contact me at jeffjl98@yahoo.com for more info.'),(2706,6152,'2001-07-31 19:07:46',5283,6152,'dragon1',0,'Not all Red Dragons are Red! This one I found while exploring caves in Northwest Georgia. He was quite cranky about having his picture taken. I won his trust with some jerky and nuts I had in my pouch and we sat and talked for hours!\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2707,6152,'2001-07-31 18:58:57',4262,6152,'thing',0,'I had to know what color he was. I had traveled hundreds of miles to the North Pole to find out... Finally I found him after weeks of searching. He has a blue atomic glow which is augmented by the chill -- he\'s actually a very sensitive Thing!                                     Interested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2708,6152,'2001-07-31 18:55:09',5295,6152,'colossy',0,'The trip back to 1958 in my Time Machine had left me groggy -- I was seeing phantoms...(and Colossal Beasts). I was on a mission to study the numerous irradiated Monsters which roamed the countryside in the fifties so I could accurately depict their colors for you as you sit there, all safe and sound behind your computer screen. I hope you appreciate this....I will \"Bring Your Kit To Life\" - email me @ tomcabarts@aol.com for details - or visit my ebay store at:http://www.ebaystores.com/tomcabsfantasticartshop'),(2709,6152,'2001-07-31 19:00:35',5301,6152,'empyrian',0,'Finally - here was my second chance! Life had lost all it\'s meaning since the Control Voice had canceled my favorite show...\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com\r\n\r\n'),(2710,6152,'2001-07-31 18:57:06',5293,6152,'mole',0,'As my eyes grew accustomed to the light I could barely make the shape of a figure ambling towards me all hunched over... suddenly I could see as he reached for me - he had a huge Mole right in the middle of... AAAAAHHHHHH!!!   \r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2711,6152,'2001-07-31 19:08:49',4703,6152,'gillman',0,'What a beautiful day it had turned into here on the Amazon. Our captain seems a little disturbed - I really don\'t think he knows where he\'s going! We\'ve anchored here at this dead end little lagoon where the water is so deep as to appear -- not really bluegreen anymore, but black... What\'s that strange breathing sound? It\'s coming from that grotto right over here by the AAAAAAAUGH!!!!\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2712,6152,'2001-07-31 19:10:29',5292,6152,'reaper',0,'Well... The breaths are... becoming more dif.. dif... difficult... I... Oh! Here he his now! Hey Bud! HowYa Doooin? (plop!)\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2713,6152,'2001-07-31 19:07:07',5291,6152,'hydra',0,'Hey Guys! Look over here! This looks new! I didn\'t see this portal on the Travel Brochure... Let\'s check it out--\r\nWHOOOPS! WhOA! What the...? The ruins ain\'t ruined anymore! I don\'t think we\'re in modern Greece no more, fellas... Fellas? EEEYIKES!!!!\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2714,6152,'2001-07-31 19:06:21',5294,6152,'digmole1',0,'Hey look, Thelma! Here\'s another danged gopher hole! Lemme git my trap. You stay right there so\'s ah don\' lose the danged thang... OK Thelma! Ah\'m ready! Thelma? THELLLLMA!!!\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com\r\n\r\n'),(2715,6152,'2001-07-31 19:08:15',5300,6152,'boris',0,'Happy Valentines Day, Elsa!  \r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2716,6152,'2001-07-31 19:09:51',5299,6152,'bigheadaliens',0,'It was a battle of the brains as the Intergalactically famous Spacecop Bugsy Rawzwell finally nabbed the Notoriously Villainous Veinyhead McNoggin. \r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2717,6152,'2001-07-31 19:02:33',5298,6152,'bela',0,'You are getting veeerrry SSlleeepy... Coooome to Meeee, my sweet Pizza Delivery Man of the Night!\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2718,6152,'2001-07-31 19:04:11',5297,6152,'mollusk',0,'Hope everybody likes Escargot!\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2719,6152,'2001-07-31 19:03:22',5296,6152,'behemoth',0,'\"Watch it!! Don\'t get drool on my new Studebaker!\"\r\n\r\nInterested in a buildup service? Email me at tomcabarts@aol.com'),(2720,6107,'2001-08-02 13:35:40',5303,6107,'Ghost',0,'Although this kit came pre-assembled and painted, I\'m the maniac who put the time and care into replacing the original boring white wires with glowing E.L.  Not a simple task.  Although the paint job it came with was really nice in most areas it was absolutely horrible in all the flesh zones so I went in and did a fair amount of shading and retouching.  Now they are perfect.  \r\n\r\nI\'m hoping that some other builders will see this and jump on the E.L. bandwagon.  Hmmmmm, lightsabers that look and glow like lightsabers, instrument panels?  Lot\'s of posibilities.\r\n\r\nCheck out my web page for better pictures.  Also, if you want to know where to get E.L. wire then try Coolight.com'),(2721,6127,'2001-10-30 19:53:34',5304,6268,'MAXPICS',0,'Sculpted by Brett Coronado Mad Max is now available www.resin_image.com\r\n'),(2722,6127,'2001-10-30 19:40:15',5304,6268,'MAXPICS',0,'Sculpted by Brett Coronado Available now from Resin-Image\r\nwww.resin_image.com\r\n'),(2723,4863,'2001-08-08 06:20:34',5306,5431,'daminar1',0,''),(2724,4863,'2001-08-08 06:22:54',5306,5431,'Daminar1',0,''),(2725,5435,'2001-08-16 03:46:37',5308,5438,'fxpredgrem',0,'Do you have one of these in the \"raw\" and want it to look like this?\r\nVisit my web site (HEAVY D\'s) to find out how at:\r\nwww.parlorcity.com/dscreations/\r\nThanks!'),(2726,5557,'2001-08-26 06:19:26',5267,5571,'',0,''),(2727,5557,'2001-08-26 06:41:10',5309,5557,'bat1',0,'Very imposing model kit. 2 pieces, easily built and painted!'),(2728,5557,'2001-08-26 06:54:05',5310,5557,'jimh4',0,'A truly beautiful bust, with lots of different painting challenges!'),(2729,5557,'2001-08-26 07:11:16',3489,5557,'prd',0,'Nicely detailed kit! Including the 43 seperate dreadlocks! Ugh!'),(2730,5557,'2001-08-26 07:18:55',5311,5557,'bwa07',0,'A comic book classic!! Flashback to the Aurora days!'),(2731,5557,'2001-08-26 07:21:48',5311,122,'',0,''),(2732,5571,'2001-08-27 18:57:41',5312,5571,'revellfrank3',0,'For a detailed description of the build-up and painting techniques used on this model, visit HEROES, VILLAINS & MONSTERS at www.geocities.com/christopher_saghy/index.html  (Click my name at the top of this page for a direct link.)\r\n'),(2733,6175,'2001-09-18 19:31:26',4059,6175,'bgfull',0,'To view this kit in greater detail go here \r\nhttp://hills.ccsf.cc.ca.us/~gfaust01/'),(2735,6175,'2001-09-18 19:28:49',3494,6175,'bluebat',0,'To see more of this kit in greater detail go here\r\nhttp://hills.ccsf.cc.ca.us/~gfaust01/'),(2736,6243,'2001-11-01 08:06:28',5316,6243,'newcal',0,'\"He will become abhorrent to human sight,\r\nHe will be shunned and forced to live as an outcast in the swamps and marshes.\r\nHe will be transformed to a mortal mockery, \r\na shameful mark of his vile cruelty...\"'),(2737,5237,'2001-11-05 17:20:23',5320,5237,'chariot1',0,'Andrea Models 90mm white metal. This kit is unbelievable in it\'s detail'),(2738,5237,'2001-11-05 17:21:52',5321,5237,'key',0,'As you can see I\'ve added a few more bits of old car'),(2739,5237,'2001-11-05 17:26:50',5318,5237,'vampwng',0,'Wonderfull kit. If you don\'t bother with the innane bat nipple covers'),(2740,5237,'2001-11-05 17:09:01',5325,5237,'E',0,''),(2741,5237,'2001-11-05 17:10:13',5324,5237,'bdandy',0,'Changed the face a bit and added wings on this one.'),(2742,5237,'2001-11-05 17:29:49',5323,5237,'alitaba',0,'The base is the remmenants of my automatic transmission'),(2743,6288,'2001-11-10 10:04:03',4800,149,'',0,''),(2745,6294,'2004-01-28 08:50:11',5330,6361,'Super',0,''),(2746,6288,'2001-11-10 09:41:17',4800,149,'',0,''),(2747,6288,'2001-11-10 09:37:40',5331,6288,'fakk2',0,''),(2748,6288,'2001-11-10 10:03:07',5332,6288,'ALIEN',0,''),(2749,6288,'2002-10-10 12:57:22',5330,6602,'Super',0,''),(2750,6288,'2002-10-10 12:58:22',5334,6602,'wolverine',0,''),(2751,6288,'2001-11-11 03:20:33',4800,149,'',0,''),(2752,6288,'2001-11-11 03:13:10',5336,6288,'Roge',0,''),(2753,6288,'2002-04-07 04:32:28',5335,6476,'Storm',0,''),(2754,6288,'2002-10-10 12:57:38',5330,6602,'Super2',0,''),(2755,6288,'2002-10-10 12:58:53',5334,6602,'wolverine2',0,''),(2756,5319,'2001-11-11 16:09:45',4778,149,'gorehound',0,''),(2757,6340,'2001-11-12 15:06:17',5337,6340,'1',0,'I am happy to present you my latest work, Ha Ri Ken Polimar - techno polymer suit. This figure is a complete redesign of a long time ago animation hero, created by Tatsunoko Production, Japan, in the early eighties. You can see some images at the bottom of this article.\r\n\r\nIt\'s name, Polimar, comes from the world of plastic materials: a polymer is a material made of different plastic molecules linked together. His costume can change shape ant turn who wears it into a flying machine, a tank and a racing car, so I guess the name was right, after all.\r\nWhat about the Ha Ri Ken? Oh, well, here in Italy we used to call him Hurricane Polimar, since Ha-Ri-Ken meant nothing to us, and the name \"hurricane\" fit the character enough.\r\nBut this was wrong, at least partially.\r\nThe Japanese name was made of three ideograms and a single word, \"polima\" that was the Japanese way of writing the English\"polimer\".\r\nThe three ideograms were Ha, Ri, Ken, and they should mean something like \"exploding punch attack\" (I\'m still studying Japanese, so I could be completely wrong).Maybe who gave him this name liked that it sounded as Hurricane, but we\'ll never know.\r\nIn my personal version, I added \"techno polymer suit\" because the suit he now wears is an evolution of the one he used years ago. This polymer does not just change shape, but it melts and reticulate into the skin, creating a special support for helping the wearer to stand shocks.When I was seven or eight, this character was very popular between kids, and most people still remember him. I didn\'t like it very much, maybe I was too young.\r\nLately, I rediscovered this character, and I was so fascinated by his blood red suit that I decided to make a sculpture of him in my own style.\r\n\r\nI studied plastic materials at university, and I thought that a scientific explanation to Polimar suit could have been the fusion of flesh and plastic.Then I tried to imagine how the suit could be shaped. The polimer needed to be an inteligent material, otherwise it could not adapt to any body characteristics, and I brought this to the extreme consequences: the suit has not a defined shape, it changes any time melting into skin and muscles. Only few parts keep a defined shape: hands, breast, elm and wings. \r\nI studied very carefully the position and weight of the model, because i wanted it to be very dynamic and look like it was coming down very quickly to the ground. I obtained a good effect balncing the body with a very small but heavy wooden base. \r\nI also wanted minimal junction points between the base and the body, but the position and the weight gave me a lot of problems. The single glued foot was not enough for keeping the model up, so I had to put a very long and thick metal wire inside the left leg, starting near the heel and ending deep down into the wooden base. I used a giutar metal string to bond the wire to the metal skeleton, and finally I covered it with the sculpting clay. \r\n\r\nThe model now is firmly attached to the base, and quite no risk of falling because of unbalance, since the breaking concrete base is made of plaster, hard and heavy.The wings are made of slightly curved plasticard sheet, while the seal on the breast is made of carefully hand-cutted brass foil.\r\nPainting was completely done in acrylic colors, as ever, but I also used Tamiya clear red paint to obtain the shiny, muscle-like areas and the front of the helmet.\r\nAirbrush was used fro covering big areas, but any strip of the suit was then refined alone to get anyone different from others\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n'),(2758,5201,'2001-11-12 15:18:59',5329,5251,'blade.jpeg',0,'painted using humbrol enamels'),(2759,5201,'2001-11-12 15:34:29',5327,5251,'superman.jpg',0,'I love this charcter, 50s style superman'),(2760,6351,'2001-11-14 16:57:04',4796,6351,'Gwen1',0,'Sorry Mr. James, but I never did like guinevere. I rebaptized mine Vivian, the lady  of the lake, Guardian of Excalibur. Not being a fan of wigs, I replaced the silky blond hair with some kind of a golden coiffe.'),(2761,6351,'2001-11-14 16:58:05',4796,6351,'Gwen2',0,'Sorry Mr. James, but I never did like guinevere. I rebaptized mine Vivian, the lady  of the lake, Guardian of Excalibur. Not being a fan of wigs, I replaced the silky blond hair with some kind of a golden coiffe.'),(2762,6351,'2001-11-21 17:38:18',3248,6351,'Bride1',0,''),(2763,6351,'2001-11-14 16:53:36',3248,6351,'Bride2',0,''),(2765,5319,'2001-11-16 12:49:11',4778,5319,'gorehound',0,'Great Kit. needs very little clean up. Excellent detail in the fur and the victim.'),(2766,5319,'2001-11-16 12:49:37',4778,5319,'Gorehound',0,'Great Kit. needs very little clean up. Excellent detail in the fur and the victim.'),(2767,5319,'2001-11-16 12:52:11',4778,5319,'Gorehound',0,'Great Kit. needs very little clean up. Excellent detail in the fur and the victim.'),(2768,5435,'2001-11-21 00:07:23',5308,5438,'orngglow',0,'The shoulder canon was out for repair in this shot. :)!'),(2769,6361,'2002-08-28 09:45:53',5341,6476,'lurz',0,'http://www.wendygital.com/ohmygod'),(2770,6361,'2002-10-10 13:00:16',5340,6571,'batman2',0,'http://www.wendygital.com/ohmygod'),(2772,6361,'2002-10-10 13:00:27',5