looks great when its finished.  '),(2786,6377,'2001-12-12 22:45:42',3804,6377,'PredatorResin',0,'I love the way the Predator is standing in this kit...hes just killed an Alien that is still clutching the Predator\'s ankle!  Nice detail and one of the best poses for a Predator kit!'),(2787,6377,'2001-12-12 23:34:48',3489,6377,'PredatorHalcyon',0,'This kit is just a plain plastic model and a pain in the ass to pu together!  All the dreads had to be painted on individually (painstaking) and its very fragile.  It looks neat, but I would never make another one!'),(2788,6377,'2001-12-12 23:36:20',3517,6377,'Steel',0,'I\'m a big fan of anything Superman, so this vinyl kit was a treat to put together and paint.  Great pose too!'),(2789,6377,'2001-12-12 23:38:12',3804,6377,'Predatorunknown',0,'This is a true \"garage\" kit...I have no idea who made it or where it came from, but it looks cool!  Its about 3-4 inches wide, but its still cool!'),(2790,6377,'2001-12-12 23:41:46',3272,6377,'PredatorBilliken',0,'This was such a sweet kit to put together.  There are 3 alternatives to the head...you can have the mouth closed, open, or you can put the mask on.  One my favorite vinyl kits!'),(2791,6391,'2004-01-20 14:11:55',5352,6391,'image',0,'This 13.5\" polyresin sculpture is what is commonly called \"The Grey\". it is a fine quality item and comes packaged in a gloss black box and custom foam. Based on eyewitness accounts. It is available from http://www.realalien.com'),(3041,6817,'2004-01-30 17:08:42',5563,6817,'Gallows1',0,'This is my first attempt at building and painting a garage kit'),(2793,5435,'2001-12-19 08:57:54',5353,5438,'grembount',0,'O.K. boys!  Is this what everyone\'s been lookin\' for?  Well here he is,...freshly \"harvested\" from the still warm and steamy corpse.  So NOW,...where do I collect my BOUNTY MONEY???????\r\n\r\nHelmet/Mask was designed and produced by Steven Alford, \"the hivemaster\"!\r\nYou can find his unique Predator mask designs on E-BAY!\r\n'),(2794,5435,'2001-12-19 08:57:04',5354,5438,'profbount',0,'This custom Predator had no problem finding America\'s most wanted S.O.B. Piece of S---!\r\nWe just need to know how to spell the name on the Bounty Hunter\'s check!\r\n\r\nHelmet/Mask was designed and produced by Steven Alford, \"The Hivemaster\"!\r\nYou can find his unique Predator mask designs on E-BAY!'),(2795,6243,'2001-12-27 12:31:05',5356,6243,'Eyedio',0,'A dead on version of this massive beast!'),(2796,6243,'2001-12-27 12:52:25',5355,6243,'Ancclose',0,''),(2797,6243,'2001-12-27 12:31:39',5356,6243,'EyeCentaurfull',0,''),(2798,6243,'2001-12-27 12:32:07',5356,6243,'CentWaist',0,''),(2799,6243,'2001-12-27 12:32:34',5356,6243,'EyeNative',0,''),(2800,6243,'2001-12-27 12:33:23',5355,6243,'Ancestorclose',0,''),(2801,6243,'2001-12-27 12:33:51',5355,6243,'Ancestorfront',0,''),(2802,6243,'2001-12-26 21:40:51',5355,6243,'ancestor',0,''),(2805,5569,'2001-12-29 11:19:09',5359,81,'Igor',0,'BudgiesKits Present Igor'),(2806,5569,'2001-12-29 11:19:45',5357,81,'Wishmaster3',0,'BudgiesKits Present Wishmaster'),(2807,5569,'2001-12-29 11:20:26',5358,81,'Ollie1',0,'BudgiesKits Present The Curse of The Werewolf Deform'),(2808,5237,'2002-01-04 18:30:10',5361,5237,'norm',0,'Andrea 120 mm scale'),(2809,5237,'2002-01-04 18:24:54',5360,5237,'CLD',0,''),(2810,5237,'2002-01-04 18:25:15',3923,5237,'nina1',0,''),(2811,5237,'2002-01-04 18:27:15',5362,5237,'predhead',0,''),(2812,4863,'2002-01-10 12:28:35',5363,5431,'sabrina1',0,''),(2813,5363,'2002-01-10 23:42:32',5161,255,'',0,''),(2814,5363,'2002-01-10 23:51:25',5370,5367,'yama',0,'A nice kit I received for my birthday.'),(2815,5363,'2002-01-10 23:52:55',5369,5367,'tomb',0,'One of the worst kits I ever bought, the lesson to be learned here is look in the box because the picture on the outside might not be an exact match!!!'),(2816,5363,'2002-01-10 23:54:06',5368,5367,'sdheroes',0,'A nice set of 3 Super Deformed figures that come in about 3 varieties.'),(2817,5363,'2002-01-10 23:55:22',5367,5367,'mean',0,'I added a few bits to this like screws from an old watch, This kit cost £1.99 from a toy shop in Basildon!'),(2818,5363,'2002-01-10 23:57:02',5366,5367,'girl',0,'I\'m sorry I cant remember what she\'s called.'),(2819,5363,'2002-01-10 23:58:18',5365,5367,'firia',0,'The line work on the armour took ages and I almost ruined it when I applied the varnish and it started to run!!!'),(2820,5363,'2002-01-10 23:59:33',5364,5367,'apc',0,'A desert storm version of the aliens kit. I still like John Pilkingtons though, a favouite contributor of mine.'),(2821,4863,'2002-01-12 13:56:18',5371,5431,'Sophie1',0,''),(2822,5547,'2002-01-14 14:54:51',4872,5547,'',0,''),(2823,6387,'2004-01-20 14:13:28',5372,149,'gremach',0,'Hellga 6\"120mm sculpture by Nexus Sculpture'),(2827,5764,'2002-01-30 11:28:39',4970,5764,'KONGSACRIFICE',0,'Sculpted by Jim Davidson, solid resin cast kit, 11\" tall, $150.00'),(2828,5764,'2002-01-30 11:04:52',4970,5764,'Kongsacrifice_icon',0,''),(2829,5764,'2002-01-30 11:22:04',4970,5764,'Sacrifice_icon.gif',0,''),(2830,5764,'2002-01-30 12:15:31',5373,5764,'RHEDO1',0,''),(2831,5764,'2002-01-30 12:30:27',5374,5764,'MED4',0,''),(2832,5764,'2002-01-30 12:57:32',5375,5764,'Kong2B',0,''),(2833,6291,'2004-01-20 14:21:17',3919,6291,'Ckaren',0,''),(2834,5551,'2002-02-02 05:31:43',5376,5551,'Bio2',0,''),(2835,6418,'2002-02-03 12:32:19',5377,6418,'Smilodonfatalis',0,'Smilodon fatalis, the infamous saber-tooth cat of the last Ice Age America is a new resin model produced by Paleocraft. The model is in 1/10 scale and part of a new 6 piece series featuring prehistoric saber-tooth predators. The saber-tooth series also includes a Megantereon cultridens, Machairodus giganteus, Barbourofelis fricki, homotherium latidens and the marsupial Thylacosmilus atrox. The Smilodon model is a one piece cast and comes with a beveled pine base for display. For more information about the Smilodon or others in the saber-tooth series please visit the Paleocraft website at : http://www.paleocraft.com'),(2836,5999,'2002-02-03 22:13:22',5298,5999,'JanusDracula',0,'Acrylics and Oils\r\n'),(2837,6414,'2002-02-04 16:57:53',3725,6414,'chewbacca',0,''),(2838,6414,'2002-02-04 17:00:57',3725,6414,'chewbacca',0,''),(2839,6414,'2002-02-04 17:12:20',5378,6414,'hansolo',0,''),(2840,6414,'2002-02-04 17:18:17',3739,6414,'yoda',0,''),(2841,6414,'2002-02-04 17:51:42',4846,6414,'c3po',0,''),(2842,6414,'2002-02-04 18:00:37',5379,6414,'darthvader',0,''),(2843,6414,'2002-02-04 18:12:06',4656,6414,'stormtrooper',0,''),(2844,5999,'2002-02-05 16:20:04',4150,5999,'grinch',0,'This is my sister\'s Christmas present for 2001. \r\n'),(2845,6252,'2002-02-11 23:36:17',5380,6380,'monkey',0,'Monkey magic...... Monkey magic...\r\nMonkey magic...... oooohhhhhooo!!!'),(2846,5933,'2002-02-24 14:13:24',5381,5927,'crissy0.jpg',0,'This kit is a tribute to Jaws. It features the female swimmer in the opening scene. Kit contains 2 resin pieces, one is the translucent green water base and the other is the flesh colored resin figure. finished size is 9 1/2\" in length,7 1/2\" wide and 4\" high.'),(2847,5323,'2002-02-27 17:43:45',3240,5323,'creature',0,'Monogram reissue of the original, and now\r\nclassic, Aurora Creature from the Black Lagoon styrene\r\nkit. This version got a major face-lift\r\nwith Posthumous Productions\' resin\r\nreplacement head sculpted by the talented\r\nDavid Grant. Kit was finished with Liquitex\r\nand Testors acrylics, artist oils and pastels. Basecoat\r\nand additional shading were applied with an Iwata HP-B.\r\n\r\n'),(2848,5323,'2002-02-27 15:39:57',4577,5323,'phantom',0,'Another standout kit in Geometric Design\'s\r\nline of classic monster busts - beautiful sculpture by Tim Bruckner and squeaky-clean castings by Mark Brokaw. The Phantom\r\nwas finished with Freak Flex, Liquitex, and\r\nTestors acrylics, artist oils and pastels.\r\nFleshtones and shading effects applied with an Iwata HP-B.'),(2849,5619,'2002-03-03 20:42:18',5382,5713,'Witch',0,''),(2850,5619,'2002-03-03 20:35:58',5382,5713,'Witch',0,''),(2851,5619,'2002-03-03 20:34:25',5382,5713,'Witch',0,''),(2852,6243,'2002-03-05 14:50:21',5383,6243,'closemoon',0,'1976 KING KONG resin model.  A huge resin model that is a very accurate depiction of the horrific sacrifice of Dwan to the massive prehistoric ape.  Kit includes KONG/Dwan, stone alter, and Kong base. '),(2853,6243,'2002-03-13 15:21:54',5383,6243,'FMWStraight',0,'The Giant Prehistoric ape accepts his \"gift\" from the natives!  \"Full Moon Wedding\" from Burroughs Model Works!!!!!!'),(2854,6243,'2002-03-13 15:22:53',5383,6243,'FMWLeft',0,'The horrific sacrificial ceremony of the 1976 KING KONG. '),(2855,5411,'2002-04-05 07:19:49',3752,5411,'',0,''),(2856,5411,'2002-04-05 07:19:17',3752,5411,'C:\\Mes documents\\perso\\images\\images_gremlins\\alex',0,'My second kit using an airbrush. Details added using enamels'),(2857,6473,'2002-04-22 15:24:58',3213,6473,'',0,''),(2858,6470,'2002-04-11 17:24:36',4214,6470,'',0,''),(2859,6470,'2002-04-11 17:29:15',4214,6470,'',0,'This was my first model kit ever and I personally think I did a decent job on it. Used black washes and a creme color for the skin and black with silver for the armor. And for the blood, I mixed a LOT of fluorescent yellow with a little bit of fluorescent green\r\n\r\n<img src=\"http://www.villagephotos.com/pubimage.asp?id_=206703\" width=320 height=224 >'),(2912,5411,'2002-09-06 07:50:11',5438,5411,'supermanbust',0,''),(2913,5411,'2002-09-06 07:54:12',5439,5411,'DareDevilbust',0,'I repainted the face of this pre-paint bust and add some highlights there and there...'),(2914,5411,'2002-09-06 07:56:46',5440,5411,'maximus',0,''),(2915,5411,'2002-09-06 08:09:07',5441,5411,'napo',0,''),(2916,5411,'2002-09-06 08:13:02',5442,5411,'norman',0,''),(2917,5411,'2002-09-06 08:18:49',5443,5411,'OffH',0,''),(2918,5411,'2002-09-06 08:22:43',5444,5411,'rob',0,''),(2919,5350,'2002-09-07 11:31:43',5393,5702,'Chained.jpg',0,''),(2920,5350,'2002-09-07 11:41:23',5393,5702,'Chained',0,''),(3042,5329,'2004-02-20 21:38:57',4941,5771,'mottled',0,'<B>Based on the many eyed Beholder monster from <font color=red>Advanced Dungeons and Dragons</font>. I created this out of various materials I had hanging around.\r\nThe core is a styrofoam ball while the covering is <font color=blue>Model Magic</font> by <font color=green>Crayola</font> (neat stuff).  \r\nBase is made of many different materials and depict treasures collected for and by this creature. \r\nDrips of resin simulate drool and slime. Painted in acrylics with a dark wash. <BR>\r\nAbout 3\" across and the base is 4\"x4\".\r\nI plan on producing a small kit similar to this. <BR>\r\n<BR>My others: \r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2407> <IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/greenbeholder_icon.gif alt=\"Baby Green Beholder - 1st one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2347><IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/bluebeholder_icon.gif alt=\"Baby Blue Beholder - 2nd one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2319><img src=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/beholder_icon.gif alt=\"Hatchling Beholder - 3rd one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2326><img src=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/redbeholder_icon.gif alt=\"Red Beholder - 4th one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=2605><IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/greenbeholder2_icon.gif alt=\"Green Beholder - 5th one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<A HREF=http://www.gremlins.com/garage/galleryView.jsp?buildupUid=3042><IMG SRC=http://www.gremlins.com/phillip_besio/mottled_icon.gif alt=\"Green Beholder - 6th one produced\" align=middle></a>\r\n<HR>More info write:<A HREF=mailto:trekist@hotmail.com>trekist@hotmail.com</a><BR>pics are being updated'),(2922,5119,'2002-09-24 05:55:30',5445,6489,'cw',0,'Budd Root\'s Cavewoman.  More detailed shot can be seen at http://www.libertymeadows.com/cwmodel.htm.  The original art is at http://www.basementcomics.com/gallery/cho/cho35.jpg'),(3037,6504,'2004-01-25 11:35:19',3461,6504,'gortpredator2',0,'Very good detail and likeness of the movie creature.  This kit was purchased as is from a professional modeler.'),(2924,6361,'2002-10-10 12:45:55',5446,6571,'cyclops',0,'For more information visit our website: http://www.wendygital.com/ohmygod'),(2925,5119,'2002-10-16 09:15:17',5447,5118,'ainoko',0,''),(2926,5119,'2002-10-16 09:15:52',5447,5118,'ainoko',0,''),(3039,6817,'2004-01-30 17:30:56',5562,6817,'Damselindistress1',0,'scratch built. This is my first sculpture. I just started in this hobby. Hope you like it. I may try to make a kit of it.'),(2928,6583,'2004-01-20 14:17:56',5556,6583,'T2',0,'I like how did this kit. this is one my favorties that i have done. i went for a very gory effect. most of it was done by airbrush and some parts i drybrushed by hand i also used the wash technique in many areas. email me and tell me what you think.'),(2931,6604,'2003-01-12 09:12:30',4520,54,'cyclops jpg',0,'the kit is vinyl,not resin..painted with a mixture or acrylics and oils..'),(2932,6604,'2002-11-16 12:16:58',4520,6604,'cyclops jpg',0,''),(2933,6604,'2002-11-16 12:55:13',4520,6604,'cyclops',0,''),(2934,5237,'2002-11-18 13:43:16',5455,5237,'WNGDREAP',0,'Another old Arfix kit conversion'),(2935,5237,'2002-11-18 13:42:37',5454,5237,'Mora',0,'Sol resin'),(2936,5237,'2002-11-18 13:42:00',5453,5237,'matrix',0,'Andrea 54mm white metal kit with a stupid name (not Matrix) so they can avoid copyright, but it\'s obvious who it is!'),(2937,5237,'2002-11-18 13:41:15',5452,5237,'ripley2',0,'Andrea 54mm white metal and resin kit with a stupid name so they can avoid copyright. Also it\'s a mix of films 1 and 2 ie base from one - tooled up Ripley from two'),(2938,5237,'2002-11-18 13:40:31',5451,5237,'holybell',0,'Sol resin'),(2939,5237,'2002-11-18 13:38:21',5450,5237,'HDDISKa',0,'I\'ve seen this on Gremlins done with fibre optic wire thingies but can I find it to add this version to it.....no'),(2941,5237,'2002-11-18 13:36:15',5456,5237,'vampirella',0,'Famous kit done a different way'),(2943,5363,'2002-11-25 23:21:57',5364,5367,'apc',0,'Well, John Pilkington gets 2 mentions here:\r\n1: Thanks for helping me get some pictures uploaded and\r\n2: After seeing John\'s kit I had to have a go. I went for a desert camo look. The picture has\'nt come out great but I\'m quite pleased although it\'s not as good as John\'s.'),(2944,5363,'2002-11-26 02:24:47',5459,5367,'anderson',0,'I added this kit after a long time since makeing it, mainly because it stands in the shadow of Michael Metric\'s version.'),(2945,5363,'2002-11-26 02:26:53',5462,5367,'cthulhu',0,'This was my first test with SuperSculpey. It takes a bit of getting used to so I did some little monsters based on the Cthulhu mythos.'),(2946,5363,'2002-11-26 03:14:56',5477,5367,'Stuart',0,'This was a tiny kit I found in a cheap toy shop. I added the keys to the pic so you can see how small it really is.\r\nThe kit came with about 50 little soldiers, which I think were added later and not part of the main tank sprues.'),(2947,5363,'2002-11-26 03:19:57',5481,5367,'X',0,'The biggest difficulty with this kit was the decals. They just kept comeing off! Not eased by my move from Basildon to Merthyr Tydfil 2 years ago either when I had to glue all the guns back on (doh).'),(2948,5363,'2002-11-26 03:23:25',5464,5367,'delorean',0,'I do not like cars!\r\nI learned a big lesson with this kit-DO NOT USE SUPER GLUE ON WINDOWS- I left it as it was, with the windows misted up. Make of that what you will :)'),(2949,5363,'2002-11-26 06:48:20',5465,5367,'Dredd',0,'This is the first in the \"Judge\" series, the others being Anderson and Death.\r\nIt\'s quite an old kit of mine, and that\'s my excuse for the paint job. This is a floppy leg kit, which means if you dont reinforce the legs (like I did\'nt) the sun will make it fall forward. So I have it placed high up...I should fix it but never seem to get round to it.'),(2950,5363,'2002-11-26 23:36:13',5480,5367,'Urd',0,'A nice little kit.'),(2951,5363,'2002-11-26 23:38:28',5467,5367,'Grey',0,'This kit came out just after the start of the X-Files. It\'s such a simple kit with quite a bit of character. The base came with it.\r\nI painted it mostly with a toothbrush!'),(2952,5363,'2002-11-26 23:42:55',5472,5367,'Raptor',0,'Guess which film this model cashed in on?\r\nI did have the T-Rex as well but gave it away.\r\nMy dinosaur obsessed son would dearly like to get his hands on this kit but so far I\'ve fought him off (he\'s only 2)'),(2953,5363,'2002-11-27 01:35:25',5479,5367,'Term',0,'I hacked this kits arm off and stuck some pen bits and wire up there. To explain just how much research I did on this kit , it was\'nt until after I had cut the arm off that I checked to see it was the correct one! (it was)'),(2954,5363,'2002-11-27 08:07:30',5463,5367,'Dalek',0,'Exterminate!!! This kit was a pig to do, mainly because of the different plastics involved. Trying to get them to stick together, even with super glue was an ordeal. There were 2 versions you could make though, I went for the sink plunger model.'),(2955,5363,'2002-11-28 06:59:25',5460,5367,'Blazer',0,'I bought this kit as it was \"something different\". As usual with these foreign kits all the instructions are in Japanese which gives you a little extra challenge.\r\nI thought I\'d let you know my website now has all of my kits on display: \r\nhttp://freespace.virgin.net/chris.morse/index.html \r\nPlease pay a visit'),(2956,5363,'2002-11-28 07:02:33',5461,5367,'cerebus',0,'This is my first attempt at moddeling an actual character in SuperSculpey. It\'s cerebus from the Dave Sim comic. I used metal foil and nails for the inner skeleton. It\'s rough but bears the likeness OK.'),(2957,5363,'2002-11-28 23:25:12',5466,5367,'Drop',0,'A superb model, with at least 3 variations on weapon arrays. Let down only by the decals which when applied spoiled the whole thing. So I peeled them all off leaving some bits on which I could\'nt get off. Although this seemed to give it a more weathered look.'),(2958,5363,'2002-11-28 23:27:34',5468,5367,'Labor',0,'This is from the superb films Patlabor 1 & 2. If you\'ve never seen them and like anime watch them. They easily rival the great Akira! The little lady figure is metal.'),(2959,5363,'2002-11-28 23:31:44',5469,5367,'Lupin',0,'This kit was a present from my good friend Richard in Basildon. The second car kit I\'ve made I did\'nt make the same mistake I did on the Delorean! It comes from the Hayao Miyazaki film from Studio Ghibli. If these names mean nothing to you you are DEFINATLEY missing out!!! Look the name up on Ebay and but the 12 film boxset.'),(2960,5363,'2002-11-28 23:35:03',5470,5367,'Nellie',0,'This was a gift from a friend of my fathers who was going into a nursing home and could no longer make kits :(\r\n I gave him the original photo, so I hope you liked it Peter. The actual kit can be made into the RAF version or the Bond version. Again (is it me?) the only trouble was the decals....I ended up painting most of them on!'),(2961,5363,'2002-11-28 23:38:02',5471,5367,'Pod',0,'What a pig of a model!  I did not think much of this fiddly peice of rubbish. By the end I had given up on the paint scheme and used the \"chaos\" logo on it instead.'),(2962,5363,'2002-11-28 23:40:37',3514,5367,'Robo',0,'The best kit from the worst film. The backpack really makes this kit. His helmet comes off to reveal Peter Wellers face (not the other guy). And because it\'s vinyl you can shape the backpack perfectly with the hairdryer.'),(2963,5363,'2002-11-28 23:47:04',5474,5367,'scene',0,'This was a year in the makeing (mostly because I have to work round the kids now!) It\'s no \"Francois Verlinden\" (and if you dont recognise that name then shame on you) but I\'m quite pleased. it\'s the model that got me hooked on Tamiya 1/35 scale military kits. And compared to what I usually do they are quite cheap: The Dragon Wagon which is the US 40 tonne tank transporter I got for £80 which is one of the most expensive kits they make, then the Sherman was £18 and the little Howitzer was £14. The rocks I got from a pile at work and the moss form the local park. This was the first kit I used my airbrush on too. I bought a new one on Ebay for £7!!! And I got the compressor from D9 models in Newport for £100.'),(2964,5363,'2002-11-28 23:50:39',5475,5367,'Scorp',0,'This was a bit of fun, the kit comes with about 50 people but they are so small there was no way I was gonna paint that lot! One of the buildings is called \"Communications in Print\" which is where I was working at the time, back in 96\''),(2965,5363,'2002-11-28 23:53:15',5476,5367,'spider',0,'Quite a good kit but a lousy photo. I got this at Comet Miniatures for £10 a few years ago...I bet their a bit more expensive now! This kit sits nicely on top of my TV at home and gets a lot of comment...especially recently now the film is out.'),(2966,5363,'2002-11-28 23:56:54',5478,5367,'swamp',0,'My second attempt at sculpting a character in SuperSculpey. It\'s Swamp Thing from the comic of the same name, and I\'ve added some mushrooms on him and even a few beetles etc. It was quite fun to do. I thought I\'d mention this for anybody like me who was haveing trouble uploading pictures, John Pilkington figured out it\'s the browser! You can\'t do it with Internet explorer, but you can with Netscape!'),(2967,5237,'2002-11-30 17:04:47',5485,5237,'Nadia',0,'Sol kit with added wings'),(2968,5237,'2002-11-30 17:07:44',5484,5237,'Silentmobius',0,'one piece resin wall plaque I got on e-bay. Had more holes in it than  politicians promises, but with milliput thinned and painted on to it, it came out alright'),(2969,5237,'2002-11-30 17:17:23',5483,5237,'Yuna1',0,'Sol vinyl kit. Changed the colour scheme though.'),(2970,5237,'2002-11-30 17:16:47',5482,5237,'Kali1',0,'Not the monsters in motion version. this one was much cruder and older I suspect. The sword blades are an AOL cd cut to shape. Well they keep coming through the door and I finally found a use for one.'),(2971,5237,'2002-11-30 17:12:50',3518,5237,'Terminatora',0,'Thought I would have a go at this one as it\'s so popular.'),(2973,6637,'2003-01-06 01:34:45',5487,6637,'FlyingDutchman1',0,'Made from modified Revell Ghost Ship, rotten wood (with live wood-worms), spider webs, and lots and lots of dust.\r\nAnd, of course, it GLOWS IN THE DARK :).'),(2974,6637,'2003-01-03 03:37:15',5487,6637,'FlyingDutchman2',0,'Made from modified Revell Ghost Ship, rotten wood (with live wood-worms), spider webs, and lots and lots of dust.\r\nAnd, of course, it GLOWS IN THE DARK :).'),(2975,6637,'2003-01-03 03:36:56',5487,6637,'FlyingDutchman3',0,'Made from modified Revell Ghost Ship, rotten wood (with live wood-worms), spider webs, and lots and lots of dust.\r\nAnd, of course, it GLOWS IN THE DARK :).'),(2976,6361,'2003-01-13 09:19:33',5488,6571,'sup11',0,'visit our website www.wendygital.com/ohmygod'),(2977,6361,'2003-01-13 09:26:08',5489,6571,'jango',0,''),(2978,4864,'2003-01-30 08:17:53',5490,4864,'GodziMegaguirus',0,'Super resin kit from Japan. Visit my monster gallery www.monsterjones.com for more Godzilla models.'),(2979,4864,'2003-01-30 08:48:18',5492,4864,'KongLogroll',0,'Extrented base with spider pit, added ground cover. See my website www.monsterjones.com for more Kong models.'),(2980,4864,'2003-01-30 09:06:08',5493,4864,'Tobanga',0,'Reposed figure, added girl victim, and added more bark to its bite using Celluclay. Brushed glue and sprinkled sand to quicksand base. See my website www.monsterjones.com for more classic B-mvie monsters!'),(2981,4864,'2003-01-30 09:27:50',5494,4864,'CreatureAuroraRH',0,'Resin replacement head from Posthumous Productions on the classic Creature kit!\r\nVisit www.monsterjones.com for more Creature kits!'),(2982,4864,'2003-01-30 09:41:46',5495,4864,'OzWitch',0,'Produced in the U.K., I am not sure who sculped it...but a SUPER likeness!!\r\nAnyone gotta bucket of water for this Dame of Darkness? Check out my website www.monsterjones.com for more monster models.'),(2983,5237,'2003-01-31 14:59:21',5499,5237,'Spart',0,'Part Andrea part Pegaso 54mm white metal'),(2984,5237,'2003-01-31 15:00:23',5480,5237,'URD',0,'Original Volks resin kit with added wings '),(2985,5237,'2003-01-31 15:00:54',5497,5237,'eva',0,' '),(2986,5237,'2003-01-31 15:02:30',5496,5237,'Wmt',0,'Japanese (I think) garage kit with white metal arms. I redid the face. makes it more disturbing.'),(2987,5237,'2003-01-31 15:05:12',5500,5237,'Balrog',0,'Games Workshop kit with a few added extras'),(2988,5237,'2003-01-31 15:07:40',5501,5237,'Ciberwinger',0,'I removed the warped base and put the numerous bits onto a piece of slate'),(2989,5435,'2003-02-07 14:10:44',5503,5438,'gremconda',0,'Another MUST have for the Creech lover in YOU!\r\nSee more at my web site at:\r\nwww.parlorcity.com/dscreations/'),(2990,5435,'2003-02-07 14:37:35',5504,5438,'gremate',0,'WonderFest 2002 award winner!'),(2991,5435,'2003-02-08 13:25:54',5505,5438,'grembust',0,'Need I say more!  This bust build/paint-up is featured in Model Maniacs Magazine Issue #5.  Grab a copy and check out how I did the paint work on this AWESOME piece!\r\nThis is a WonderFest Award winner!  The \"Dane\" strikes again!'),(2992,5435,'2003-02-07 14:52:27',5506,5438,'gremfinshd',0,'I replaced the OEM head (YUK!), with a Posthumous replacement head (YUM!)\r\nThe snake was out to lunch. ;)'),(2993,5435,'2003-02-10 01:49:34',4592,5438,'gremshot',0,'WOW!  This Creech realy came out nice!\r\nAll drybrushed with acrylics.  This was a commissioned build-up.\r\nI can do one of these for you too!\r\nwww.parlorcity.com/dscreations?'),(2994,5435,'2003-02-10 02:04:34',4592,5438,'gremhorz',0,'Here is a better single image of the Horizon Gillman.'),(2995,5435,'2003-02-10 02:15:24',4592,5438,'gremhorzbk',0,'...and here\'s a back view of the Horizon Gillman.'),(2996,6660,'2003-02-12 02:50:27',3240,6660,'creat',0,'This is the Monogram reissue of the Aurora original.'),(2997,6660,'2003-02-14 05:06:43',5173,6660,'wolf',0,'I was a little disappointed by the skull. There\'s very little detail in the sculpt. Some cunning paintwork overcomes this, though.'),(2998,6660,'2003-02-15 02:18:34',4634,6660,'frank',0,'This is the luminators reissue of the Aurora kit. I bought the Aurora glow in the dark kit as a kid. It was my first figure kit and I don\'t know when it, and the rest of my childhood kits, got thrown out. I was really pleased to find the monogram reissue. I chose to paint him that lovely greeny/brown colour that apples go when they rot rather than the green I painted him when I was a kid.'),(2999,5435,'2003-02-16 16:49:18',5511,5438,'gremsprman',0,'This bust was released in October at the Chiller Theater Show.  Bust shown here is actual paint-up by Daniel Tarr and was incorporated with graphics into this preliminary box-art sample.  An AWESOME addition to any Superman collection!  Please e-mail with any inquiries.\r\nAlso, visit my web site at:\r\nwww.parlorcity.com/dscreations/'),(3000,5363,'2003-02-17 05:58:31',5512,5367,'ambush',0,'I called this \"The ambush\" and basically it involves a Pershing medium tank and an M8 Greyhound armoured car (both made by Tamiya) lying in wait in a ruined cottage (made by Great North Roads). There are a few soldiers sneaking around too.'),(3001,5363,'2003-02-17 05:58:02',5513,5367,'convoy',0,'These are all kits from the Games Workshop Warhammer 40K range. They are made in plastic and metal.\r\nThe metal is poor quality and the plastic high quality. One of the kits had a barrel missing but Games Workshop replaced it with a hole sprue of extras at no cost!\r\nThere were going to be 2 other kits in this scene, but it was way too cramped. (one of the kits left out is pictured inset)'),(3002,5363,'2003-02-17 06:01:05',5514,5367,'marines',0,'This is 2 figures from a box of about 8. I placed these 2 on a lid filled with some clay.'),(3003,4863,'2003-03-04 05:36:52',5516,5431,'stefania',0,'www.jjmodels.com'),(3004,4863,'2003-03-04 08:32:10',5517,5431,'claudia',0,'www.jjmodels.com Exclusive distributor for USA www.anotherworlddesigns.com '),(3005,4863,'2003-03-05 05:06:06',5518,5431,'sarahgothic',0,'www.jjmodels.com\r\nExclusive distributor for US \r\nwww.anotherworlddesigns.com'),(3006,4863,'2003-03-06 00:54:50',5519,5431,'deborahgold',0,'www.jjmodels.com'),(3007,4863,'2003-03-07 01:50:00',5520,5431,'ysiil',0,'www.jjmodels.com exlusive distributor for USA anotherworlddesigns.com'),(3008,4863,'2003-03-10 03:56:28',5521,5431,'asha',0,'www.jjmodels.com - exclusive distributor for USA www.anotherworlddesigns.com'),(3009,5633,'2003-03-14 19:40:28',5522,5633,'daredevil',0,''),(3010,5363,'2003-03-19 00:42:20',5523,5367,'Lancaster',0,'Where to start with this kit? It\'s by Airfix and was very dissapointing quality wise. Once I started work on it though my interest rose. It\'s a 1:72 scale model and was going well until a box fell on it and broke the wheels off. So I damaged the wing area with a burned out propeller and shot up wing as disguise. Bullet holes and warped propeller supplied by a candle and a compass.\r\nThe painting instructions were from the 70\'s and only listed humbrol numbers which was\'nt much help so you need a color reference.\r\nJust to say to all the modellers interested in Historical or Military kits you should have a browse over at the www.totalmodel.com community.'),(3011,4864,'2003-03-20 07:50:18',5524,4864,'BigWrap',0,'Huge resin kit from Yuji Sakai, master sculptor. Added custom base with destroyed Japanese castle. For more Godzilla model visit my website at www.monsterjones.com'),(3012,4864,'2003-03-20 08:18:12',5526,4864,'GodziPL',0,'Polar Light\'s HUGE styrene Godzilla...very cool kit, best bang for your model buck! Customized base, reposed head, hands, new toothpick fangs...this buildup won first place in the Polar Lights Godzilla model contest of 2002. Visit my website at www.monsterjones.com for more Godzilla!'),(3013,4864,'2003-03-20 09:14:57',5525,4864,'Godzilla89',0,'Big vinyl kit 50cm tall with added glass eyes. Visit my website at www.monsterjones.com for more Godzilla'),(3014,4864,'2003-03-21 06:12:28',5526,4864,'GodziPL2',0,'Huge kit, custom base, reposed head and hands. visit my website at www.monsterjones.com for more Godzilla!'),(3015,6401,'2003-03-24 10:52:28',5528,6401,'miho1',0,'Super Deformed Mihoshi is from the Tenchi Muyo series.  Mine\'s a scratchbuilt, but there is also a resin kit based on the drawing. See other stuff at my website, http://web.utk.edu/~north'),(3016,4864,'2003-03-26 13:02:25',3240,4864,'CreaturePL2',0,'Polar Light reissue of the Aurora classic! Visit my website at www.monsterjones.com for more Creature kits.'),(3017,5207,'2003-04-11 09:59:28',5530,5207,'rans',0,'This is a display I made from two different kits and many made from scratch parts  I completed it in Summer of 2003'),(3018,5363,'2003-04-13 23:36:17',5531,5367,'huey',0,'The Huey helicopter was from Panda.\r\nThe M113 was from Italeri.\r\nThe troops were from verlinden.\r\nThe base is concrete with lots of sawdust on.\r\nThe scale is 1/35 and depicts a scene from Vietnam.'),(3019,5363,'2003-04-21 23:48:02',5532,5367,'barbarella',0,'This was a very well made kit. I was\'nt sure what I was going to get as it was from Bangkok and I\'ve heard varying things about them. In the end I got this from www.modelfactoryplus.com and it was excellent quality. It also came recorded delivery.\r\nUnbelievably I did this kit in a week! i was very fortunate with the skin, I first tried airbrushing it, then quickly realised I did\'nt have the skill for that. So I went for my usual method of mixing the paint on the model, and it came out OK.'),(3020,4864,'2003-04-23 12:09:06',5533,4864,'ItTerror',0,'Super resin kit from Action Hobbies! Visit my model gallery at www.monsterjones.com for more cool 50\'s Sci-Fi!'),(3021,4864,'2003-04-29 11:33:00',5535,4864,'KongElas',0,'Rare resin garage kit from Cananda, added new teeth to both figures. For more King Kong kits check out my website at www.monsterjones.com'),(3022,4864,'2003-04-29 11:38:22',5536,4864,'KongNY',0,'Great wall hanging kit!! For more Kong models check out my website at www.monsterjones.com'),(3023,4864,'2003-04-29 11:46:22',5537,4864,'KongTrex',0,'Mighty BIG resin kit!For more King Kong models check out my website at www.monsterjones.com.'),(3024,4864,'2003-04-30 12:05:06',5538,4864,'CreaDH2',0,'Another great Dark Horse Creature...still one of the BEST swimming Creature models around! See my website for more Creature models at www.monsterjones.com.'),(3025,4864,'2003-04-30 12:45:19',5539,4864,'GodziGhidrah',0,'1/350 resin kit, added electrical wire for anti-gravity energy bolts on custom base. Visit ww.monsterjones.com for more Godzilla models.'),(3026,6718,'2003-05-12 00:55:49',5540,6718,'womanoidweapon',0,'Sentient plant-creature with humanoid appearance. Internal morphology is biomechanical.This entity is a weapon with camouflage capabilities.Extreme caution.'),(3027,4863,'2003-05-20 00:38:25',5541,5431,'freedom',0,'www.jjmodels.com - For USA www.anotherworlddesigns.com'),(3028,4863,'2003-05-20 00:51:27',5541,4863,'freedom',0,'www.jjmodels.com - For USA www.anotherworlddesigns.com'),(3029,4863,'2003-05-20 04:59:15',5543,5431,'angelica',0,'www.jjmodels.com - For USA anotherworlddesigns.com'),(3030,5363,'2003-05-21 23:16:30',5544,5367,'miss',0,'This is the 1:350 scale ship from Tamiya, costing about £60.\r\nThe ship is huge, just under a meter long and has so many tiny guns to stick on it\'s enough to make a grown man weep!\r\nIt does look impressive when finished though, so if you want to persevere the effort will be worth it.\r\nThe ship is famous on 2 counts:\r\n1: The Japanese surrendered on her at the end of the War, and\r\n2: The film Under Seige of course!!!'),(3031,6702,'2003-05-31 09:24:18',3476,6702,'alien3',0,'first try!!'),(3032,5633,'2003-06-07 12:14:52',5545,5633,'george',0,''),(3033,5363,'2004-06-08 05:58:18',5546,5367,'barb',0,'The quality is excellent, all I had to do was drill the heel to fix her to the base, plus a bit of sanding on the legs.\r\nI painted her mostly with my new Iwata Eclipse airbrush, the best one I ever bought.\r\nThe model is very impressive and the photo dpoesnt really do it justice.'),(3066,5119,'2004-06-23 06:18:15',5577,6871,'gsa',0,''),(3067,6294,'2005-08-25 04:02:34',5578,6294,'Logan',0,''),(3034,6401,'2003-06-23 15:20:42',5548,6401,'neko',0,'Sometimes you see a kit and you know immediately that you have to build it. Such was the case with the Neko Rei kit, which represents my favorite scene in Neon Genesis Evangelion. You know, the one where Rei says \"Gawd, I feel sexy!\", climbs down out of her Eva, puts on a cat costume, and spends the next three hours giving Shinji a tongue bath...\r\n\r\nMore pics at http://web.utk.edu/~north'),(3036,4863,'2003-12-03 06:17:41',5555,149,'ladyalex',0,'Dark Ladies Collection on www.jjmodels.com'),(3043,6803,'2004-03-21 16:37:45',4059,6803,'BG7',0,''),(3044,6803,'2004-03-21 16:23:38',3498,6803,'michellecat',0,''),(3045,6803,'2004-03-21 16:24:58',3498,6803,'catwoman33',0,''),(3046,6803,'2004-03-21 16:39:27',3476,6803,'',0,''),(3047,6803,'2004-03-21 16:27:03',4059,6803,'modelbat',0,''),(3048,6803,'2004-03-21 16:29:19',3494,6803,'batmanmodel',0,''),(3049,6803,'2004-03-21 16:31:16',3252,6803,'babe',0,''),(3050,6803,'2004-03-21 16:33:40',3919,6803,'battlevamp',0,''),(3051,5329,'2004-03-27 19:52:09',5567,5771,'chaostree2',0,'Created for Warhammer, about 10\" tall. Back side.'),(3052,5329,'2004-03-26 20:19:40',5567,5771,'chaostree',0,'Created for Warhammer, about 10\" tall'),(3053,5237,'2004-03-30 16:11:03',5568,5237,'bigfire',0,'Pegaso Models Fire Elemental/Demon. Very nice limited edition kit from Italy'),(3054,5237,'2004-03-30 16:43:56',5569,149,'',0,''),(3055,5237,'2004-03-30 16:23:38',5569,5237,'Venus',0,'1/6 resin via e-bay'),(3056,5237,'2004-03-30 16:25:28',5571,5237,'vam',0,''),(3057,5237,'2004-03-30 16:41:00',5574,5237,'jane',0,'Old Phoenix kit in white metal 80mm I think'),(3058,5237,'2004-03-30 16:41:26',4031,5237,'Misato',0,'1/6 resin'),(3059,5237,'2004-03-30 16:42:08',5572,5237,'bettypages',0,''),(3060,5547,'2004-04-11 09:45:32',5575,5547,'CreatureWalksAmongUsBust2.jpg',0,''),(3061,5547,'2004-04-11 09:46:16',5575,5547,'CreatureWalksAmongUsBust2.jpg',0,''),(3062,5633,'2004-05-13 16:05:30',5576,6737,'darthmaul',0,'\"The Disciple\" is produced by Fito\'s Model Kits!\r\nThis is a 1/6 scale figure made in 8 parts of poliurethane resin'),(3063,5633,'2004-05-13 16:06:42',5576,6737,'darthmaul1',0,''),(3064,5633,'2004-05-13 16:06:52',5576,6737,'darthmaul2',0,''),(3065,5633,'2004-05-13 16:07:01',5576,6737,'darthmaul3',0,''),(3068,5575,'2006-01-24 04:32:16',3965,5575,'dark',0,''),(3069,5575,'2006-01-24 04:27:43',3965,5575,'dark1',0,''),(3070,307,'2007-07-08 15:44:34',5580,7106,'',0,'Pretty on a Pillow is the newest kit offered by Fogger Studios.  Shipping is free if you live in the continental United States.  Just go to www.foggerstudios.com and purchase via PayPal.  Just one other note - I\'m not the painter!  Rick Cantu is the talented guy who painted this version of Pretty, but I can\'t seem to get his name to show up in the painter section above!');
